E["item:a-clue-to-sanders-treasure"] = {t="item",n="A Clue to Sanders' Treasure",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, A Clue to Sanders' Treasure leads seekers farther along Captain Sanders' trail. It marks the second step in a hunt across the bluffs and coastlines.",h="In Westfall, A Clue to Sanders' Treasure leads seekers farther along Captain Sanders' trail.",sec={{t="A Pirate's Riddle",b="After following Captain Sanders' first treasure map, you find a parchment pointing farther inland into Westfall. Its scrawled note sends you east from the coast and up the bluffs toward the main road.\n\nNear crumbling stone ruins and an abandoned chimney, an old barrel marks where Sanders hid the next clue. The trail leads deeper into the troubled farmlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this clue?",a="Captain Sanders left a handwritten note to guide anyone clever enough to follow his trail to another hidden container in Westfall.",al={"sanders clue","clue to sanders treasure","what is a clue to sanders treasure"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this clue lead?",a="The clue sends you east from the coast and up the bluffs toward the Westfall road. An old barrel lies near a ruined chimney.",al={"where do i go","clue destination","chimney location"},it="next_step"},{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was a pirate. His legacy lives on in the treasure caches and riddles he hid across Westfall's shores and countryside.",al={"who is captain sanders","sanders lore","captain sanders"},it="people"},{q="Where does this clue come from, and who made it?",a="This written note was left behind by Captain Sanders, an infamous swashbuckler who buried his illicit plunder throughout Westfall. Rather than leaving a direct map to his booty, the crafty sea captain penned a chain of riddles and directions, hiding each message in landmarks across the coast to test anyone bold or clever enough to track his legacy.",al={"who made sanders clue","where did clue come from","origin of clue"},it="origin",add="e66b6229"},{q="Why is this clue valuable to treasure hunters?",a="On its own, the parchment is just a cryptic rhyme, but to an aspiring fortune seeker, it is a vital step toward uncovering Captain Sanders' fabled hidden stash. Following its directions is the only way to locate the next breadcrumb in his elaborate scavenger hunt and ultimately claim whatever riches the pirate captain stowed away.",al={"why want sanders clue","why is clue important","what good is sanders clue"},it="why_wanted",add="4dc920ed"}},kw={"barrel","chimney","clue","pirate","sanders","treasure","westfall"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},src={"A Clue to Sanders' Treasure","Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 2)"}}
E["item:a-mysterious-message"] = {t="item",n="A Mysterious Message",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, a courier's intercepted message gives the People's Militia proof of who directs the Defias Brotherhood.",h="In Westfall, a courier's intercepted message gives the People's Militia proof of who directs the Defias...",sec={{t="Whispers of Blacknails",b="The dispatch names VanCleef as the brotherhood's authority and mentions an associate called Blacknails. Its wider network remains hidden. By decoding the document, the People's Militia gains leverage over captured cutpurses and a way to find the brotherhood's true stronghold.",sp=1},{t="Intercepted Orders",b="A Defias Messenger carries the message between Defias operations at Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Jangolode Mine. Its interception marks a break in Gryan Stoutmantle's investigation. For weeks, the People's Militia suspected someone directed the bandit uprising, but had no sure proof.\n\nThe missive confirms Edwin VanCleef commands the brotherhood's efforts across Westfall. He does so through coded ranks and intermediaries.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="What does this message reveal to the People's Militia?",a="The message gives Gryan Stoutmantle proof that Edwin VanCleef directs the Defias Brotherhood's operations across Westfall. It confirms the militia's suspicions about who commands the outlaws.",al={"what does the note say","mysterious message lore","what is in the message"},sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Who is Blacknails?",a="Blacknails is named in the intercepted text as an associate or agent. Little else is known of their identity or whereabouts, leaving them among the shadowy figures operating deep within the Defias network.",al={"who is blacknails","blacknails lore","defias blacknails"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries this message?",a="A Defias Messenger carries the message along Westfall's roads between Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Jangolode Mine to coordinate bandit operations.",al={"who has the message","who drops mysterious message","defias courier"}},{q="What happens after Gryan Stoutmantle reads it?",a="With VanCleef's role confirmed, the militia turns to finding the Defias headquarters. A captured thief agrees to lead scouts to the secret hideout in exchange for his life.",al={"what comes next","stoutmantle reaction","after mysterious message"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is A Mysterious Message?",a="It is a sealed letter carried by a Defias Messenger across Westfall. Addressed to an operative named Blacknails, it contains crucial correspondence among the conspirators operating within the region.",al={"mysterious message","what is this message","defias note"},it="identity",add="9bec86bb"},{q="Where does A Mysterious Message come from, and who made it?",a="The message originates within the upper ranks of the Defias Brotherhood, penned as instructions to their operative Blacknails and transported along the courier route connecting Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Jangolode Mine.",al={"who wrote the mysterious message","who sent mysterious message","mysterious message origin"},it="origin",add="ea5b5889"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want A Mysterious Message?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia are desperate to pinpoint the Defias Brotherhood's secret hideout and understand their command structure. Intercepting this missive provides them with concrete written evidence that Edwin VanCleef directly orchestrates the Brotherhood's rebellion.",al={"why want mysterious message","stoutmantle message why","why get mysterious message"},it="why_wanted",add="f3ab4b79"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions helping in Westfall, the intercepted document proves the unrest in the kingdom's farmlands is a calculated insurgency led by Edwin VanCleef, not random banditry.",["class:Rogue"]="The intercepted dispatch gives rogues a glimpse of the operational security, courier paths, and coded communications used by the Defias underworld."},kw={"blacknails","defias messenger","edwin vancleef","gryan stoutmantle","moonbrook","mysterious message","westfall"},rel={"quest:65","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:jangolode-mine","subzone:gold-coast-quarry","subzone:defias-hideout"},src={"A Mysterious Message","The Defias Brotherhood (5)"}}
E["item:another-clue-to-sanders-treasure"] = {t="item",n="Another Clue to Sanders' Treasure",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, a scrap of Captain Sanders' parchment points toward his next hidden marker.",h="In Westfall, a scrap of Captain Sanders' parchment points toward his next hidden marker.",sec={{t="A Trail on the Coastal Bluffs",b="Captain Sanders hid his stolen riches across Westfall, leaving riddles and buried markers instead of one map that could be seized. This scrap carries the trail onward from the previous hiding place. It says to turn north and seek a discarded jug beside a lonely windmill above the sea cliffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written on this clue?",a="The parchment says to face north from the hidden barrel and walk straight to an empty jug beside a lone windmill on the sea bluffs.",al={"what does the clue say","sanders clue text","directions on clue"},it="item"},{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was a pirate who left caches of stolen goods along Westfall's shores and bluffs. He hid markers across the region instead of leaving an intact map.",al={"who is sanders","captain sanders background","sanders westfall pirate"},it="people"},{q="Where does this clue lead next?",a="The clue points north along Westfall's coastal cliffs to a lone windmill on the bluffs, where an empty jug marks the next step in Sanders' trail.",al={"where to go next","sanders windmill clue","where is the jug"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Another Clue to Sanders' Treasure?",a="It is a handwritten scrap of parchment discovered tucked away in an old barrel along the Westfall coast. The paper carries another set of nautical directions penned by Captain Sanders, guiding anyone bold enough to follow his trail toward the next hidden piece of his trail.",al={"what is another clue to sanders treasure","sanders clue parchment","what is this clue parchment"},it="identity",add="b0e51eff"},{q="Where does this clue come from, and who made it?",a="The clue was written and hidden by Captain Sanders, an old seafarer who left a trail of clues scattered across the coast and countryside of Westfall. You recover this specific scrap of parchment from an abandoned barrel where he stashed it long ago.",al={"who wrote another clue to sanders treasure","who made sanders clue","where did this clue come from"},it="origin",add="37a7a825"},{q="Why does anyone want Another Clue to Sanders' Treasure?",a="Following Sanders' trail is the only way to uncover his buried chest. Each clue builds directly upon the last, offering the exact landmarks needed to trace the captain's steps across Westfall to whatever fortune he stashed away.",al={"why find sanders clue","why do i want sanders treasure clue","what is the point of sanders clue"},it="why_wanted",add="632540c2"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how to read cryptic directions and search forgotten seaside caches for hidden plunder."},kw={"bluffs","captain sanders","clue","parchment","sanders treasure","westfall","windmill"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},src={"Another Clue to Sanders' Treasure","Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 3)"}}
E["item:final-clue-to-sanders-treasure"] = {t="item",n="Final Clue to Sanders' Treasure",z="westfall",s="Along Westfall’s coast, Captain Sanders’ final directions send scavengers out to sea. A note in an old jug points west toward his buried treasure.",h="Along Westfall’s coast, Captain Sanders’ final directions send scavengers out to sea.",sec={{t="A Sailor's Parting Words",b="Captain Sanders left his final directions in an old whiskey jug on the Westfall coast. The pirate had scattered cryptic notes along the shoreline, and this one completes the trail. From the jug, the directions point due west into the ocean. Follow them through the surf to a lonely offshore rock, where his ironbound sea chest lies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the final clue say?",a="The note points west from the whiskey jug and out into the sea. A small offshore island holds the treasure chest.",al={"clue text","what is written on clue","sanders directions"}},{q="Where was this clue found?",a="The clue was inside an old whiskey jug on the Westfall coast. It was the third step in Captain Sanders’ trail of hints.",al={"where do i find final clue","old jug location","clue location"},it="place"},{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was a pirate whose belongings and treasure maps washed up along Westfall’s coast. Before his death, he left hidden notes and markers across the countryside that lead to his hoard.",al={"who is captain sanders","sanders pirate lore","who hid the treasure"},it="people"},{q="Where does this clue ultimately lead?",a="The note leads west from Westfall’s coast to a solitary island. Captain Sanders’ sea chest rests there.",al={"where is the chest","sanders island","island location"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Final Clue to Sanders' Treasure?",a="It is a weathered slip of paper pulled from Captain Sanders' old whiskey jug along the Westfall coastline. Smelling faintly of spirits with ink run from moisture, this note marks the culmination of a scavenger hunt laid down by the late pirate captain, offering the last directions needed to uncover his buried hoard.",al={"what is final clue to sanders treasure","final clue identity","what is this clue"},it="identity",add="ed69490f"},{q="Where does the Final Clue to Sanders' Treasure come from, and who made it?",a="The clue was penned by Captain Sanders himself and sealed inside an old jug beside the lone windmill on the sea bluffs of Westfall. The pirate captain hid it as the last step in an elaborate trail across the coast, ensuring that only someone determined enough to follow his scattered trail markers would ever reach his hidden booty.",al={"who made final clue","where did the final clue come from","origin of final clue"},it="origin",add="0f7c35ef"},{q="Why does anyone want the Final Clue to Sanders' Treasure?",a="Anyone following Captain Sanders' trail seeks his long-lost pirate booty. While previous hints led from one shoreline landmark to another, this final note explicitly directs the finder beyond the Westfall beaches and out into the open sea, straight toward the solitary island where the captain's chest sits waiting.",al={"why want final clue","why find final clue","purpose of final clue"},it="why_wanted",add="9095866c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can follow Captain Sanders’ directions out to sea and search Westfall’s shores for treasure beyond Defias pockets."},kw={"captain sanders","chest","clue","pirate","treasure","westfall","whiskey jug"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},src={"Final Clue to Sanders' Treasure","Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 4)"}}
E["item:furlbrow-s-deed"] = {t="item",n="Furlbrow's Deed",z="westfall",s="Beside their broken wagon near Westfall's border, Theodore and Verna Furlbrow have lost their farm to the Defias Brotherhood. Their land deed is in bandit hands, and with it went their home and livelihood.",h="Beside their broken wagon near Westfall's border, Theodore and Verna Furlbrow have lost their farm to the...",sec={{t="Stolen Land and Forged Claims",b="Theodore Furlbrow and Verna signed the deed to secure their family farm in Westfall. After the Defias Brotherhood overran the region, bandits drove them from home and carried the deed into Elwynn Forest. Notes on its back show the thieves planned to copy it and forge claims to other properties. The Furlbrows lost their livelihood and took to the road, with no home to return to.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Defias steal the deed?",a="Notes on the deed show the Defias meant to study its seal and signatures, then forge claims to seized homesteads across Westfall.",al={"why steal deed","why did bandits want the deed","defias deed purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who does this deed belong to?",a="The deed belongs to Farmer Theodore Furlbrow and his wife Verna. Outlaws drove the Westfall homesteaders from their farm.",al={"who owns furlbrows deed","who is furlbrow","whose deed is this"},it="identity"},{q="Where can the Furlbrows be found?",a="You can find Theodore and Verna just inside Westfall, beside their broken wagon on the main road from Elwynn Forest.",al={"where are the furlbrows","farmer furlbrow location","where to return deed"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Furlbrows still care about the deed if they fled?",a="The Furlbrows know Westfall is too dangerous for honest folk now. Still, proof of ownership gives them hope of reclaiming their land if peace returns.",al={"why do they want deed back","will furlbrows return"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Furlbrow's Deed come from, and who made it?",a="The deed is an official land title for an expanse of farmland in Westfall, signed by Theodore Furlbrow and cosigned by his wife, Verna. It established their rightful ownership of their family homestead before Defias bandits shook them down and stole it right out of their hands.",al={"furlbrow deed origin","who made furlbrows deed","where did the deed come from"},it="origin",add="4593623b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how the Defias have damaged civil order in the lands beside Stormwind, even by stealing simple property titles.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can bring a little comfort to people driven from their homes while the kingdom has too few soldiers."},kw={"deed","defias","farm","furlbrow","theodore","verna","wagon","westfall"},rel={"quest:184","npc:farmer-furlbrow","zone:westfall","zone:elwynn","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65"},src={"Furlbrow's Deed","Furlbrow's Deed (Classic)"}}
E["item:furlbrow-s-pocket-watch"] = {t="item",n="Furlbrow's Pocket Watch",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Farmer Furlbrow searches for the pocket watch he lost when Defias bandits drove him from home. Verna’s father gave it to him on their wedding day.",h="In Westfall, Farmer Furlbrow searches for the pocket watch he lost when Defias bandits drove him from home.",sec={{t="A Keepsake in the Ruins",b="Defias bandits drove Farmer Furlbrow and Verna from their home at the Furlbrow Pumpkin Patch in the night. In their flight, he left the watch in a wardrobe in the overrun farmhouse. Benny Blaanco and his cutthroats keep watch nearby.\n\nThe couple now camps along the road. The watch is one of the few pieces of their former life the outlaws have not ruined.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the pocket watch so important to Farmer Furlbrow?",a="Verna’s father gave the watch to Farmer Furlbrow on their wedding day. After the Defias Brotherhood took their land, home, and livelihood, it remains the couple’s last deeply sentimental possession.",al={"why does furlbrow want his watch","furlbrow watch importance","who gave furlbrow the watch"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the pocket watch kept?",a="The watch lies in a wardrobe in the Furlbrow farmhouse, among the pumpkin fields west of the main road where the Furlbrows are stranded.",al={"where is the pocket watch","furlbrow wardrobe location","how to find the watch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is guarding the watch?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has taken over the farmhouse. Benny Blaanco and his cohort loiter near the wardrobe.",al={"who has furlbrow's watch","watch guard westfall","benny blaanco watch"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Did the Defias steal the watch directly?",a="The Defias did not steal the watch directly. The Furlbrows fled in a panic when the bandits raided the pumpkin patch, and Farmer Furlbrow forgot to pack it. It remained in their bedroom wardrobe as the farm was overrun.",al={"did defias loot the watch","was the watch stolen"},it="history"},{q="What is Furlbrow's Pocket Watch?",a="It is a cherished family heirloom belonging to Farmer Furlbrow. The watch was given to him by his wife Verna's father as a gift on their wedding day. When the Defias Brotherhood overran their pumpkin farm, the couple had to flee for their lives in the middle of the night, inadvertently leaving the precious timepiece behind in their wardrobe.",al={"what is furlbrows watch","pocket watch furlbrow","farmer furlbrow pocket watch"},it="identity",add="42b91745"},{q="Where does Furlbrow's Pocket Watch come from, and who made it?",a="The watch originally belonged to Verna Furlbrow's father, who presented it to Farmer Furlbrow on the couple's wedding day. The specific craftsman or city of its manufacture is unknown, but to the displaced farmers, it represents one of the few lasting tokens of their family and former life before the Defias drove them from their land.",al={"who made furlbrows pocket watch","where did furlbrow get the watch","pocket watch origin furlbrow"},it="origin",add="ba43cdcd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Helping the Furlbrows recover their heirloom shows how completely the Stormwind crown has failed to protect Westfall’s hard-working farmers from organized banditry."},kw={"benny blaanco","defias","farmer furlbrow","furlbrow's pocket watch","the forgotten heirloom","verna furlbrow","wardrobe","westfall"},rel={"quest:64","npc:farmer-furlbrow","npc:verna-furlbrow","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","quest:65"},src={"Furlbrow's Pocket Watch","The Forgotten Heirloom"}}
E["item:gnoll-paw"] = {t="item",n="Gnoll Paw",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Gnoll Paw bounties help defend Westfall’s farmsteads from Riverpaw packs. The People's Militia pays for proof that patrols have slain gnolls.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Gnoll Paw bounties help defend Westfall’s farmsteads from Riverpaw packs.",sec={{t="Bounty of the Militia",b="The People's Militia defends Westfall from Sentinel Hill. The royal army is absent, and the crown seems blind to troubles in the countryside. So ordinary citizens and volunteers face outlaws, rogue mechanoids, and Riverpaw gnolls.\n\nCaptain Danuvin offers bounties for proof that gnolls have been slain. Their paws show that patrols have searched the scrublands instead of resting beneath the watchtower.",sp=0},{t="A Coordinated Menace",b="Riverpaw gnolls forage across Westfall’s plains. Militia observers have noticed signs that the packs coordinate closely with Defias thieves based around the Deadmines. The gnolls terrorize farmsteads and prey on supply wagons, helping shield the bandits from local resistance.\n\nBringing in gnoll paws helps keep the overland routes between Sentinel Hill and Elwynn Forest open.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Why does Captain Danuvin want Gnoll Paws?",a="Captain Danuvin asks for Gnoll Paws as proof that a patrol has crossed the Westfall plains and slain gnolls. With few resources and no aid from the crown, the militia pays bounties for that evidence.",al={"why collect paws","danuvin gnoll paws","what are gnoll paws for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which gnolls drop these paws?",a="The paws come from Riverpaw gnolls that prowl Westfall’s grasslands, hills, and abandoned farms.",al={"where to get gnoll paws","which gnolls have paws","gnoll paw location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Are the gnolls acting alone in Westfall?",a="No. Captain Danuvin and the militia suspect Riverpaw gnolls work with bandits and thieves based around the Deadmines. Together, they threaten local farmsteads.",al={"are gnolls working with defias","gnoll deadmines connection","who commands the gnolls"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Why isn't Stormwind dealing with the gnoll threat?",a="Stormwind has left Westfall largely to its own devices amid domestic turmoil and political paralysis. Local farmers and The People's Militia bear nearly all the work of defending the countryside.",al={"why no stormwind army","where is the army","why does the militia fight gnolls"},it="history"},{q="What is a Gnoll Paw?",a="A Gnoll Paw is a severed hand taken from a Riverpaw gnoll prowling the plains of Westfall. For the People's Militia stationed at Sentinel Hill, these grizzly trophies serve as undeniable physical proof that an adventurer has actively patrolled the territory and culled the aggressive gnoll packs threatening local homesteads.",al={"what is gnoll paw","gnoll paw item","what are gnoll paws"},it="identity",add="aa4b645a"},{q="Where do Gnoll Paws come from?",a="These paws come directly from the wild Riverpaw gnolls scattered across the grasslands and abandoned farms of Westfall. The feral gnolls roam the region preying on farmers and coordinating with outlaws, making their severed paws a grim bounty taken directly from fallen raiders in the field.",al={"where to get gnoll paws","who drops gnoll paws","gnoll paw source"},it="origin",add="96952327"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, taking bounties from The People's Militia helps keep Stormwind's western breadbasket safe from roaming beasts and organized bandits.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track Riverpaw packs across Westfall’s open plains while helping secure rural outposts."},kw={"danuvin","gnoll paw","patrolling westfall","people's militia","riverpaw","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:102","npc:captain-danuvin","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:gnoll","quest:12","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:deadmines"},src={"Gnoll Paw","Patrolling Westfall"}}
E["item:handful-of-oats-classic"] = {t="item",n="Handful of Oats (Classic)",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Old Blanchy needs oats after the Furlbrows' wagon breaks down.",h="In Westfall, Old Blanchy needs oats after the Furlbrows' wagon breaks down.",sec={{t="Fodder Among the Ruins",b="Westfall once fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. Now its farms lie overgrown or under the control of Defias bandits and rogue harvest golems. Sacks of grain and oats remain by barns and outbuildings, and in overgrown fields. Travelers and refugees whose wagons break down along the dusty roads can gather the leftover oats for their weary draft horses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Handfuls of Oats used for?",a="The oats feed Old Blanchy, the Furlbrow family's weary mare. Their wagon broke down on a Westfall road, leaving her exhausted and hungry.",al={"what are oats for","why collect oats","handful of oats use"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Where can these oats be found?",a="Oats lie in sacks scattered across abandoned Westfall farms. Look especially in the southwest.",al={"where to find oats","sack of oats location","how to get oats"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the oat sacks left unguarded?",a="The Defias Brotherhood rose suddenly, and rogue harvest machinery rampaged through the fields. Farmers fled in haste, leaving harvested grain and other supplies in their fields and barns.",al={"why abandoned sacks","who left the oats"},it="origin"},{q="What is a Handful of Oats?",a="A Handful of Oats is simple livestock feed scooped from the burlap sacks left scattered across Westfall's farmsteads. In fertile days, these grains sustained the kingdom's workhorses and plowing beasts. Today, with the fields abandoned to rogue harvest golems and bandits, loose oats are among the few scraps of clean fodder left for a hungry beast of burden.",al={"what are handful of oats","handful of oats item","what is handful of oats"},it="identity",add="67495104"},{q="Why does anyone want a Handful of Oats?",a="Verna Furlbrow desperately needs them to nourish Old Blanchy, her family's devoted workhorse. After the Furlbrows fled their home, their wagon broke down on the road, leaving Blanchy exhausted, starving, and on her last legs. A few nourishing handfuls of grain are all that keep the faithful mare alive while the family remains stranded.",al={"who wants handful of oats","why gather oats","why need handful of oats"},it="why_wanted",add="a4d08151"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Westfall, you can offer stranded refugees like the Furlbrows a small act of mercy by gathering oats on Stormwind's neglected frontier."},kw={"blanchy","furlbrow","grain","handful of oats","oats","sacks of oats","westfall"},rel={"quest:151","npc:blanchy","zone:westfall","topic:gnoll"},src={"Handful of Oats (Classic)","Poor Old Blanchy"}}
E["item:lewis-note"] = {t="item",n="Lewis' Note",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Quartermaster Lewis sends a courier by gryphon to seek armor for Westfall's garrison. The order goes to a private armorer in Stormwind.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Quartermaster Lewis sends a courier by gryphon to seek armor for Westfall's garrison.",sec={{t="A Plea for Steel",b="The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill receives little support from Stormwind's House of Nobles. Skirmishes with the Defias Brotherhood keep wearing down its small supply of gear. So Quartermaster Lewis turns to private trade to keep the defenders equipped. His order goes outside the kingdom's military channels. An Alliance courier must fly by gryphon to Old Town and present it to Osric Strang, who owns Limited Immunity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lewis' Note?",a="Lewis' Note is Quartermaster Lewis's written order to Osric Strang, an armorer in Stormwind, asking him to send protective gear to the Westfall garrison.",al={"what is this item","lewis note purpose","what does the note do"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote this note?",a="Quartermaster Lewis wrote the note. He manages supplies, provisions, and armaments for the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",al={"who is lewis","quartermaster lewis"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives the note?",a="The note first goes to Thor, the gryphon master at Sentinel Hill. From there, it travels to Osric Strang at his armor shop, Limited Immunity, in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"where does the note go","who gets lewis note","osric strang note"},it="target"},{q="Why doesn't the garrison just get armor from the kingdom?",a="Stormwind's government has largely neglected Westfall. Its defenders receive neither direct military funding nor armor from the crown, so Lewis relies on traders such as Osric Strang to equip the militia.",al={"why buy from osric","why no stormwind help","stormwind aid westfall"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human adventurer, carrying the order shows you how to use the kingdom's gryphon routes. It also shows how little Stormwind's rulers do to equip Westfall's defenders."},kw={"gryphon","lewis' note","limited immunity","old town","osric strang","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","thor"},rel={"quest:6181","quest:6281","npc:quartermaster-lewis","npc:osric-strang","npc:thor","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:old-town","zone:westfall"},src={"Lewis' Note","A Swift Message (Classic)","Continue to Stormwind (Classic)"}}
E["item:okra"] = {t="item",n="Okra",z="westfall",s="At Saldean's Farm, Okra helps feed Westfall's homesteaders. The crop grows in the farm's plots and thickens the stews that sustain them.",h="At Saldean's Farm, Okra helps feed Westfall's homesteaders.",sec={{t="A Staple of Saldean's Farm",b="Saldean's Farm still yields vegetables while much of Westfall lies fallow, threatened by Defias outlaws and rogue harvest golem attacks. Okra grows in the tilled plots around the farm and persists through the harsh conditions. It nourishes local homesteaders when trade and supplies from Stormwind run dry.",sp=0},{t="Westfall Stew",b="Salma Saldean's famous Westfall Stew depends on okra. She combines sliced pods with whatever meat settlers can hunt across the dusty plains, including vulture flesh, goretusk snouts, and coastal murloc eyes. The pods break down in the heat, thickening thin broth into a filling, restorative meal. For settlers clinging to their homesteads, fresh okra turns sparse scavenging into a hot supper.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does okra grow in Westfall?",a="Okra grows in the tilled plots at Saldean's Farm along Westfall's central road. The green plants thrive in furrows near Farmer Saldean's homestead.",al={"okra location","where to find okra","where does okra grow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is okra used for?",a="Salma Saldean gathers okra at Saldean's Farm for her signature Westfall Stew. Its natural starch thickens the broth, blending vulture meat, boar snouts, and murloc eyes into a hearty meal.",al={"okra uses","what is okra for","why do i need okra"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is okra important to the Saldeans?",a="With trade disrupted and little aid from the kingdom, homesteaders rely on what they can grow and hunt. Okra is one of the few cultivated crops remaining at Saldean's Farm, helping feed the family and passing travelers.",al={"saldean okra","why okra matters"},it="motive"},{q="What is okra?",a="Okra is an edible vegetable that grows in the tilled soil of Westfall. Cultivated on farmsteads such as the Saldean Farm, its pods are hearty enough to survive the region's troubled climate and make a reliable staple crop for the struggling homesteaders.",al={"what is okra","okra item","okra plant"},it="identity",add="301f0b5e"},{q="Where does okra come from?",a="Okra is cultivated locally on the farms of Westfall, most notably by Salma and Farmer Saldean at the Saldean Farm. While much of the countryside has fallen to ruin and neglect, sturdy crops like okra continue to grow in the surviving tilled fields.",al={"where does okra come from","who grows okra","okra origin"},it="origin",add="5bbd3a8c"},{q="Why does Salma Saldean want okra?",a="Salma Saldean needs fresh okra as an essential ingredient for her famous Westfall Stew. When sliced and simmered alongside wild game and local meats, the vegetable helps thicken the savory broth, providing a rich, filling meal to sustain the people of the plains.",al={"why is okra wanted","why does salma want okra","who wants okra"},it="why_wanted",add="b45f6830"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A wandering cook knows a good stew needs more than raw meat. Okra gives tough wilderness forage the starch and body of a hot meal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind nobles dine on imported meats, while frontier Alliance homesteaders cultivate stubborn crops like okra amid Westfall's ruins."},kw={"crop","farm","okra","saldean","salma saldean","vegetable","westfall stew"},rel={"quest:36","npc:salma-saldean","subzone:saldean-s-farm","zone:westfall","topic:murloc"},src={"Okra","Westfall Stew (Classic 2)"}}
E["item:red-leather-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Leather Bandana",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, the Red Leather Bandana marks those who defy Stormwind’s Crown. The Defias Brotherhood wears it to cover their faces and show their cause.",h="In Westfall, the Red Leather Bandana marks those who defy Stormwind’s Crown.",sec={{t="Mark of the Brotherhood",b="Across Westfall’s fields and abandoned farms, highwaymen, looters, and rebellious laborers wear crimson bandanas to hide their faces. The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill sees each as proof of loyalty to Edwin VanCleef's rogue fraternity. Scout Galiaan gathers the bandanas from travelers to follow the Brotherhood’s movements and dwindling numbers across the region.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red leather bandanas?",a="The Defias wear red bandanas to hide their faces while raiding farms and roads. They also show allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's uprising against Stormwind.",al={"defias mask","why red bandana","defias bandana meaning"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Who wants these bandanas collected in Westfall?",a="Scout Galiaan of the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill asks travelers to gather the bandanas. He tracks the gang’s movements and confirms the deaths of roving bandits with them.",al={"who takes red bandanas","galiaan bandana quest","sentinel hill bandana turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these bandanas found?",a="Defias rogues, highwaymen, and smugglers carry these bandanas at camps, in fields, and in mines across Westfall.",al={"red bandana drop","farm red bandanas","who drops red leather bandana"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, each red bandana taken from a fallen outlaw means one less brigand threatening Westfall’s starving farmers and beleaguered militia.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the crimson mask as a sign of underground banditry in human lands. Thieves organized with military precision wear it."},kw={"brotherhood","defias","galiaan","mask","red leather bandana","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:153","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill"},src={"Red Leather Bandana","Red Leather Bandanas"}}
E["item:scale-of-old-murk-eye"] = {t="item",n="Scale of Old Murk-Eye",z="westfall",s="Along Westfall's coast, Captain Grayson seeks proof that Old Murk-Eye is dead. The ghost haunts Westfall Lighthouse, where the murloc's attacks left the beacon dark.",h="Along Westfall's coast, Captain Grayson seeks proof that Old Murk-Eye is dead.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Coastal Scourge",b="Old Murk-Eye made Westfall's coast a killing ground. Captain Grayson, the ghost bound to Westfall Lighthouse, says the cunning murloc rallied weaker-minded murlocs to raid the shore. Murk-Eye drove away the keeper's family, leaving the beacon dark when Grayson's ship struck the rocks.\n\nWhen the family returned to relight the flame, Murk-Eye attacked again and slaughtered them. Grayson seeks one of the creature's scales as proof that the shore is clear of its fiercest predator.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scale of Old Murk-Eye used for?",a="Captain Grayson needs the scale as proof that Old Murk-Eye is dead. The ghost haunts Westfall Lighthouse and seeks vengeance because Murk-Eye left the beacon dark when Grayson's ship wrecked, then slaughtered the lighthouse keeper's family.",al={"who wants the scale","murk eye scale turn in","scale of old murk eye use"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is a vicious, cunning murloc leader who prowls Westfall's sandy shores. He can organize and coerce his kin into deadly, coordinated raids against shoreline outposts.",al={"who is murk eye","murk eye lore","old murk-eye"}},{q="Why did Old Murk-Eye target the lighthouse?",a="Old Murk-Eye first raided the lighthouse to drive away the keeper and his family, leaving the coast in darkness. When they returned to relight the flame, he rallied his kin for another attack and murdered the whole family. Ships were left blind to the dangerous coastal shoals.",al={"why attack lighthouse","lighthouse raid","murk eye lighthouse"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Scale of Old Murk-Eye?",a="It is a tough, distinctive scale taken directly from the hide of Old Murk-Eye, the notorious murloc leader terrorizing the coast of Westfall. Carrying it serves as irrefutable proof that the deadly coastal raider has finally been slain.",al={"what is scale of old murk eye","scale of old murk eye item","murk eye scale"},it="identity",add="6e72b95e"},{q="Where does the Scale of Old Murk-Eye come from?",a="The scale comes from the natural hide of Old Murk-Eye, an unusually cunning and vicious murloc prowling the Westfall shoreline. It was not forged or crafted by mortal hands, but harvested from his carcass after besting him in battle.",al={"scale of old murk eye origin","where to get scale of old murk eye","who made scale of old murk eye"},it="origin",add="383f15e9"},{q="Why does Captain Grayson want the Scale of Old Murk-Eye?",a="Captain Grayson, the ghost of a sea captain lingering at the Westfall Lighthouse, seeks vengeance and closure. Old Murk-Eye scared off the lighthouse keeper's family, leaving the beacon dark the night Grayson's ship struck the rocks, and when the family returned he raided again and slaughtered them. Grayson demands the scale as undeniable evidence that the beast is dead and the coast is safer.",al={"why does grayson want the scale","why is scale of old murk eye wanted","who wants scale of old murk eye"},it="why_wanted",add="e7059369"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance sailor traveling the Great Sea toward Stormwind, helping end Old Murk-Eye's attacks can keep the Westfall beacon lit and vessels from striking the rocks."},kw={"captain grayson","coastal menace","murloc","old murk-eye","scale of old murk-eye","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"npc:old-murk-eye","quest:104","npc:captain-grayson","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","zone:westfall","topic:murloc"},src={"Scale of Old Murk-Eye","The Coastal Menace (Classic)"}}
E["item:shaw-s-report"] = {t="item",n="Shaw's Report",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Shaw's Report carries SI:7 intelligence to Gryan Stoutmantle. Written by Master Mathias Shaw, it tells of the Stonemasons Guild, Edwin VanCleef, and their grievance with the crown after Stormwind was rebuilt.",h="In Westfall, Shaw's Report carries SI:7 intelligence to Gryan Stoutmantle.",sec={{t="Intelligence on the Stonemasons",b="Shaw's Report reaches Sentinel Hill from SI:7's covert headquarters in Stormwind. It gives the People's Militia its first clear account of who leads the bandits ravaging Westfall. Edwin VanCleef once led the Stonemasons Guild, whose masons rebuilt Stormwind City after its destruction in the First War.\n\nThe crown and nobility refused to pay them fairly, and resentment took root. Shaw's intelligence links the displaced craftsmen to the uprising now seizing the kingdom's outer territories.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="What is Shaw's Report?",a="Shaw's Report is a sealed intelligence dossier that Master Mathias Shaw prepared for Gryan Stoutmantle. Shaw leads Stormwind's covert SI:7 agency, and the report contains the crown's intelligence on the Stonemasons Guild and Edwin VanCleef's history.",al={"shaw report","what does shaw write","shaws report contents"},it="identity"},{q="What does the report reveal about Edwin VanCleef?",a="The report names Edwin VanCleef as the former head of the Stonemasons Guild. He oversaw Stormwind's reconstruction after the First War, then he and his artisans revolted after the kingdom's rulers denied them proper payment.",al={"vancleef in report","what does it say about vancleef"}},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need this report?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle needs the report because he leads the People's Militia against coordinated bandit raids in Westfall. With no regular kingdom troops to help, he relies on Mathias Shaw's intelligence to learn who directs the outlaws and what drives them.",al={"why send report to gryan","why stoutmantle needs report"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does Stoutmantle react to the report?",a="The report leaves Gryan Stoutmantle deeply unsettled. He remembers Edwin VanCleef as an industrious, accomplished craftsman and struggles to believe such a respected builder turned villain without further proof.",al={"gryan reaction","stoutmantle reaction"}},{q="Where does Shaw's Report come from, and who made it?",a="The report was drafted by Master Mathias Shaw, the head of Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7. Working out of his headquarters in Old Town, Shaw compiled SI:7's gathered intelligence concerning the history of the Stonemasons Guild and Edwin VanCleef to send back to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill.",al={"who wrote shaws report","who made shaw's report","where does shaw's report come from"},it="origin",add="c86c6e50"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Shaw's Report shows how far Master Mathias Shaw's reach extends. He leads SI:7, Stormwind's espionage network.",["faction:Alliance"]="The report lays bare Stormwind's internal rot. An unpaid debt to the kingdom's architects helped spark an insurrection that threatens the realm's farmlands."},kw={"defias","edwin vancleef","gryan stoutmantle","mathias shaw","shaw's report","si:7","stonemasons guild","westfall"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:edwin-vancleef","quest:65","topic:stonemasons-guild","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:2300","zone:westfall"},src={"Shaw's Report","The Defias Brotherhood (4)"}}
E["item:stoutmantle-s-response-to-solomon"] = {t="item",n="Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon",z="westfall",s="From Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle sends word to Lakeshire that no soldiers can be spared for Redridge Mountains.",h="From Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle sends word to Lakeshire that no soldiers can be spared for Redridge...",sec={{t="A Plea Denied",b="Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire asks Sentinel Hill for help as Blackrock orcs and gnolls press his town. Gryan Stoutmantle answers in writing and mourns Lakeshire's losses. Yet Westfall faces a war of its own. The People's Militia formed after the Crown withdrew its garrison, and farmers and volunteers now fight the Defias Brotherhood alone. Stoutmantle's forces are already bleeding and stretched thin, with no men to spare for another abandoned frontier.",sp=0},{t="The Kingdom's Neglect",b="Redridge and Westfall share a grim plight. The royal court in Stormwind City has forsaken them both. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and the kingdom's standing army is mysteriously kept from provincial borders. Outlying towns must form volunteer watches or perish. Solomon receives the sealed reply and sees that neither town can save the other. The realm frays while the capital remains silent.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written in Stoutmantle's response?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle writes that Westfall fights a brutal war against the Defias Brotherhood and has lost Stormwind's army, as Redridge has. He mourns the fallen defenders but declines Magistrate Solomon's request for reinforcements.",al={"what does the letter say","stoutmantle letter contents","response to solomon text"},it="item"},{q="Why did Solomon ask Westfall for help in the first place?",a="Lakeshire faces heavy assaults by gnolls and Blackrock orcs. Magistrate Solomon's plea to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind has brought no troops, so he asks the People's Militia across Elwynn for help from fellow frontier defenders.",al={"why ask westfall","solomon asking stoutmantle","why did lakeshire ask for the militia"}},{q="Why can't the People's Militia spare any troops?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer army struggling to hold Sentinel Hill and the surrounding plains against the Defias Brotherhood. Casualties mount daily, and without regular army support, sending fighters to Lakeshire would leave Westfall undefended.",al={"why won't militia help","can westfall help redridge","why refuse solomon"},it="motive"},{q="Why isn't the Stormwind Army protecting these towns?",a="No one in either town knows why the Stormwind Army is absent. Stoutmantle writes that Stormwind withdrew its troops and left Westfall defenseless, while Solomon wonders what could call the army away from its people. Both regions rely on local volunteers.",al={"where is stormwind army","why won't stormwind help","stormwind desertion"},it="history"},{q="What is Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon?",a="It is an official written dispatch from Gryan Stoutmantle, commander of the People's Militia in Sentinel Hill, addressed to Magistrate Solomon in Redridge. The letter delivers the grim news that Westfall is engulfed in its own desperate war against the Defias Brotherhood and cannot send any soldiers or resources to aid Lakeshire.",al={"what is stoutmantle's response","stoutmantle letter solomon","gryan response lakeshire"},it="identity",add="399f6159"},{q="Where does Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon come from, and who made it?",a="It was penned by Gryan Stoutmantle himself at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. After reading Magistrate Solomon's plea for reinforcements, Stoutmantle drafted the reply and entrusted it to you to carry across the kingdom back to Redridge Mountains.",al={"who wrote stoutmantle's response","who made stoutmantle response to solomon","where did stoutmantles response come from"},it="origin",add="945d8c3a"},{q="Why does anyone want Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon?",a="Magistrate Solomon is awaiting this reply in Lakeshire, hoping for military aid to fend off the Blackrock orc invasion threatening Redridge. He needs Stoutmantle's word to know whether the People's Militia can ride to Lakeshire's defense or if his town must face its perils alone.",al={"who wants stoutmantle's response","why deliver stoutmantle letter","why bring response to solomon"},it="why_wanted",add="c46920a1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this letter shows outlying settlements pleading with one another for aid while the capital withholds its forces.",["race:Human"]="As a human defender, you see Westfall and Redridge struggling to survive without Stormwind's royal guards."},kw={"gryan","lakeshire","letter","magistrate solomon","messenger to westfall","peoples militia","redridge","solomon","stoutmantle","westfall"},rel={"quest:143","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:12","subzone:lakeshire","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon","Messenger to Westfall (2)"}}
E["item:verna-s-westfall-stew-recipe"] = {t="item",n="Verna's Westfall Stew Recipe",z="westfall",s="As the Furlbrows prepare to leave their Westfall farm, Verna sends her stew recipe to Salma Saldean. Its familiar comfort may remain for those who stay.",h="As the Furlbrows prepare to leave their Westfall farm, Verna sends her stew recipe to Salma Saldean.",sec={{t="A Farewell Gift",b="Verna and Farmer Furlbrow have made their home in Westfall for years. Now the Defias Brotherhood and rogue harvest golems run rampant across the countryside. The Furlbrows wait for their wagon to be repaired so they can flee toward Stormwind.\n\nWhile they wait, Verna writes down her beloved Westfall Stew formula. She entrusts it to travelers bound for her neighboring friend, Salma Saldean. That way, those left behind may still know the stew's familiar comfort.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Verna giving away her stew recipe?",a="Verna and Farmer Furlbrow are fleeing Westfall because bandits and rogue machines have overrun their fields. As they leave their farm, Verna hopes her friend Salma Saldean will keep making the stew for those who remain.",al={"why verna gives recipe","why westfall stew recipe","verna recipe purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is the recipe meant for?",a="Verna's recipe is meant for Salma Saldean, who lives just beyond the fork in the road at the Saldean Farm.",al={"who gets the recipe","who do i bring the recipe to","where does the stew recipe go"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the Furlbrows planning to go?",a="The Furlbrows are waiting for their wagon to be repaired so they can flee to Stormwind City. They seek safety from the chaos and brigandry threatening the countryside.",al={"where are furlbrows going","where does verna go","furlbrow destination"},it="place"},{q="What makes Westfall Stew notable in the region?",a="Westfall Stew is a regional staple made possible by local farming and game. With food scarce and farms abandoned, its hearty recipes help surviving farming families endure.",al={"what is westfall stew","why westfall stew matters","westfall stew lore"},it="fame"},{q="What is Verna's Westfall Stew Recipe?",a="It is a handwritten culinary guide penned by Verna Furlbrow, detailing the ingredients and preparation needed to make hearty Westfall Stew. Rather than let her signature local dish be lost when she abandons her dangerous homeland, Verna jots down the instructions on parchment so her neighbor can continue feeding travelers and locals alike.",al={"verna stew recipe","what is verna's westfall stew recipe","vernas westfall stew recipe item"},it="identity",add="39bb19d7"},{q="Where does Verna's Westfall Stew Recipe come from, and who made it?",a="The recipe was scribbled down by Verna Furlbrow right at the Furlbrow homestead in northern Westfall. Facing mounting attacks from Defias bandits and scavenging beasts, she wrote it out personally just before packing her family wagon to flee the countryside.",al={"who made verna stew recipe","verna recipe origin","where did verna stew recipe come from"},it="origin",add="b68c02b6"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For cooks, Verna's handwritten recipe preserves local knowledge as Westfall's farms fall into ruin.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the recipe tells of loyal homesteaders driven from their land by lawlessness while Stormwind struggles to project its authority."},kw={"cooking","furlbrow","recipe","saldean's farm","salma saldean","verna furlbrow","westfall stew"},rel={"quest:36","npc:verna-furlbrow","npc:salma-saldean","npc:farmer-furlbrow","subzone:saldean-s-farm","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Verna's Westfall Stew Recipe","Westfall Stew (Classic)"}}
E["item:wiley-s-note"] = {t="item",n="Wiley's Note",z="westfall",s="At Lakeshire, Wiley the Black writes a confidential note for Gryan Stoutmantle to repay a debt. Its contents point to alliances made by the Defias Brotherhood, drawing Stormwind's intelligence service into the inquiry.",h="At Lakeshire, Wiley the Black writes a confidential note for Gryan Stoutmantle to repay a debt.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Ledger",b="Wiley the Black, a rogue in Lakeshire, writes the dispatch in Redridge. He gives it to Gryan Stoutmantle to repay an old favor. In the note, Wiley tells what he knows of the Defias Brotherhood's plans. The Brotherhood has allies among regional gnolls, kobolds, and goblin operatives.",sp=0},{t="The Stonemason Connection",b="Wiley's note links the Defias Brotherhood to the Stonemasons Guild, which rebuilt Stormwind after the Second War. Seeing the political weight of that connection, Gryan Stoutmantle sends the note to Master Mathias Shaw, spymaster of SI:7. So Stormwind's intelligence service joins the inquiry.",sp=1,bt={"q123.3"}}},faq={{q="Who wrote Wiley's Note?",a="Wiley the Black, a rogue in Lakeshire, wrote the note. He gave it to Gryan Stoutmantle of the People's Militia to repay an outstanding favor.",al={"author of wileys note","who is wiley","wiley the black note"},it="origin"},{q="What information does the note contain?",a="The note warns that the Defias Brotherhood is plotting something vast and has allies among gnolls, kobolds, and goblins. Gryan Stoutmantle seeks advice on its more sensitive contents.",al={"wileys note contents","what does the note say","defias note info"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the note need to be delivered?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle receives the note at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. After reading it, he orders it delivered to Master Mathias Shaw at SI:7 headquarters in Stormwind City.",al={"who gets wileys note","turn in wileys note","where do i take the note"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send the note to SI:7?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle suspects the note points to a deeper conspiracy than banditry. He sends it to Mathias Shaw, head of Stormwind intelligence, for investigation.",al={"why show mathias shaw","why give note to shaw","si7 wileys note"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see Wiley the Black and Master Mathias Shaw, leader of SI:7, handle the missive.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see local banditry in Westfall recognized as an organized threat to Stormwind's stability."},kw={"defias brotherhood","gryan stoutmantle","mathias shaw","sentinel hill","si:7","stonemasons","wiley the black","wiley's note"},rel={"npc:wiley-the-black","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:mathias-shaw","quest:65","quest:2300","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:old-town"},src={"Wiley's Note","The Defias Brotherhood (2)","The Defias Brotherhood (3)"}}
E["npc:brainwashed-noble"] = {t="npc",n="Brainwashed Noble",z="westfall",s="Deep in the caverns outside the Deadmines, Brainwashed Noble remains in Defias hands. Enchantment has stripped him of his will, and he now guards their refuge beside undead minions instead of walking Stormwind's grand halls.",h="Deep in the caverns outside the Deadmines, Brainwashed Noble remains in Defias hands.",sec={{t="A Pawn of the Brotherhood",b="Brainwashed Noble wanders the passages into the Deadmines among bandits and rotting corpses. His highborn finery points to Stormwind's House of Nobles, perhaps as a sitting member or a scion. Edwin VanCleef took him captive. The Defias chose enchantment over ransom and bent his mind into that of a spellcasting guard for their sanctuary. Their hatred for the peers who refused to pay after Stormwind was rebuilt reaches even into the caverns beneath Westfall.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Who is the Brainwashed Noble?",a="Brainwashed Noble is an aristocratic human thought to belong to Stormwind's House of Nobles. The Defias Brotherhood captured and magically subdued him deep in the Deadmines caverns.",al={"who is brainwashed noble","what is brainwashed noble","noble in deadmines"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a Stormwind noble inside the Deadmines caves?",a="The Defias Brotherhood holds a bitter grudge against Stormwind's aristocracy over debts left unpaid after the city was rebuilt. A captured noble gives them magical labor and a means of personal vengeance.",al={"why is he in deadmines","why is noble in caves"},sp=1,it="why_here",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Where can the Brainwashed Noble be found?",a="Brainwashed Noble wanders the cavern tunnels of Moonbrook that lead toward the Deadmines entrance, among passages inhabited by skeletal undead.",al={"brainwashed noble location","where does he spawn"},sp=1,gp=true,bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="How was he brainwashed?",a="No one knows which caster brainwashed him. Renegade spellcasters and enchanters among the Defias in Westfall can bend a captive's mind through sorcery.",al={"who brainwashed him","how is he controlled"}},{q="Whose side is the Brainwashed Noble on?",a="He serves the Defias Brotherhood, though not by choice. Robbed of his own will, this aristocratic captive now guards the network of tunnels leading toward Edwin VanCleef's stronghold, turning his arcane arts against anyone who intrudes upon outlaw territory.",al={"brainwashed noble side","who does the brainwashed noble fight for","is brainwashed noble defias"},it="side",add="7d2ae820"},{q="Who is the Brainwashed Noble tied to?",a="His past ties him to Stormwind's House of Nobles, the ruling aristocracy currently governing under Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. In his present shattered state, however, he is bound entirely to Edwin VanCleef and the Defias conspirators who hold his leash deep within the Moonbrook mines.",al={"brainwashed noble ties","who controls brainwashed noble","brainwashed noble faction"},it="ties",add="0b33d704"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, seeing a peer of the realm reduced to a mindless sentry beneath Westfall shows how deep the Defias Brotherhood's grudge runs against Stormwind's ruling elite.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize Brainwashed Noble's magical staves and arcane tricks, such as Polymorph. They suggest he received formal magical training in the capital before his mind was shattered."},kw={"brainwashed noble","deadmines","defias brotherhood","house of nobles","moonbrook","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"subzone:deadmines","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","zone:deadmines","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:65","topic:human"},src={"Brainwashed Noble"}}
E["npc:captain-danuvin"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Danuvin",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Captain Danuvin rallies Westfall’s defenders. He directs People's Militia volunteers and recruits to patrol the roads and drive back Gnolls and outlaws. Their orders guard supply lines and farmlands from hostile hands.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Captain Danuvin rallies Westfall’s defenders.",sec={{t="Holding the Hill",b="Captain Danuvin directs patrols from Sentinel Hill's fortified tower. Stormwind's regular garrison has withdrawn, leaving Westfall's defenses weak. So he relies on travelers, farmhands, and volunteer fighters to keep some order across the plains.",sp=0},{t="Patrolling the Frontier",b="Captain Danuvin watches the roads and open lands around Sentinel Hill. Riverpaw Gnolls raid near the central outposts, so he sends patrols to thin their packs and secure the perimeter. His orders keep marauders and opportunists from surrounding the camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Captain Danuvin?",a="Captain Danuvin can be found at Sentinel Hill, the Alliance outpost in central Westfall. He is usually near the fortified tower overlooking the road.",al={"danuvin location","where is captain danuvin","danuvin westfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction does Captain Danuvin represent?",a="Captain Danuvin serves the Alliance and supports Westfall's local defenders. He works closely with Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia.",al={"danuvin faction","who does danuvin serve"},it="side"},{q="What duties does he assign to adventurers?",a="Captain Danuvin assigns recruits to patrol the plains and drive back Riverpaw Gnolls advancing on Sentinel Hill.",al={"danuvin quests","what does captain danuvin want","patrolling westfall quest"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Danuvin relying on volunteers instead of the Stormwind Army?",a="Stormwind has left Westfall without garrison troops. Captain Danuvin and the leaders at Sentinel Hill rely on mercenaries and militia recruits.",al={"why no stormwind army","why militia","stormwind garrison westfall"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Danuvin have connections outside of Westfall?",a="Captain Danuvin's ties are to Westfall, his homeland. He has vowed to stand by the citizens who stayed, so he focuses on the plains and roads around Sentinel Hill.",al={"danuvin redridge","danuvin connections"},it="ties"},{q="What is his role compared to Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia and directs Westfall's broad defense. Captain Danuvin handles field tactics, road patrols, and the Gnoll threat near the base.",al={"stoutmantle vs danuvin","is danuvin in charge"},it="identity"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Captain Danuvin is one of the few military figures upholding order in Westfall despite the crown's neglect. As an Alliance recruit, you can help defend the realm.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can bring your discipline and strength against Gnoll packs and help clear the highway.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can help Captain Danuvin defend your homeland and keep Stormwind's breadbasket safe from raiders and beasts."},kw={"captain danuvin","danuvin","gryan stoutmantle","patrolling westfall","peoples militia","riverpaw","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:102","quest:12"},src={"Captain Danuvin"}}
E["npc:captain-grayson"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Grayson",z="westfall",s="At Westfall Lighthouse, Captain Grayson keeps watch over the beacon that failed him. His ship struck the dark coast, and now he tends the light so other sailors do not share his fate.",h="At Westfall Lighthouse, Captain Grayson keeps watch over the beacon that failed him.",sec={{t="A Life Cut Short by the Rocks",b="Captain Grayson once sailed the southern seas of the Eastern Kingdoms as a ship’s captain. One night, the lighthouse fire went dark as his vessel neared Westfall’s jagged shoals. The ship struck the rocks, and Grayson died with it. He awoke as an earthbound phantom, bound to the coast.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy at the Beacon",b="After death, Captain Grayson went to Westfall Lighthouse, hoping to learn what waited beyond life. There he saw Old Murk-Eye, a notorious murloc, drive away the keeper and his family. The brave keepers returned to rekindle the flame. But Old Murk-Eye rallied the surrounding murlocs and led a second, brutal slaughter. Grayson could only watch as the family was butchered.",sp=0},{t="A Ghostly Vigil",b="With the keepers dead and Westfall crumbling under neglect, Captain Grayson bears the beacon’s solemn burden on his spectral shoulders. He asks passing travelers to gather fuel for the great flame. He also seeks vengeance for the slaughtered family: hunt down Old Murk-Eye and drive back the coastal murlocs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Grayson?",a="Captain Grayson is a human ghost pirate at Westfall Lighthouse. His ship struck the coast when the beacon went dark, and now he tends the light to protect passing sailors.",al={"grayson identity","who is the ghost pirate","lighthouse ghost"},it="identity"},{q="How did Captain Grayson die?",a="Captain Grayson died when his pirate vessel struck the treacherous rocks along Westfall’s shore. The lighthouse was dark that night, leaving him and his crew without warning as the ship was torn apart.",al={"grayson death","how did grayson become a ghost","what killed captain grayson"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the real lighthouse keeper?",a="Coastal murlocs attacked the keeper and his family. The brave family escaped the first assault and returned to relight the beacon, but Old Murk-Eye rallied a second attack and slaughtered them before Grayson’s eyes.",al={"where is the lighthouse keeper","what happened to the keepers","lighthouse family"},it="history"},{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is a cunning, vicious murloc chieftain on the Westfall shoreline. He led the attack that killed the lighthouse keeper’s family and threatens anyone trying to keep the beacon lit.",al={"murk eye lore","old murk eye","murloc leader westfall"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Grayson want the lighthouse kept lit?",a="Grayson drowned when the coast was pitch black, and sees keeping the lighthouse lit as his solemn duty after death. He wants to spare other sailors the same fate on the shoals.",al={"grayson motivation","why light the beacon"},it="wants"},{q="Is Captain Grayson hostile to adventurers?",a="No. Though Grayson was a pirate in life, he bears no ill will toward the living. He has witnessed too much slaughter and seeks peace and help tending the flame.",al={"is grayson friendly","grayson hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="Whose side is Captain Grayson on?",a="Captain Grayson serves no mortal kingdom. Though he was once a living pirate captain and remains neutral to living travelers, he seeks aid from travelers willing to secure the coast. In death, his true allegiance is not to Stormwind or any navy, but to the Westfall Lighthouse and the safe passage of mariners.",al={"captain grayson faction","is grayson alliance or horde","who does grayson serve"},it="side",add="8f770f95"},{q="Why is Captain Grayson at the lighthouse?",a="Grayson was drawn to the lighthouse after his ship was smashed against the Westfall shoreline because the beacon was dark. Bound to the mortal world as a spirit, he journeyed here and watched helplessly as Old Murk-Eye and his murlocs slaughtered the lighthouse keeper's family. With the keepers dead, Grayson resolved to remain and protect the beacon himself.",al={"why is captain grayson here","why did grayson come to westfall lighthouse","what brought grayson to the lighthouse"},it="why_here",add="2ee261a8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="With the Defias Brotherhood choking Westfall and Stormwind neglecting its borders, Alliance travelers must answer Grayson’s plea and keep the lighthouse flame burning.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can honor your sacred duty to defend the helpless and drive back the murderous murlocs by helping Grayson, though he is an undead spirit.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can offer solace to Grayson’s restless soul. Guilt and grief anchor his spirit after he watched an innocent family die."},kw={"captain grayson","ghost pirate","grayson","lighthouse","old murk-eye","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"subzone:westfall-lighthouse","quest:103","quest:104","quest:152","zone:westfall","topic:murloc","topic:pirate","topic:alliance"},src={"Captain Grayson"}}
E["npc:daphne-stilwell"] = {t="npc",n="Daphne Stilwell",z="westfall",s="On Westfall’s cliffs, Daphne Stilwell keeps watch over her orchard and home. She and her husband Jordan fled the north and now aid the Church of the Holy Light while guarding their land from nearby outlaws.",h="On Westfall’s cliffs, Daphne Stilwell keeps watch over her orchard and home.",sec={{t="A Life on the Cliffs",b="West of Moonbrook and the Deadmines exit, Daphne Stilwell tends a homestead and apple orchard on the bluffs. The Longshore lies below, while gryphon routes to Stranglethorn Vale pass high above. The farm may look quiet from either way, but bandits and scavengers roam nearby. Daphne works among the trees and keeps watch over her isolated land.",sp=0},{t="Refugees of the North",b="Before they came to Westfall, Daphne and her husband Jordan lived near Pyrewood Village in Lordaeron. They worked in what is now Shadowfang Keep. Darkness and disaster drove them south with thousands of other human refugees. Near Stormwind, Jordan’s renowned skill as a craftsman and Daphne’s steady presence brought them close to the Church of the Holy Light. They support the church and provide holy arms to paladins of the Silver Hand.",sp=0},{t="Defending the Farm",b="Daphne Stilwell faces danger from the Defias Brotherhood near the Deadmines. Jordan travels or works on holy weapons outside the capital, often leaving her alone to tend their coastal home. When brigands raided the farm for retribution or plunder, Daphne took up arms beside aspiring paladins sent by the Cathedral. She proved fierce and capable in battle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Daphne Stilwell?",a="Daphne Stilwell tends an isolated farmhouse above Westfall’s Longshore. She is married to the famed blacksmith Jordan Stilwell, and they fled the devastated northern kingdoms together.",al={"who is daphne","daphne stilwell info","stilwell wife"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Daphne come from?",a="Daphne lived in the north near Pyrewood Village and worked in what is now Shadowfang Keep. Calamity drove her and Jordan south to lands under Stormwind’s influence.",al={"daphne origin","where is daphne from","is daphne gilnean"},it="origin"},{q="Why is her farm attacked by the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Daphne’s farm overlooks Westfall’s southern waters from the cliffs above the Deadmines exit tunnels. Its closeness to the Defias stronghold makes it a target for outlaws seeking supplies or hoping to remove meddlers.",al={"why do defias attack daphne","defias farm attack","stilwell farm bandits"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="What is Daphne's connection to paladins?",a="Jordan aids the Church of the Holy Light by forging sanctified weapons. During their Tome of Valor trials, paladins of the Silver Hand are sent to Westfall to guard Daphne from bandits.",al={"paladin quest daphne","tome of valor daphne","why do paladins visit daphne"},it="ties"},{q="Can Daphne defend herself?",a="Yes. When the Defias attack her orchard, Daphne takes up a weapon and fights beside the paladins defending the homestead.",al={"does daphne fight","is daphne a warrior"},it="power"},{q="How do you reach her farmhouse?",a="Daphne’s farm sits on the clifftops of southwestern Westfall, southwest of Moonbrook near the Deadmines secret cove exit, overlooking the Longshore.",al={"where is daphne farm","how to get to stilwell farm","daphne stilwell location"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Daphne Stilwell on?",a="Daphne Stilwell is aligned with the Alliance and remains deeply loyal to the Church of the Holy Light. Alongside her husband Jordan, she has long aided the paladins of Stormwind, offering shelter and support to young defenders of the Light who seek out their secluded homestead.",al={"daphne stilwell faction","daphne stilwell alliance","who does daphne stilwell serve"},it="side",add="fe5dc862"},{q="What does Daphne Stilwell want?",a="Daphne wants little more than to tend her apple orchard and live in quiet peace alongside her husband, Jordan. However, with the Defias Brotherhood roaming the cliffs of Westfall and threatening her home, she relies on visiting paladins to help keep the bandits at bay.",al={"what does daphne stilwell need","daphne stilwell goal","daphne stilwell motives"},it="wants",add="5fa85e8c"},{q="Why is Daphne Stilwell here?",a="Daphne settled on this isolated bluff overlooking the Longshore after she and her husband fled Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. When darkness and madness overtook their northern home, they journeyed south into the kingdom of Stormwind to build a quiet life farming far from the Scourge.",al={"why is daphne in westfall","why is daphne stilwell at this farm","why did daphne leave shadowfang"},it="why_here",add="57f727ad"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you prove your devotion to protecting the innocent by defending Daphne Stilwell from Defias marauders during the Tome of Valor trials.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share the burden of the Stilwells, northern refugees who still serve the Alliance and the Church of the Holy Light amid Westfall’s dangers."},kw={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","jordan stilwell","longshore","orchard","pyrewood village","shadowfang keep","tome of valor","westfall"},rel={"npc:jordan-stilwell","quest:1649","zone:westfall","subzone:longshore","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","zone:shadowfang","zone:deadmines"},src={"Daphne Stilwell"}}
E["npc:farmer-furlbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Farmer Furlbrow",z="westfall",s="Near the Jansen Stead, Farmer Furlbrow and his wife, Verna, are stranded beside their broken wagon. Driven from their northern Westfall farm by the Defias Brotherhood, they hope to reach Elwynn Forest.",h="Near the Jansen Stead, Farmer Furlbrow and his wife, Verna, are stranded beside their broken wagon.",sec={{t="A Life Packed on a Wagon",b="The Furlbrows salvaged what they could and set out for Elwynn Forest. Theodore urged neighbors like Farmer Saldean to leave as well. Now bandits and wild beasts threaten them on the road.\n\nVerna tends their horse, Old Blanchy, while Theodore keeps watch. He hopes to recover the pocket watch Verna's father gave him on their wedding day. He also wants to warn Sentinel Hill about the approaching bandits.",sp=0},{t="Evidence of Land Seizure",b="Before the Furlbrows fled, Defias thugs pressured Theodore and took the deed to his farmland, which Verna had cosigned. They believed it could help them forge deeds of their own. The bandits still hold it.\n\nYou can recover the deed and return it to Theodore. If Westfall becomes fit for honest folk again, the deed could help the Furlbrows reclaim their land.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Farmer Furlbrow?",a="Driven from their northern Westfall pumpkin farm by the Defias Brotherhood, Theodore Furlbrow and his wife, Verna, fled together. They are stranded beside their broken wagon near the Jansen Stead.",al={"farmer furlbrow","theodore furlbrow","who is furlbrow"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Farmer Furlbrow stranded on the road?",a="Theodore's wagon broke down as he and Verna fled Westfall for Elwynn Forest. They are stranded by the road with their horse, Old Blanchy.",al={"why is his wagon broken","why is furlbrow on the road","broken cart westfall"},it="why_here"},{q="What heirloom did Farmer Furlbrow lose?",a="Theodore lost the pocket watch Verna's father gave him on their wedding day as they fled their farm. He hopes to recover it.",al={"forgotten heirloom watch","furlbrow watch","pocket watch"},it="item"},{q="Does Farmer Furlbrow have any family outside Westfall?",a="No relatives outside Westfall are recorded. Theodore's family is his wife, Verna, who is stranded with him beside their broken wagon and their horse, Old Blanchy.",al={"furlbrow family","furlbrow brother"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Farmer Furlbrow on?",a="Farmer Furlbrow is an ordinary Westfall peasant loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. He has no love for the Defias Brotherhood that seized his lands and drove him out. Though bitter over the lack of royal protection, he still turns to fellow Alliance travelers and the People's Militia for aid.",al={"farmer furlbrow faction","who does furlbrow support","is furlbrow alliance"},it="side",add="d2bcffbc"},{q="What does Farmer Furlbrow want?",a="Farmer Furlbrow wants nothing more than to fix his broken wagon and escape Westfall with his wife, Verna, and their old horse, Blanchy. With their pumpkin farm overrun by Defias bandits, his priority is gathering supplies, recovering his lost family heirloom, and putting the lawless frontier behind them.",al={"what does furlbrow need","farmer furlbrow goal","furlbrow intentions"},it="wants",add="81475819"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance citizen, you see how completely civil authority has failed in Westfall. Loyal people must abandon their homes without royal soldiers to defend them."},kw={"blanchy","defias","furlbrow","heirloom","jansen","pumpkin","theodore","verna","wagon","watch"},rel={"npc:verna-furlbrow","quest:64","quest:184","quest:109","subzone:jansen-stead","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall"},src={"Farmer Furlbrow"}}
E["npc:farmer-saldean"] = {t="npc",n="Farmer Saldean",z="westfall",s="At Saldean's Farm in central Westfall, Farmer Saldean and his wife, Salma, keep working troubled fields. Other farmers flee or give up, but he faces rogue harvest golems and growing banditry.",h="At Saldean's Farm in central Westfall, Farmer Saldean and his wife, Salma, keep working troubled fields.",sec={{t="Holding the Plow",b="Farmer Saldean remembers Westfall before its prosperity crumbled. Overgrown fields, rampaging mechanical harvest watchers, and predatory bandits now surround his farm. Yet he refuses to yield his land.\n\nOther homesteaders have abandoned their acres or turned to thievery. Saldean and his wife, Salma, stay to harvest what little grain they can. He asks wandering adventurers to destroy the rogue Harvest Watchers in his fields and his neighbors' fields, so he can clear the soil for planting.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe of Westfall",b="Between Sentinel Hill and the northern bridge, Saldean's defense of his homestead helps keep civilian life going. He remains tied to the People's Militia despite the hard times. Once his immediate troubles are settled, he sends able-bodied travelers to Gryan Stoutmantle.\n\nClearing the wild harvest reapers can give his farm only a temporary reprieve. The lawlessness strangling the countryside still has to be dealt with.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Farmer Saldean?",a="Farmer Saldean is a veteran human farmer at Saldean's Farm in Westfall, where he lives with his wife, Salma. Though famine, rogue harvest golems, and growing banditry threaten his land, he refuses to abandon it.",al={"saldean","who is saldean","saldean npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Farmer Saldean's farm in trouble?",a="Westfall's automated harvest golems have malfunctioned and gone wild. They prowl cropland and attack anyone in sight, so Saldean needs adventurers to destroy the mechanical watchers in his fields and neighboring fields and reclaim his land.",al={"why are harvest golems attacking","saldean farm problem"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can Farmer Saldean be found?",a="Farmer Saldean can be found outside his farmhouse at Saldean's Farm, just off the main road in central Westfall and north of Sentinel Hill.",al={"saldean location","where is saldean","saldean farm location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Saldean support the People's Militia?",a="Yes. Saldean is busy defending his crops and home, but he directs capable adventurers down the road to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill to help the People's Militia defend the region.",al={"saldean gryan stoutmantle","saldean militia"},it="side"},{q="What unique items does Saldean sell?",a="Saldean sells staple bread and Special Chicken Feed, a curious grain sought by travelers hoping to befriend the local fowl wandering Westfall.",al={"saldean vendor","special chicken feed vendor"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What does Farmer Saldean want?",a="Saldean wants nothing more than to protect his homestead, harvest his crops, and scrape together a living alongside his wife, Salma. With Westfall gripped by lawlessness and neglected by Stormwind, he relies on traveling adventurers to clear the rogue mechanical harvest reapers running amok through his fields and to assist the local People's Militia in restoring safety to the region.",al={"what does saldean want","saldean goal","farmer saldean wants"},it="wants",add="b644bbfd"},{q="Why is Farmer Saldean here?",a="Saldean refuses to be driven off his land. The thieves have run off nearly every other farmer in Westfall, but he stays behind at Saldean's Farm with his wife, Salma, to tend his soil and hold onto his home despite the encroaching dangers.",al={"why is saldean in westfall","why does saldean stay","farmer saldean origin"},it="why_here",add="340c71f6"},{q="Who is Farmer Saldean tied to?",a="Farmer Saldean runs his homestead alongside his wife, Salma Saldean, who manages their hearth and cooking. He also works in cooperation with Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill, directing able-bodied champions to aid their struggle against the outlaws threatening the breadbasket of the kingdom.",al={"farmer saldean family","who is saldean married to","salma saldean relation"},it="ties",add="4625baa0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see Saldean's stubborn resolve among Westfall's remaining loyalists. They cling to Kingdom soil even when the crown's soldiers are nowhere to be seen.",["profession:Cooking"]="Farmers like Saldean are the crumbling backbone of Stormwind's food supply. Securing his crop keeps basic bread on tables across the kingdom."},kw={"chicken feed","farmer saldean","harvest watcher","saldean","saldean's farm","salma","the killing fields","westfall"},rel={"subzone:saldean-s-farm","quest:9","quest:109","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Farmer Saldean"}}
E["npc:foreman-thistlenettle"] = {t="npc",n="Foreman Thistlenettle",z="westfall",s="Below the Deadmines, Foreman Thistlenettle's crew lies trapped beneath Moonbrook. He served both the Miners' League and the Explorers' League, and died with his miners when the tunnels fell in. Now he walks again as a ghoul, his guild badge still with him.",h="Below the Deadmines, Foreman Thistlenettle's crew lies trapped beneath Moonbrook.",sec={{t="A Brother's Grief",b="Wilder Thistlenettle has waited in Stormwind for word of his missing brother and the crew. The occupied tunnels have kept all news from reaching him. Now rumors say the fallen foreman walks among the dead. Travelers near the Deadmines are asked to end his torment and bring his badge to his grieving brother.",sp=1},{t="Tragedy in the Deadmines",b="Before the Defias Brotherhood took full control of the Deadmines, mining crews worked its rich veins. Foreman Thistlenettle led one expedition for both the Miners' League and the Explorers' League. Deep beneath Moonbrook, a violent cave-in sealed his party away from the surface. The miners died in the darkness, but found no rest. A necrotic taint raised Thistlenettle and his crew as ravenous ghouls, stalking the shadowed passages.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Who was Foreman Thistlenettle before he died?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle was a dwarf who worked with both the Miners' League and the Explorers' League. Before outlaws fully fortified the Deadmines, he led miners there to excavate and survey its underground veins.",al={"thistlenettle lore","who is foreman thistlenettle","thistlenettle background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Foreman Thistlenettle an undead ghoul?",a="A cave-in buried Foreman Thistlenettle and his mining party, killing them. Dark energies or lingering necromancy in the mines then animated their remains as restless ghouls.",al={"why is he a ghoul","how did thistlenettle die","thistlenettle undead"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Foreman Thistlenettle located?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle haunts a dead-end, collapsed tunnel in the Deadmines' outer maze, before the portal to its inner depths. His former miners, now ghouls, surround him.",al={"where to find thistlenettle","thistlenettle location","deadmines foreman spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is looking for Foreman Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle, Foreman Thistlenettle's brother, seeks proof of his fate. Wilder lives in Stormwind City's Dwarven District and asks travelers to bring back Thistlenettle's Badge.",al={"who wants thistlenettle dead","wilder brother","thistlenettle quest giver"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Foreman Thistlenettle on?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle belongs to no faction or cause anymore. Now a mindless, ravenous ghoul, he and his reanimated crew attack anyone foolish enough to venture into their collapsed corner of the Deadmines, whether Defias, Alliance, or wandering treasure hunters.",al={"thistlenettle faction","is foreman thistlenettle hostile","who does thistlenettle serve"},it="side",add="81248170"},{q="What does Foreman Thistlenettle want?",a="Whatever dwarven ambitions he possessed in life died in the cave-in. In undeath, Foreman Thistlenettle has no grand designs or schemes—only the blind, restless hunger shared by all ghouls, prowling the dark rubble for anything living that draws near.",al={"what does thistlenettle want","foreman thistlenettle motive","thistlenettle goal"},it="wants",add="a595eadc"},{q="Why is Foreman Thistlenettle here in the Deadmines?",a="He originally ventured deep into the Deadmines overseeing an expedition on behalf of the Miners' League and the Explorers' League. When disaster struck and a subterranean collapse crushed his crew, they were trapped beneath the rock and could never leave, even after death.",al={"why is thistlenettle in deadmines","how did thistlenettle get here","why is foreman thistlenettle here"},it="why_here",add="194368c4"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the loss of an Explorers' League foreman and his crew shows the dangers beneath the human kingdoms.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know tunnel collapses and hostile depths can make every descent perilous."},kw={"badge","cave-in","deadmines","foreman","ghoul","miners' league","thistlenettle","wilder"},rel={"npc:wilder-thistlenettle","quest:167","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:explorers-league","zone:westfall"},src={"Foreman Thistlenettle"}}
E["npc:grimbooze-thunderbrew"] = {t="npc",n="Grimbooze Thunderbrew",z="westfall",s="In Westfall's Dagger Hills, Grimbooze Thunderbrew keeps his casks and brews potent spirits. The eccentric dwarf speaks in verse and belongs to the Thunderbrew clan.",h="In Westfall's Dagger Hills, Grimbooze Thunderbrew keeps his casks and brews potent spirits.",sec={{t="A Brewer in Exile",b="Grimbooze Thunderbrew keeps camp in the Dagger Hills, where he tends his private casks. He left the snowy peaks of Dun Morogh, home of the Thunderbrew brewing family in Kharanos, for Westfall's windswept hills. Jovial and devoted to potent spirits, he speaks only in rhymes. A traveler must complete a simple task before he answers questions, and he is ready to test a thirsty palate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Grimbooze Thunderbrew?",a="Find Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Dagger Hills of southern Westfall. He keeps camp there with his brewing equipment.",al={"grimbooze location","where is grimbooze","where to find grimbooze thunderbrew"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Grimbooze speaking in rhymes?",a="No one can say for certain why Grimbooze speaks in rhymes. He delights in verse and asks anyone with a question to complete a simple task first.",al={"why does grimbooze rhyme","grimbooze rhyming","why is he talking in verse"}},{q="What is his connection to the Thunderbrew Distillery?",a="Grimbooze belongs to the Thunderbrew clan of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. His kin, including Ragnar Thunderbrew, tend the family distillery at home, while Grimbooze brews on his own in the Westfall hills.",al={"grimbooze distillery","is grimbooze related to ragnar","thunderbrew family"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Grimbooze Thunderbrew?",a="Grimbooze is a quirky, jovial dwarven brewer hailing from the famed Thunderbrew clan of Dun Morogh. Known for his legendary love of ale and penchant for speaking in riddles and verse, he left the family's home in Kharanos to brew on his own in the hills of Westfall.",al={"who is grimbooze","grimbooze thunderbrew","about grimbooze"},it="identity",add="21ebedd0"},{q="Whose side is Grimbooze Thunderbrew on?",a="Grimbooze is loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance, like the rest of the Thunderbrew clan. However, his true passion lies entirely with brewing and fine drink rather than politics or faction warfare, making him a friendly face to anyone who appreciates good stout.",al={"grimbooze faction","is grimbooze alliance","grimbooze side"},it="side",add="182004c2"},{q="What does Grimbooze Thunderbrew want?",a="Grimbooze is always looking to craft his signature brews and share them with fellow travelers. In exchange for ingredients or a bit of assistance, he is more than happy to offer you samples of potent Thunderbrew lager to keep your spirits high.",al={"what does grimbooze want","grimbooze goal","why does grimbooze need hops"},it="wants",add="9bf66a40"},{q="Why is Grimbooze Thunderbrew in Westfall?",a="Grimbooze left the cold peaks of Dun Morogh behind for the Dagger Hills, where he now spends his days brewing and musing in verse, far from the family distillery in Kharanos.",al={"why is grimbooze in westfall","grimbooze westfall why","what is grimbooze doing in westfall"},it="why_here",add="d50f3d5e"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Thunderbrew name. Finding one of the Thunderbrew brothers brewing wild recipes in the Westfall hills brings a taste of Dun Morogh.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn from Grimbooze's brewing, part of the Thunderbrew legacy."},kw={"ale","brewer","dagger hills","distillery","grimbooze","kharanos","thunderbrew","westfall"},rel={"subzone:dagger-hills","zone:westfall","subzone:thunderbrew-distillery","subzone:kharanos","npc:ragnar-thunderbrew","topic:dwarf","quest:117","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Grimbooze Thunderbrew"}}
E["npc:gryan-stoutmantle"] = {t="npc",n="Gryan Stoutmantle",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill in Westfall, Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia. A paladin of the Silver Hand, he came home from Lordaeron to defend his birthplace after Stormwind's crown left it to banditry.",h="At Sentinel Hill in Westfall, Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia.",sec={{t="A Knight Returned Home",b="Gryan Stoutmantle first served far from Westfall. As a young man, he traveled north to Lordaeron and took vows as a Knight of the Silver Hand. He endured the horrors of the Third War there. Then word reached him that his native province was falling into lawlessness, overrun by organized brigands and abandoned by the crown. Gryan left the northern fronts to defend honest farmers, resolved that Westfall would not fall as the north had.",sp=0},{t="The People's Militia",b="When Gryan returned, Westfall had almost no defenders. Royal neglect and political paralysis in the House of Nobles kept Stormwind from sending garrison troops. So Gryan formed the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill, gathering local farmers, sentries, and traveling mercenaries into a volunteer defense corps.\n\nThe militia holds a precarious line against the Defias Brotherhood, riverpaw gnolls, and hostile mechanoids. Even when nearby Lakeshire pleads for aid, Gryan cannot spare reinforcements.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking the Kingpin",b="Gryan Stoutmantle sought to learn who directed Westfall's ruin. He called in an old debt from Wiley the Black, a rogue in Redridge, and spoke with Mathias Shaw of SI:7. Their intelligence revealed that Edwin VanCleef led the bandits. VanCleef was the slighted master architect of the Stonemasons' Guild.\n\nAfter the militia captured a bandit trying to plunder a local wagon, Gryan used the prisoner to find the Brotherhood's headquarters beneath Moonbrook, within the Deadmines. He sent veteran champions to strike VanCleef directly.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia from its headquarters at Sentinel Hill. He is a paladin of the Silver Hand.",al={"who is gryan","stoutmantle lore","leader of westfall"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the People's Militia needed if Westfall belongs to Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's House of Nobles refused to send crown soldiers or treasury funds to protect Westfall. Left alone against marauders and gnolls, local farmers formed their own defense force under Gryan's leadership.",al={"why militia","where is stormwind army","why did stormwind abandon westfall"}},{q="What is Gryan's history with the Silver Hand?",a="As a young man, Gryan traveled to Lordaeron and became a paladin of the Silver Hand. He served on northern battlefields during the Third War, then left to defend his imperiled homeland.",al={"is gryan a paladin","gryan silver hand","gryan in lordaeron"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gryan refuse to send aid to Lakeshire?",a="Gryan had to refuse Magistrate Solomon's request for reinforcements against Redridge's gnolls and orcs. The People's Militia is stretched thin defending Sentinel Hill, and Gryan fears even a small detachment would leave Westfall to the Defias.",al={"magistrate solomon request","help redridge","why no troops to lakeshire"}},{q="How did Gryan discover where the Defias were hiding?",a="Gryan sought intelligence from Wiley the Black and Mathias Shaw, then sent adventurers to investigate the Brotherhood. What they uncovered is told in a hidden passage.",al={"finding deadmines","who found vancleef","defias traitor story"},sp=1},{q="Who is Wiley the Black to Gryan?",a="Wiley the Black lives at the inn in Lakeshire and owes his life to Gryan. Gryan has little affection for the rogue's unsavory nature, but used that debt to gain intelligence on Defias operations.",al={"wiley and gryan","wiley the black debt"}},{q="Whose side is Gryan Stoutmantle on?",a="Gryan is loyal to the Alliance, the Kingdom of Stormwind, and above all, the common people of Westfall. While Stormwind's royal court has turned a blind eye to the province's plight, Gryan has taken matters into his own hands by leading the People's Militia. He remains a faithful knight fighting to reclaim the realm for its rightful citizens.",al={"gryan stoutmantle faction","who does gryan serve","what faction is gryan"},it="side",add="7558c158"},{q="What does Gryan Stoutmantle want?",a="Gryan seeks to eradicate the Defias Brotherhood and restore peace, law, and order to Westfall. He wants to reclaim the province's overrun farms, purge the bandits and thieves terrorizing honest settlers, and ensure the safety of the farmers who have been abandoned by the Crown.",al={"gryan stoutmantle goal","what does gryan want","gryan motivation"},it="wants",add="c0a0d15a"},{q="Why is Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall?",a="Westfall is Gryan's homeland. When word reached him during the Third War in Lordaeron that criminal brigands were overrunning his home soil and driving farmers from their lands, he returned south to defend the province. Stationed at Sentinel Hill, he leads the People's Militia from the heart of the contested territory.",al={"why is gryan in westfall","why did gryan come to westfall","why is gryan at sentinel hill"},it="why_here",add="d2149791"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle tied to?",a="Gryan maintains ties with Mathias Shaw, the head of Stormwind's intelligence service SI:7, who provides him with vital reconnaissance regarding the Defias. He is also connected to Wiley the Black in Redridge, an old associate whose life he once saved, and coordinates with local defenders across neighboring lands.",al={"gryan stoutmantle allies","who does gryan work with","gryan connections"},it="ties",add="9073fb6b"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Gryan shows the Silver Hand's duty by bringing the Light's protection to Westfall's farmers when the church and crown ignore the poor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Stormwind's political inaction leave loyal citizens to arm themselves and defend the heartland.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share Gryan's roots in Westfall and the resilience of Stormwind's rural folk, who face brigands and neglect from the capital."},kw={"deadmines","gryan","people's militia","sentinel hill","silver hand","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall","wiley"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","quest:12","quest:65","npc:wiley-the-black","subzone:deadmines"},src={"Gryan Stoutmantle"}}
E["npc:marisa-du-paige"] = {t="npc",n="Marisa du'Paige",z="westfall",s="In the caves outside the Deadmines, Marisa du'Paige fights beside Moonbrook's outlaws. Few of their laborers and highwaymen wield arcane magic in southwestern Westfall.",h="In the caves outside the Deadmines, Marisa du'Paige fights beside Moonbrook's outlaws.",sec={{t="Arcane Talent in the Tunnels",b="Beneath Moonbrook, caves lead toward the Deadmines. Cutpurses, renegade miners, and thugs guard those tunnels. Among them is Marisa du'Paige, a skilled human mage. Many spellcasters train in Stormwind's Mage Quarter or serve the Kirin Tor, but Marisa has joined Westfall's outlaws and brigands in their underground passages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marisa du'Paige?",a="Marisa du'Paige is a rare human mage in the outer caves leading into the Deadmines. While thieves and laborers patrol those passages, she wields arcane spells to defend the underground network.",al={"marisa dupaige","who is marisa","rare in deadmines cave"},it="identity"},{q="Where can she be found?",a="Marisa du'Paige appears infrequently in the public cavern system beneath Moonbrook in Westfall. She can be found in the tunnels just outside the Deadmines instance portal threshold.",al={"marisa du'paige location","where is marisa dupaige","marisa spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a human mage hiding in the Deadmines caves?",a="Some arcane practitioners leave Stormwind's high towers. Deserters, renegades, and sympathetic commoners have joined the outlaw cause across Westfall, bringing steel and sorcery to strongholds beneath Moonbrook.",al={"why is she here","marisa lore","marisa dupaige faction"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Marisa du'Paige on?",a="Marisa du'Paige wears the garb and walks the subterranean halls of the Defias Brotherhood. Lurking deep within the caves of Moonbrook leading toward the Deadmines, she stands with Edwin VanCleef's rebellious brotherhood, casting her arcane spells against any intruders who threaten their stronghold.",al={"marisa dupaige faction","is marisa dupaige defias","who does marisa dupaige work for"},it="side",add="5e8e0d23"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Marisa du'Paige shows that arcane training in the kingdom reaches beyond the Kirin Tor's towers and Stormwind's wizard sanctum. Rogue spellcasters sell their talents to criminal networks.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, stay alert for du'Paige in the tunnels beneath Moonbrook. A spellcaster among the cutpurses can quickly make a skirmish deadly."},kw={"deadmines","human","mage","marisa du'paige","marisa dupaige","moonbrook","rare","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:human"},src={"Marisa du'Paige"}}
E["npc:mathias-shaw"] = {t="npc",n="Mathias Shaw",z="westfall",s="In Old Town, Mathias Shaw directs SI:7, Stormwind’s covert intelligence agency. He sends spies and scouts from the shadows to guard the realm against conspiracies within and horrors beyond.",h="In Old Town, Mathias Shaw directs SI:7, Stormwind’s covert intelligence agency.",sec={{t="Master of SI:7",b="Mathias Shaw leads Stormwind’s spies and assassins from SI:7’s hidden headquarters behind the barracks in Old Town. His covert network reaches across the Eastern Kingdoms and beyond. Loyal to the House of Wrynn, Shaw weighs each threat with care. Unseen daggers and stolen messages defend Stormwind as surely as armor and palace guards.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of VanCleef",b="Mathias Shaw once called Edwin VanCleef a childhood companion. He trained VanCleef in stealth and assassination, hoping the gifted stonemason would serve the kingdom beside him. But after the Stonemasons Guild was cast out following Stormwind’s rebuilding, VanCleef turned those lessons against the crown. Shaw now directs surveillance and infiltration across Westfall to break his old friend’s rebellion.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="Eyes Across the Kingdoms",b="Mathias Shaw watches threats beyond the unrest in Westfall and Elwynn. Reports of strange Forsaken operations in the Eastern Plaguelands led him to send five of his finest agents to investigate. Only one returned alive, babbling about “Nathanos” and a “Blightcaller” before dying in his sleep days later. Shaw now depends on trusted champions to go where his scouts vanish and uncover the dangers gathering at the kingdom’s borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mathias Shaw?",a="Mathias Shaw leads SI:7, Stormwind’s intelligence service and guild of assassins. From Old Town, he directs the kingdom’s spies and covert defense under the throne’s authority.",al={"who is shaw","leader of si7","mathias shaw lore","stormwind spymaster"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Mathias Shaw be found?",a="Mathias Shaw can be found inside SI:7’s headquarters in Stormwind City’s Old Town, behind the military barracks.",al={"shaw location","where is mathias shaw","find mathias shaw"},it="why_here"},{q="What is his connection to Edwin VanCleef?",a="Shaw’s connection to Edwin VanCleef is one of Westfall’s secrets. He records SI:7’s knowledge of the Stonemasons Guild in a report for Gryan Stoutmantle. Follow the Defias Brotherhood to its end to learn how closely the two are bound.",al={"shaw and vancleef","vancleef friend","mathias and edwin"},it="ties"},{q="What does SI:7 stand for?",a="SI:7 is Stormwind’s leading intelligence organization. Its agents gather information, conduct espionage, and carry out covert assassinations to protect the kingdom and Alliance interests.",al={"what is si:7","what does si7 mean","stormwind intelligence"}},{q="Why is Mathias Shaw interested in Westfall?",a="Shaw is interested in Westfall because it is the Defias Brotherhood’s stronghold. He keeps agents there to watch the rebels and disrupt their plots against Stormwind.",al={"shaw westfall","si7 westfall","klaven's tower"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the agents Shaw sent to the Plaguelands?",a="Shaw sent five agents to investigate suspicious Forsaken movements in the Eastern Plaguelands. Four never returned. The sole survivor babbled about “Nathanos” and a “Blightcaller” before dying in his sleep days later.",al={"shaw plaguelands quest","five scouts shaw","marris stead scouts"}},{q="Whose side is Mathias Shaw on?",a="Master Mathias Shaw serves the Alliance, the House of Wrynn, and the Kingdom of Stormwind with unshakeable loyalty. As leader of the realm's intelligence bureau, every covert mission he oversees and every spy he directs is dedicated to safeguarding Stormwind from internal subversion and foreign threats.",al={"mathias shaw faction","who does shaw serve","is mathias shaw loyal"},it="side",add="ad27d291"},{q="What does Mathias Shaw want?",a="Shaw's primary concern is eliminating existential threats to Stormwind before they strike. He directs SI:7's covert network to dismantle the Defias Brotherhood's plots, monitor dangerous Forsaken movements in the north, and gather the intelligence necessary to preserve the kingdom's security during an era of profound political vulnerability.",al={"mathias shaw goal","what does shaw want","shaw motives"},it="wants",add="14719004"},{q="Why is Mathias Shaw famous or feared?",a="Shaw is known throughout the kingdom as the master of spies and the master of assassins. Renowned for supreme skill in stealth, infiltration, and silent lethality, his far-reaching intelligence web means very little happens in the kingdom without his knowledge—or the intervention of his blades.",al={"why is mathias shaw famous","why is shaw feared","master of assassins"},it="fame",add="a0b783f7"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can look to Mathias Shaw as a master of human roguecraft. Alliance rogues are often sent to him for advanced tactical assignments and specialty poisons.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can count on Shaw to gather military intelligence for Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the boy-king Anduin. His spies guard the kingdom against subversion.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the Defias Brotherhood’s revolt as part of the bitter division in the Kingdom of Stormwind after its reconstruction."},kw={"assassin","blightcaller","kearnen","mathias shaw","old town","si:7","spymaster","stormwind","vancleef"},rel={"zone:stormwind","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","quest:2300","quest:2359","npc:nathanos-blightcaller","subzone:old-town","subzone:marris-stead"},src={"Mathias Shaw"}}
E["npc:old-murk-eye"] = {t="npc",n="Old Murk-Eye",z="westfall",s="Near the Westfall Lighthouse, Old Murk-Eye stalks the southern coast. His kind revere him, while sailors fear the deadly danger he brings to anyone who comes near the lighthouse.",h="Near the Westfall Lighthouse, Old Murk-Eye stalks the southern coast.",sec={{t="Terror of the Coastline",b="Old Murk-Eye hunts in the surf around the Westfall Lighthouse. He is far tougher and more aggressive than the murlocs common along Westfall’s shores. His attacks have brought grief to local mariners, so the spectral Captain Grayson seeks his death. Grayson offers a bounty for Old Murk-Eye’s pristine scales, hoping to break his hold on the shallows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Old Murk-Eye wander?",a="Old Murk-Eye patrols the sandy shores and shallow waters of southwestern Westfall, along the coast near the Westfall Lighthouse.",al={"old murk eye location","where to find old murk eye","where is murk eye"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Captain Grayson want Old Murk-Eye dead?",a="Captain Grayson sees Old Murk-Eye as a continuing threat to the coastal waters. He offers a bounty for a scale as proof of the deed, hoping to curb the violence along the beach.",al={"grayson murk eye","why kill old murk eye"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is Old Murk-Eye different from ordinary murlocs?",a="Yes. Old Murk-Eye is stronger, more durable, and more aggressive than the Coastrunner and Tidehunter lackeys around him. He acts as a tribal champion among the local shoreline packs.",al={"how tough is murk eye","is murk eye an elite"},it="power"},{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is an infamous and hardy murloc who patrols the coastline of Westfall near the Westfall Lighthouse. Recognized as a coastal menace by locals and sailors alike, he stands out among his kin as an exceptionally tough and cunning creature whose presence poses a constant danger to anyone walking the western shores.",al={"who is murk-eye","who is old murk eye","old murk-eye lore"},it="identity",add="0038f035"},{q="Whose side is Old Murk-Eye on?",a="Old Murk-Eye fights only for himself and his fellow shoreline murlocs. He owes no allegiance to any kingdom, guild, or faction, viewing air-breathers and land-dwellers as territorial trespassers to be driven off or slain.",al={"murk-eye faction","who does murk-eye work for","is murk-eye alliance"},it="side",add="295d9e5f"},{q="Why is Old Murk-Eye in Westfall?",a="Old Murk-Eye claims the coastal waters and rocky beaches around the Westfall Lighthouse as his hunting territory. The isolated shoreline provides bountiful fishing and a base to raid unwary travelers or sailors wrecked along the jagged coast.",al={"why is murk-eye here","why is old murk eye in westfall","murk-eye location lore"},it="why_here",add="48ac0465"},{q="Why is Old Murk-Eye famous or feared?",a="Old Murk-Eye has earned a reputation among sailors and locals as a notorious threat along the Westfall surf. He is stronger and more aggressive than typical coastal murlocs, surviving countless skirmishes and terrorizing anyone who nears the lighthouse coast until spirits like Captain Grayson place a bounty on his head.",al={"why is murk eye feared","why is old murk-eye infamous","legend of murk-eye"},it="fame",add="5afdb8dc"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers clearing Westfall, Old Murk-Eye is a notorious predator who preys on stranded travelers and ship crews."},kw={"captain grayson","coastal menace","murk-eye","murloc","old murk-eye","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"npc:captain-grayson","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","quest:104","zone:westfall","topic:murloc"},src={"Old Murk-Eye"}}
E["npc:quartermaster-lewis"] = {t="npc",n="Quartermaster Lewis",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill in Westfall, Quartermaster Lewis keeps supplies moving to the People's Militia. He serves the defenders and travelers holding the frontier against the Defias Brotherhood.",h="At Sentinel Hill in Westfall, Quartermaster Lewis keeps supplies moving to the People's Militia.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Tower's Stores",b="Quartermaster Lewis keeps the People's Militia supplied from Sentinel Tower. Stormwind's royal leaders offer little aid to impoverished Westfall, so Sentinel Hill relies on local volunteers and the provisions they can gather. Lewis hands out dry rations, fresh water, arrows, shot, and throwing blades. The fighters on watch need these basics to endure Defias raids.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Quartermaster Lewis?",a="Quartermaster Lewis serves at Sentinel Tower in Westfall. He handles everyday supplies, rations, and weapons for the People's Militia and adventurers helping defend the region.",al={"quartermaster lewis lore","who is lewis","sentinel hill quartermaster"},it="identity"},{q="What does Quartermaster Lewis sell?",a="Quartermaster Lewis sells basic goods for survival, including bread, milk, water, bags, flint, arrows, bullets, and throwing daggers.",al={"what does lewis sell","lewis inventory","westfall vendor items"},gp=true},{q="What is his role in regional quests?",a="With little aid from Stormwind, Lewis sends adventurers through Thor, the gryphon master, to deliver a note to Osric Strang, his armor supplier in Stormwind's Old Town. They bring Osric's crate of armor back to Sentinel Hill.",al={"lewis quests","a swift message","return to lewis"},gp=true},{q="Is Lewis part of the Stormwind Army?",a="Lewis serves the People's Militia, as do most defenders in Sentinel Hill, rather than an official force sent by the Stormwind crown. Westfall has been left largely to defend itself against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"is lewis army","stormwind guard lewis","peoples militia lewis"},it="side"},{q="Why is Quartermaster Lewis stationed here?",a="Quartermaster Lewis is stationed at Sentinel Hill in Westfall to supply the People's Militia and traveling Alliance adventurers. With Westfall largely abandoned by the crown and overrun by the Defias Brotherhood, defenders stationed at the tower rely on Lewis to provide vital provisions, ammunition, and survival goods.",al={"why is lewis here","quartermaster lewis westfall why","why is quartermaster lewis at sentinel tower"},it="why_here",add="f4ce3c2d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Westfall, you can resupply with Lewis in hostile country where crown resources are scarce.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you can get field supplies from Lewis in central Westfall, including shot and arrows for ranged defense."},kw={"lewis","peoples militia","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","vendor","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-tower","zone:westfall","quest:6181","quest:6285","zone:deadmines"},src={"Quartermaster Lewis"}}
E["npc:salma-saldean"] = {t="npc",n="Salma Saldean",z="westfall",s="At Saldean's Farm, Salma Saldean welcomes travelers and offers meals for help around the homestead. She and her husband, Farmer Saldean, tend their Westfall farm while bandits threaten the farms and Stormwind has left the region.",h="At Saldean's Farm, Salma Saldean welcomes travelers and offers meals for help around the homestead.",sec={{t="Hospitality in a Hard Land",b="Salma Saldean welcomes travelers to a farm that has endured while neighboring homesteads burned or fell to the Defias Brotherhood. A hearty pot waits on the stove, and she looks for capable hands to help around the farmstead.",sp=0},{t="Putting Food on the Table",b="Salma feeds her family and visitors with what Westfall provides. She teaches travelers to make Goretusk liver pie and Westfall stew from wild boar, vultures, murlocs, and stray okra.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Salma Saldean?",a="Salma Saldean farms with her husband at Saldean's Farm in central Westfall. She feeds and comforts travelers while trying to keep the farm running amid the region's collapse.",al={"who is salma","salma saldean lore","saldean farm wife"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Salma Saldean located?",a="Salma can be found outside her farmhouse at Saldean's Farm, along the road in central Westfall, just north of the crossroads toward Sentinel Hill.",al={"salma location","where is salma saldean","where is saldean farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What recipes does Salma Saldean teach?",a="Salma teaches travelers to make Goretusk Liver Pie and Westfall Stew with ingredients from Westfall's wildlife.",al={"westfall stew recipe","salma food","goretusk liver pie"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is it so hard for the Saldeans to find help?",a="Finding help is hard because farmers and laborers have fled marauding bandits, rogue harvest golems, and Stormwind's absent royal army. The few homesteaders who remain are short-handed.",al={"why abandoned farm","why help needed saldean","westfall farm abandoned"},it="conflict"},{q="How do the Saldeans survive the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Saldeans rely on passing adventurers and their own resilience to defend their property. Though danger surrounds them, they refuse to leave their land and home.",al={"saldean defias","why hasn't farm burned down"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Salma's husband?",a="Salma is married to Farmer Saldean, who works alongside her against malfunctioning harvest watchers and rogue beasts.",al={"salma husband","farmer saldean"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Salma Saldean on?",a="Salma stands firmly with the honest folk and struggling farmers of Westfall. While loyal to the Alliance in spirit, she and her husband have been left to fend for themselves without aid from Stormwind, focusing their hopes entirely on neighboring homesteaders doing right by one another.",al={"salma saldean faction","who does salma support","salma saldean side"},it="side",add="4311c40a"},{q="What does Salma Saldean want?",a="Salma wants to keep her family's farm running and ensure anyone who passes by finds a warm meal and a friendly ear. With most able hands driven out by hardship and bandits, she is eager for help gathering ingredients like goretusk livers so she can sustain those holding out in Westfall.",al={"what does salma want","salma saldean goals","what does salma need"},it="wants",add="31948cda"},{q="Why is Salma Saldean here?",a="Salma remains at Saldean's Farm because it is her home. Even as neighboring settlers fled the region's rising turmoil and lawlessness, she and her husband refused to abandon their land, determined to work the soil and provide comfort to anyone in need of shelter.",al={"why is salma in westfall","why stay at saldean farm","salma saldean why here"},it="why_here",add="f65c3c8f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Salma Saldean offers cooks traveling through Westfall practical recipes, including Westfall Stew and Goretusk Liver Pie, made with local wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Salma shows the stubborn resolve of Alliance homesteaders who hold on to their livelihoods despite the Crown's neglect.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, Salma's farm offers a glimpse of the hardship Stormwind's common folk face beyond the capital's fortified walls."},kw={"farmer saldean","goretusk liver pie","saldean's farm","salma saldean","stew","westfall","westfall stew"},rel={"subzone:saldean-s-farm","quest:36","quest:22","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Salma Saldean"}}
E["npc:scout-riell"] = {t="npc",n="Scout Riell",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Scout Riell watches Westfall from the roof of its stone watchtower. She serves the People's Militia and tracks the Defias Brotherhood, asking travelers to bring back the outlaws' red silk bandanas.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Scout Riell watches Westfall from the roof of its stone watchtower.",sec={{t="Eyes Over Westfall",b="Bandits and harvest golems threaten Westfall. Stormwind's royal army is absent, and the crown refuses aid. So the People's Militia must defend the region alone. The bandanas travelers bring back give Riell proof of the Defias Brotherhood's crimes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Scout Riell?",a="Scout Riell watches from the roof of the stone watchtower at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. Climb the stairs to reach her.",al={"riell location","where is scout riell","find riell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Scout Riell ask adventurers to do?",a="Riell asks travelers to collect red silk bandanas from Defias cutpurses, highwaymen, and smugglers in Westfall and the Deadmines. The bandanas prove the outlaws have been slain.",al={"riell quest","what quest does riell give","red silk bandanas quest"},sp=1,it="wants",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Why does Riell collect red silk bandanas?",a="A red silk bandana marks a member of the Defias Brotherhood. Collecting them proves the bandits terrorizing Westfall's homesteads are being reduced and takes away their unifying symbol.",al={"why bandanas","why red silk bandanas","defias masks"},it="purpose"},{q="Who does Scout Riell work for?",a="Riell serves the People's Militia, a volunteer defense force formed by Gryan Stoutmantle. He formed it to protect Westfall after the House of Nobles in Stormwind turned a blind eye to the province's plight.",al={"riell faction","is riell stormwind army","who does riell serve"},it="side"},{q="Who is Scout Riell?",a="Scout Riell is a human scout serving Sentinel Hill and the defense of Westfall. Stationed high atop the tower overlooking the region, she keeps watch over the surrounding countryside, monitoring the movements of the Defias Brotherhood and coordinating with local defenders to push back against the outlaws threatening the farmlands.",al={"who is riell","scout riell lore","who is scout riell"},it="identity",add="c25141c7"},{q="Why is Scout Riell stationed here?",a="Riell maintains a post at the top of the Sentinel Hill tower to serve as a lookout over Westfall. From this elevated vantage point, she can scan the plains for rogue activity, track the spread of the Defias Brotherhood, and enlist passing adventurers to take the fight directly to the thieves plaguing the province.",al={"why is scout riell here","why is riell in westfall","riell location purpose"},it="why_here",add="2f6a5f48"},{q="Who is Scout Riell tied to?",a="Riell serves alongside Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia stationed at Sentinel Hill. Together with her fellow scouts and sentinels, she acts as part of Westfall's beleaguered local defense force, relying on volunteer militia and brave adventurers to safeguard the kingdom's borders in the absence of royal troops.",al={"who does scout riell know","riell faction ties","riell allies"},it="ties",add="f57d6b81"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, Scout Riell shows Westfall's grim reality. Its abandoned people must hire mercenaries to fight the rising threat of the Defias Brotherhood.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors may recognize the Defias' signature red masks as genuine silk. It is an expensive fabric for common rural highwaymen."},kw={"defias brotherhood","people's militia","red silk bandanas","riell","scout riell","sentinel hill","tower","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:214","quest:12","zone:deadmines"},src={"Scout Riell"}}
E["npc:sprite-jumpsprocket"] = {t="npc",n="Sprite Jumpsprocket",z="westfall",s="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Sprite Jumpsprocket works beside gnomish and dwarven artisans. Like many gnomes who sought refuge after Gnomeregan fell, she learns engineering among fellow tinkers.",h="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Sprite Jumpsprocket works beside gnomish and dwarven artisans.",sec={{t="A Tinker in Stormwind",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Sprite Jumpsprocket trains as an apprentice engineer. Gnomes and dwarves work side by side there, forging metal and shaping intricate devices. The capital gives apprentice tinkers room to learn from experienced masters. Their work keeps the Alliance's everyday mechanisms and marvels in good order.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Ingenuity in Exile",b="After Gnomeregan fell, displaced gnomes carried their skills in tinkering, chemistry, and mechanics across Alliance lands. In Stormwind, the Dwarven District offered them a welcome refuge, with blast furnaces and workbenches at hand. Sprite Jumpsprocket shares their resolve to master engineering despite the hardships her kin have faced.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sprite Jumpsprocket?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is a female gnome apprentice engineer who lives and works in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket","who is sprite","sprite jumpsprocket lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Sprite Jumpsprocket?",a="You can find Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, among the workshops, anvils, and fellow engineering enthusiasts.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket location","where is sprite","find sprite jumpsprocket"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does she serve in Stormwind?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket trains as an apprentice engineer in Stormwind. She is one of the gnomish tinkerers honing their craft in the Alliance capital.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket role","what does she do","sprite jumpsprocket purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are gnomes like Sprite living in Stormwind?",a="After Gnomeregan fell, many gnomes sought refuge with their dwarven cousins in Ironforge and across human lands. Many settled in Stormwind City, where their industrial skill is in high demand.",al={"why gnomes in stormwind","gnomes dwarven district","gnome refugees"},it="history"},{q="Is Sprite Jumpsprocket tied to any notable quests?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is part of the Dwarven District's engineering community.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket quest","quests for sprite"},gp=true},{q="Is she associated with Westfall?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is stationed in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. Engineering creations across the region often share gnomish designs.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket westfall","westfall engineer"}},{q="Whose side is Sprite Jumpsprocket on?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is firmly aligned with the Alliance and the Gnomeregan Exiles. Like many displaced gnomes who sought refuge among their dwarven cousins and human allies after the fall of Gnomeregan, she plies her trade in the bustling Dwarven District of Stormwind City, offering her engineering skills in service to the realm and her fellow Alliance citizens.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket faction","sprite jumpsprocket alliance or horde","who does sprite jumpsprocket serve"},it="side",add="b9758f03"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn alongside Sprite Jumpsprocket among the sprockets, copper tubing, and volatile concoctions of Stormwind's most industrial district.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you share the perseverance of Gnomeregan's exiles. Far from their lost homeland, they keep their love of craft and mechanical mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how humans, dwarves, and gnomes work together in the Dwarven District. Their work helps keep the capital running."},kw={"apprentice","dwarven district","engineer","gnome","jumpsprocket","sprite jumpsprocket","stormwind","tinker"},rel={"subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","topic:gnome","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:westfall"},src={"Sprite Jumpsprocket"}}
E["npc:the-defias-traitor"] = {t="npc",n="The Defias Traitor",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, The Defias Traitor has revealed the Brotherhood's hidden base to spare his life. The People's Militia caught him stealing Farmer Saldean's wagon and now holds him beneath the watchtower.",h="At Sentinel Hill, The Defias Traitor has revealed the Brotherhood's hidden base to spare his life.",sec={{t="Leading the Way to Moonbrook",b="Under guard at Sentinel Hill's watchtower, the traitor must lead Alliance champions through hostile country to the hidden entrance beneath ruined Moonbrook. His former comrades hate him, and his captors despise him. Yet his betrayal gives the People's Militia a chance to strike at the Brotherhood's heart.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}},{t="A Bargain for Survival",b="The Defias Brotherhood does not command every member's loyalty to Edwin VanCleef. Gryan Stoutmantle's militia caught the petty thief trying to steal Farmer Saldean's wagon. Facing execution, he chose to save himself. He revealed the hidden base's exact location in exchange for his life.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="Who is the Defias Traitor?",a="The Defias Traitor once belonged to the Brotherhood. The People's Militia caught him trying to steal Farmer Saldean's wagon, and he agreed to lead Militia allies to the hidden lair to escape execution.",al={"who is this guy","defias traitor identity","who is the traitor at sentinel hill"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he standing outside the tower in Sentinel Hill?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia hold him outside their stronghold under armed guard. He remains there until volunteers escort him to the Defias hideout.",al={"traitor location","why is he at sentinel hill","where is the traitor"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does he lead you?",a="He leads travelers southwest across Westfall's plains to the derelict town of Moonbrook. There, he points out the concealed entrance to the Defias Hideout.",al={"where does the traitor go","traitor escort destination","where is defias hideout"},sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Why did he turn against the Defias Brotherhood?",a="He turned against the Brotherhood to save himself. Caught stealing from Farmer Saldean and facing execution, he offered its greatest secret in exchange for his life.",al={"why betray defias","traitor motive","why did he flip"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is the Defias Traitor on?",a="He is primarily on his own side. Originally a rogue operating within the Defias Brotherhood, he abandoned his loyalty to Edwin VanCleef after being captured by the People's Militia. Now cooperating under guard, he helps you and the Sentinel Hill authorities purely to avoid the gallows.",al={"defias traitor side","who does the traitor serve","is the defias traitor alliance"},it="side",add="ad165ef1"},{q="What does the Defias Traitor want?",a="He simply wants to stay alive. After being caught red-handed trying to steal Farmer Saldean's wagon, he struck a desperate bargain with Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia: his life and freedom from execution in exchange for leading you directly to the Brotherhood's secret hideout.",al={"what does the traitor want","defias traitor goal","why help defias traitor"},it="wants",add="9c073637"},{q="Who is the Defias Traitor tied to?",a="He was previously bound to Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood, knowing the ins and outs of their operations across Westfall. At present, he is held by Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia of Sentinel Hill, who rely on his firsthand knowledge to strike at the thieves' headquarters.",al={"defias traitor connections","who does the traitor know","defias traitor ties"},it="ties",add="a1cd0f31"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the People's Militia and Westfall's defenders, this prisoner marks a turning point in their struggle against the outlaws terrorizing the region.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how fragile loyalty can be among criminals. Cornered by the law, thieves and cutpurses may sell out their own."},kw={"defias hideout","defias traitor","farmer saldean","moonbrook","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:65","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:defias-hideout","subzone:moonbrook","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:farmer-saldean","zone:westfall","quest:12"},src={"The Defias Traitor"}}
E["npc:thor"] = {t="npc",n="Thor",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Thor keeps Westfall linked to Stormwind by gryphon flight. His trained mounts carry travelers and urgent messages over dangerous roads.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Thor keeps Westfall linked to Stormwind by gryphon flight.",sec={{t="The Eyrie of Sentinel Hill",b="Thor tends the gryphon roost at Sentinel Hill, linking Westfall's defenders with the rest of the kingdom. On the ground, the People's Militia faces bandits, gnolls, and malfunctioning harvest golems. His gryphons carry travelers and military dispatches above those perilous roads. Reports from Gryan Stoutmantle and urgent requests for aid can reach the court in Stormwind far sooner than a messenger on foot.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thor?",a="Thor tends the gryphon roost at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. His trained mounts carry travelers between Westfall and other Alliance settlements, including Stormwind City.",al={"who is this guy","sentinel hill flight master","thor npc"},it="identity"},{q="What role does he play in Westfall?",a="Thor keeps Sentinel Hill connected by air. He coordinates couriers bearing military messages between the People's Militia and Stormwind's high command, keeping commanders informed despite Defias activity on the roads.",al={"what does thor do","thor purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is gryphon travel important here?",a="Gryphon flights offer a swift, secure way around the dangerous roads between Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and Duskwood. Defias highwaymen, Riverpaw gnolls, and dangerous wildlife threaten those routes, while gryphons keep supplies and messages moving.",al={"why fly in westfall","westfall flight path"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Thor on?",a="Thor is loyal to the Alliance and stands directly with the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill. Operating under the authority of Stormwind's network of gryphon masters, he serves the kingdom by ferrying trusted messengers, soldiers, and adventurers across sovereign skies, ensuring Westfall maintains vital contact with the capital.",al={"thor allegiance","is thor alliance","who does thor serve"},it="side",add="5cbb8458"},{q="What does Thor want?",a="Thor aims to keep aerial transit running smoothly between Sentinel Hill and friendly outposts like Stormwind City. His focus is the care and readiness of his gryphons, ensuring urgent reports and travelers can bypass the bandits and wild beasts prowling Westfall's roads without delay.",al={"thor motive","what is thor doing","thor purpose westfall"},it="wants",add="a791490a"},{q="Why is Thor stationed at Sentinel Hill?",a="Sentinel Hill serves as the beleaguered bastion of the People's Militia against the Defias Brotherhood. Thor is stationed atop this redoubt because overland travel through Westfall is fraught with ambush, making gryphon flight the quickest and safest lifeline back to Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"why is thor in westfall","thor sentinel hill location","why is thor here"},it="why_here",add="f6f75bde"},{q="Who is Thor tied to?",a="Thor is tied to the Gryphon Keepers of Stormwind and works hand-in-hand with Gryphon Master Dungar Longdrink in the capital. Locally, he collaborates with Gryan Stoutmantle and the defenders of Sentinel Hill, providing them with essential transport and reconnaissance links to the outside world.",al={"thor connections","who does thor work with","thor allies"},it="ties",add="62307107"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion helping the People's Militia, you can take Thor's quickest route back to the capital to deliver field intelligence and restock supplies."},kw={"courier","flight master","gryphon","peoples militia","sentinel hill","thor","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:6181","quest:6281","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Thor"}}
E["npc:verna-furlbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Verna Furlbrow",z="westfall",s="Near Westfall’s northern border, Verna Furlbrow waits beside her broken wagon. Outlaws drove her from the family pumpkin patch, and the road toward Elwynn Forest left her stranded.",h="Near Westfall’s northern border, Verna Furlbrow waits beside her broken wagon.",sec={{t="A String of Misfortunes",b="Verna and her husband farmed pumpkins in northern Westfall until lawlessness drove them away. Outlaws took the farm, so they loaded what they could onto their cart and set out for Elwynn Forest with their horse, Old Blanchy. Their wagon broke down just down the road from the abandoned Jansen Stead.\n\nThe broken axle keeps them from going on. Verna faces the elements, bandit raids, and scavengers, and depends on travelers to keep her household fed and guarded.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Hearth",b="Verna still welcomes those forced to the roadside. Known across the region for creating Westfall Stew, she shares meals and warm fires with wandering transients and refugees who have suffered similar fates.\n\nHer cooking pot needs ingredients from the fields: boar snouts, murloc eyes, okra, and stringy vulture meat. From what the harsh frontier provides, Verna makes hearty meals for the destitute.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Verna Furlbrow camped along the road?",a="Verna and her husband fled their pumpkin farm after outlaws overran northern Westfall. Their wagon broke down near the Jansen Stead as they traveled toward Elwynn Forest, leaving them stranded beside the road.",al={"why is verna furlbrow here","verna furlbrow location","what happened to verna"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Farmer Furlbrow to her?",a="Farmer Theodore Furlbrow is Verna's husband. They worked their Westfall homestead together until bandits drove them from their land.",al={"verna furlbrow husband","is farmer furlbrow her husband"},it="ties"},{q="What is Westfall Stew?",a="Westfall Stew is a frontier dish Verna created. She makes it with wild boar snouts, stringy vulture meat, murloc eyes, and okra gathered from neighboring abandoned farms to feed stranded refugees.",al={"westfall stew quest","verna furlbrow stew","what does verna cook"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the Furlbrows' farm?",a="Organized bandits took the Furlbrows' pumpkin farm in northern Westfall during the kingdom's recent breakdown in security. The Furlbrows had to leave their home and fields.",al={"furlbrow pumpkin farm","furlbrows farm what happened"},it="history"},{q="Who is Verna Furlbrow?",a="Verna Furlbrow is a humble Westfall homesteader and the wife of Farmer Theodore Furlbrow. Known across the countryside for her hearty Westfall Stew and generous spirit, she and her husband worked a pumpkin patch in northern Westfall until violent unrest tore their livelihood apart. Now displaced and stranded by the roadside, she tries to keep spirits high despite relentless misfortune.",al={"who is verna furlbrow","verna furlbrow identity","verna furlbrow lore"},it="identity",add="c5a3789f"},{q="Whose side is Verna Furlbrow on?",a="Verna is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and stands firmly with the Alliance. Like many ordinary folk in Westfall, she harbors no love for the outlaws tearing the province apart, wishing only for peace, safety, and a chance to escape the lawlessness plaguing the countryside.",al={"verna furlbrow faction","is verna furlbrow alliance","verna furlbrow side"},it="side",add="b45ce146"},{q="What does Verna Furlbrow want?",a="Verna wants nothing more than to feed her family and safely escape Westfall. Having lost their farm, she and her husband intended to seek refuge in Elwynn Forest, but their broken wagon and hungry, weary horse have brought them to a standstill. For now, she seeks provisions like ingredients for her stew and oats for Old Blanchy to survive by the roadside.",al={"what does verna furlbrow want","verna furlbrow goal","why help verna furlbrow"},it="wants",add="0d4268c1"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Verna created Westfall Stew and teaches frontier cooks to make a hearty meal from scavenged meats and wild crops.",["faction:Alliance"]="The stranded Furlbrows show the human cost of Stormwind's neglected borders. Ordinary people are driven from their homes without royal soldiers sent to defend them."},kw={"broken wagon","furlbrow","jansen stead","old blanchy","refugee","theodore furlbrow","verna furlbrow","westfall stew"},rel={"npc:farmer-furlbrow","quest:36","quest:151","quest:64","subzone:jansen-stead","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Verna Furlbrow"}}
E["npc:wiley-the-black"] = {t="npc",n="Wiley the Black",z="westfall",s="At the Lakeshire Inn, Wiley the Black stays clear of trouble. He owes his life to Gryan Stoutmantle and shares what he knows of the Defias Brotherhood.",h="At the Lakeshire Inn, Wiley the Black stays clear of trouble.",sec={{t="A Scoundrel's Debt",b="Wiley the Black keeps to the Lakeshire Inn, far from Westfall's turmoil and Redridge's gnoll-infested borders. Gryan Stoutmantle, commander of the People's Militia, once saved his life. Stoutmantle grumbles that he should have let Wiley rot. So when the militia needs insight into the Defias conspiracy, it turns to Wiley. Reluctantly, he shares covert intelligence to repay his debt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wiley the Black?",a="Wiley the Black is inside the Lakeshire Inn in Lakeshire, a town in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"wiley location","where is wiley the black","wiley redridge","lakeshire inn wiley"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Wiley helping Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle once saved Wiley's life. Wiley repays that debt with information about the Defias Brotherhood, though he is reluctant to risk himself.",al={"why help gryan","wiley gryan relationship","wiley stoutmantle debt"},it="motive"},{q="How does Wiley know about the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Wiley knows the underworld and Defias operations well. He shares what he knows to repay Gryan Stoutmantle, though whether he once belonged to the Brotherhood is unconfirmed.",al={"is wiley defias","how does wiley know defias","wiley defias connection"},it="ties"},{q="What role does he play in the Defias investigation?",a="When the People's Militia captures clues to a larger conspiracy, Stoutmantle sends adventurers to Lakeshire with a message for Wiley. Wiley examines the situation and writes a note directing the militia toward the rebellion's leaders.",al={"wiley quest role","what does wiley do","defias brotherhood wiley"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Wiley the Black?",a="Wiley the Black is a shady rogue currently residing at the inn in Lakeshire. Known as a scoundrel with illicit connections, he possesses surprisingly deep inside knowledge regarding the Defias Brotherhood and their covert operations across the human kingdoms.",al={"who is wiley","wiley the black lore","about wiley the black"},it="identity",add="03fe7b6d"},{q="Whose side is Wiley the Black on?",a="Wiley looks out primarily for himself, keeping his distance from formal Alliance politics. However, because Gryan Stoutmantle once saved his life, Wiley is willing to settle his personal debt by aiding the People's Militia against the Defias.",al={"is wiley loyal to the alliance","wiley the black faction","wiley the black allegiance"},it="side",add="7107b7b4"},{q="What does Wiley the Black want?",a="Wiley wants to clear his ledger with Gryan Stoutmantle and keep out of trouble. Providing critical intelligence on the Defias Brotherhood fulfills his obligation to Gryan, allowing him to settle his debt while keeping a safe distance from Westfall's fighting.",al={"what does wiley want","wiley the black goals","why is wiley helping"},it="wants",add="72fbb4af"},{q="Why is Wiley the Black in Redridge?",a="Wiley has taken up lodging upstairs at the Lakeshire Inn, far away from Westfall and the direct reach of Stormwind's authorities. Staying in Redridge allows him to maintain a low profile while keeping an ear to the ground.",al={"why is wiley in lakeshire","why is wiley here","wiley in redridge"},it="why_here",add="9b688ede"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Wiley shows how tradecraft and intelligence can keep someone alive. He knows when to trade information and whom to repay.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Stormwind's army absent, the Alliance relies on unofficial contacts like Wiley to piece together the rebellion in Westfall."},kw={"defias","gryan stoutmantle","informant","lakeshire","redridge","wiley","wiley the black"},rel={"quest:65","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","zone:westfall"},src={"Wiley the Black"}}
E["quest:102"] = {t="quest",n="Patrolling Westfall",z="westfall",s="Gnoll packs threaten the people still living on Westfall’s grasslands. From Sentinel Hill, Captain Danuvin calls on volunteers to hunt them, fearing they work with thieves in the Deadmines.",h="Gnoll packs threaten the people still living on Westfall’s grasslands.",sec={{t="Abandoned by the Crown",b="Sentinel Hill is Westfall’s main defense, held by local volunteers instead of royal troops. With Stormwind sending no soldiers to protect the outer farmlands, the people formed the People’s Militia. Captain Danuvin once farmed in Westfall. Now he leads the militia and refuses to abandon his homeland.\n\nThe militia depends on travelers passing through to help hold its perimeter against dangers gathering across the plains.",sp=0},{t="The Scavengers of the Grasslands",b="Gnolls threaten the refugees and squatters struggling to survive in Westfall. Danuvin’s scouts believe the packs work with bandits based in the Deadmines. So he sends hunters to collect gnoll paws. He hopes to curb the packs’ growing patrols and break any cooperation between the beasts and the outlaws.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Danuvin?",a="Captain Danuvin commands the volunteer defenders at Sentinel Hill. Once a farmer in Westfall, he took the lead when Stormwind withdrew its support and refuses to abandon the people who remain.",al={"captain danuvin","who is danuvin","quest giver sentinel hill"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the People's Militia fighting gnolls instead of Stormwind soldiers?",a="Stormwind’s House of Nobles has largely ignored Westfall’s plight, leaving the region without royal soldiers. Displaced farmers and laborers formed the People’s Militia to defend their land from bandits and wild beasts.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are stormwind guards","why militia"},it="why_me"},{q="Are the gnolls in Westfall organized?",a="Gnolls are usually chaotic scavengers, but Captain Danuvin sees signs that Westfall’s packs coordinate with thieves based in the Deadmines. They may guard the criminals’ outer reaches.",al={"are gnolls working with defias","gnoll alliance","deadmines thieves gnolls"}},{q="Why does Captain Danuvin ask for gnoll paws?",a="Captain Danuvin asks for gnoll paws as proof that the beasts have been killed and removed from the grasslands.",al={"why gnoll paws","paw bounty","proof of kills"},it="item"},{q="Where are the gnolls typically found?",a="Gnoll hunting parties and camps lie across Westfall’s central and southern plains. They roam open fields around abandoned homesteads and near the hillsides.",al={"gnoll locations","where to find gnolls westfall"},gp=true},{q="What happens once the gnoll threat is pushed back?",a="The People’s Militia hopes that thinning the gnoll and outlaw ranks will let people reclaim the plains and restore the breadbasket that once fed the kingdom.",al={"what next westfall","militia goal","breadbasket of stormwind"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Captain Danuvin want you to patrol Westfall?",a="Captain Danuvin refuses to abandon his homeland. Stormwind's crown has turned its back on Westfall, leaving its remaining farmers and residents vulnerable to rampant lawlessness. Danuvin and the People's Militia are determined to reclaim the region and restore it to the fertile breadbasket it once was, but they cannot secure the plains while gnolls roam unchecked and harass the locals.",al={"why patrol westfall","danuvin motive","why kill gnolls westfall"},it="motive",add="939494a1"},{q="Why are the gnolls in Westfall?",a="The gnolls prowling the grasslands appear to be working in coordination with the thieves entrenched in the Deadmines. Taking advantage of the kingdom's military withdrawal, these marauders terrorize the local farms and collaborate with the bandits to keep Sentinel Hill and the remaining populace besieged and divided.",al={"who are the gnolls","why are gnolls here","westfall gnolls deadmines"},it="target",add="91e73c26"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Westfall’s struggling rural people stand at odds with the aristocracy in Stormwind Keep, which has turned away from their plight.",["race:Human"]="As a human, seeing Westfall’s golden fields overrun by gnolls shows how fragile the kingdom’s recovery remains after the recent wars."},kw={"danuvin","deadmines","gnolls","paws","peoples militia","sentinel hill","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:captain-danuvin","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:12","topic:gnoll","zone:deadmines","topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:deadmines"},m={start="Captain Danuvin",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=102,ri={"Gnoll Paw"}},src={"Patrolling Westfall"}}
E["quest:103"] = {t="quest",n="Keeper of the Flame",z="westfall",s="At Westfall Lighthouse, Captain Grayson keeps watch over the coast. He seeks oil to keep the beacon burning after murlocs killed the living keepers, guiding ships safely past the reefs.",h="At Westfall Lighthouse, Captain Grayson keeps watch over the coast.",sec={{t="A Spectral Duty",b="Westfall Lighthouse stands on a rocky islet off Westfall’s southwest shore. Its light once guided sailors through the Great Sea’s shallow waters. That duty ended when Old Murk-Eye led a murloc attack and killed the keeper and his family. Captain Grayson died in the waters by these rocks and now watches over the tower as a ghost. He could not stop the slaughter in life, but he will not let the lighthouse go dark.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Beacon",b="No living keeper remains to tend the flame, so Captain Grayson needs an unusual fuel. Harvest Watchers roam Westfall’s abandoned farmlands, carrying flasks of machinery oil inside their rusted bodies. Grayson sends you ashore to recover the oil from these broken constructs. With it, the beacon can keep burning and guide captains past the reefs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Grayson?",a="Captain Grayson is the ghost of a sailor who shipwrecked and died on Westfall’s dangerous coast. He watches over Westfall Lighthouse to help keep living sailors from meeting the same fate.",al={"captain grayson","lighthouse ghost","who is the ghost at westfall lighthouse"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the original lighthouse keepers?",a="Old Murk-Eye led the murloc attack that killed the lighthouse keeper and his family. Captain Grayson watched helplessly as a ghost.",al={"what happened to lighthouse keeper","who killed the lighthouse keeper","keeper family dead"},it="history"},{q="Where does the oil for the lighthouse flame come from?",a="Harvest Watchers roaming Westfall’s abandoned farms and fields carry the oil for the lighthouse.",al={"where to get oil","harvest monster oil","flask of oil"},it="item"},{q="Why does Grayson care about keeping the beacon lit?",a="Grayson wants the beacon to guide sailors across the Great Sea and past the coastal rocks. He died on those reefs and now watches over the lighthouse.",al={"why light the torch","grayson motivation","lighthouse flame purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is a notorious murloc who prowls Westfall’s coast and leads attacks on shore settlements. His raiders killed the lighthouse keeper and his family.",al={"old murk-eye","murk eye","murloc leader westfall"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the Westfall Lighthouse located?",a="Westfall Lighthouse stands on a rocky islet off Westfall’s southwestern coast. You can reach it by swimming through the shallow coastal waters.",al={"lighthouse location","where is westfall lighthouse","find lighthouse"},it="place"},{q="Why are Harvest Monsters the source of the lighthouse oil?",a="The mechanical Harvest Monsters that roam the abandoned fields of Westfall run on flasks of heavy machinery oil. With the lighthouse keeper's family dead and normal supply lines cut off, Captain Grayson must rely on whatever fuel can be salvaged from these rogue automatons to keep the beacon's signal fire burning.",al={"harvest monsters oil","why harvest golems oil","harvest monsters target"},it="target",add="44c879dd"},{q="Why does Captain Grayson need your help instead of gathering the oil himself?",a="Captain Grayson is a restless ghost bound to the immediate vicinity of the Westfall Lighthouse. Because his spirit cannot travel inland to hunt down the malfunctioning Harvest Monsters himself, he must rely on passing adventurers to venture into the fields and harvest the fuel necessary to maintain the beacon.",al={"why does grayson need me","why cant grayson get oil","why me grayson"},it="why_me",add="cbe3424a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Westfall beacon helps keep trade ships and naval vessels bound for Stormwind Harbor from running aground along the kingdom’s crumbling coast.",["profession:Engineering"]="Harvest Watchers roaming Westfall’s farms carry volatile machine fluids that can fuel a lantern."},kw={"beacon","captain grayson","flask of oil","great sea","harvest monsters","old murk-eye","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"npc:captain-grayson","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","zone:westfall"},m={start="Captain Grayson",level="16",id=103,ri={"Flask of Oil"}},src={"Keeper of the Flame (Classic)"}}
E["quest:104"] = {t="quest",n="The Coastal Menace",z="westfall",s="On Westfall's rocky shore, Captain Grayson's ghost calls travelers to face The Coastal Menace. His ship broke on the rocks after murlocs drove the lighthouse keeper's family from their post. The family returned, but Old Murk-Eye led another attack and killed them. Now Grayson seeks the chieftain's death and justice for the shore.",h="On Westfall's rocky shore, Captain Grayson's ghost calls travelers to face The Coastal Menace.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Dark",b="The Westfall Lighthouse once guided ships through the jagged shallows along the southern coast. After murlocs frightened the lighthouse keeper's family from their post, Captain Grayson's ship struck the rocks in the dark. The family returned and lit the flame again, but danger still stalked the shore.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of the Coast",b="Old Murk-Eye rallied the weaker-minded murlocs along the coast and led them against the lighthouse. In that second attack, the keeper's family died while Captain Grayson watched, helpless. Now the ghostly captain calls for Murk-Eye's death and asks for a scale as proof. He hopes to bring peace to the dead and protect sailors on the Great Sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is a cunning murloc chieftain who prowls Westfall's southern coast. He rallies other murlocs and leads attacks on human settlements along the shore.",al={"murk-eye","murk eye","who is murk eye","who is the coastal menace"},it="target"},{q="Why does Captain Grayson want Old Murk-Eye dead?",a="Captain Grayson wants Old Murk-Eye dead because murlocs drove the lighthouse keeper's family from their post. With the shore dark, Grayson's ship struck the rocks. Later, Grayson watched Murk-Eye lead a second attack that killed the returned keeper and his family.",al={"grayson grudge","why kill murk eye","grayson backstory"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Old Murk-Eye be found?",a="Old Murk-Eye prowls Westfall's open beaches and shallows near the Westfall Lighthouse and nearby murloc encampments.",al={"murk-eye location","where is murk eye","find murk eye"},gp=true},{q="What proof does Grayson ask for?",a="Captain Grayson asks for one scale from Old Murk-Eye as proof that the chieftain is dead.",al={"proof of death","scale of murk eye","quest turn in"},it="item"},{q="Who was Captain Grayson in life?",a="Captain Grayson was a sea captain whose ship struck the rocks below the Westfall Lighthouse. His spirit remains near the shore, seeking retribution against the murlocs and safer waters for passing vessels.",al={"captain grayson","ghost at the lighthouse","lighthouse ghost"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the lighthouse keeper's family?",a="The lighthouse keeper's family first fled after Old Murk-Eye harassed the tower. They returned to relight the lantern, but Murk-Eye led a second attack that killed the whole family.",al={"keeper family","who lived at lighthouse","lighthouse massacre"},it="history"},{q="Why does Captain Grayson need you to kill Old Murk-Eye?",a="Captain Grayson is a ghost, bound to the rocky coast where his ship shattered upon the shoals. Incorporeal and powerless to physically avenge the keeper's slaughtered family or bring justice to the shores, he cannot strike down the murloc leader himself. Moreover, Westfall lacks any organized military or guard force along its southwestern beaches, leaving the duty entirely in the hands of traveling adventurers.",al={"why cant grayson kill murk eye","why does grayson need me","why grayson need help"},it="why_me",add="871c093a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Westfall's coastal waters carry vital shipping for Stormwind. Driving away leaders like Old Murk-Eye helps keep the southern sea routes safe from sabotage.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know the lighthouse keeper's family's murder as a grim chapter in Westfall's loss of safety. Their deaths give you another reason to avenge your fellow citizens."},kw={"captain grayson","coastal menace","great sea","murloc","old murk-eye","scale of old murk-eye","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"npc:captain-grayson","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","zone:westfall","topic:murloc"},m={start="Captain Grayson",level="20",id=104,ri={"Scale of Old Murk-Eye"}},src={"The Coastal Menace (Classic)"}}
E["quest:109"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Gryan Stoutmantle",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle gathers Westfall's defenders against threats to the farms.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle gathers Westfall's defenders against threats to the farms.",sec={{t="A Plea Across the River",b="Guards along the Elwynn border and farmers driven west both send capable travelers toward Sentinel Hill. Those who answer join a defense built from local volunteers. No royal battalions come to their aid.",sp=0},{t="Sentinel Hill and the Militia",b="From the stone tower atop Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle organizes farmers, retired veterans, and mercenaries into the People's Militia. You join their bitter guerrilla war to keep Westfall's farmlands from falling into lawlessness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran fighter who commands the People's Militia. From the tower atop Sentinel Hill, he organizes Westfall's defenses and gathers fighters to protect its farmers from bandits and beasts.",al={"gryan stoutmantle","who is stoutmantle","sentinel hill leader"},it="target"},{q="Why is the People's Militia needed?",a="The People's Militia is needed because the Stormwind army has turned its attention to the capital, leaving Westfall with little support from the crown. Residents formed the militia to defend themselves from bandits, rogue harvest automatons, and marauding Riverpaw gnolls.",al={"why militia","why no stormwind army","why is westfall abandoned"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Sentinel Hill located?",a="Sentinel Hill lies near the center of Westfall, along the main road. Its sturdy stone watchtower and fortified camp are gathering places for the People's Militia.",al={"find sentinel hill","sentinel hill location","where to find stoutmantle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends adventurers on this assignment?",a="Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, border guards such as Guard Thomas and Deputy Rainer, and displaced farmers such as Farmer Furlbrow and Farmer Saldean send capable fighters to Gryan.",al={"who gives quest","quest givers","report to gryan quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after reporting to Gryan?",a="When you report to Stoutmantle, he puts your fighting skill to work for the People's Militia. Your first assignments target the Defias brigands and gnolls threatening Westfall.",al={"what next","stoutmantle follow up","militia quest chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Westfall technically still part of the Alliance?",a="Yes. Westfall remains Alliance territory under the nominal authority of the Stormwind Kingdom. The crown's garrison neglects the province, leaving armed citizens to defend it.",al={"is westfall alliance","does stormwind own westfall"},it="ties"},{q="Why are you asked to report to Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="With Stormwind focusing its military inward and largely abandoning Westfall to bandits and scavengers, the folk holding the line there are stretched thin. Gryan Stoutmantle and his People's Militia desperately need experienced fighters to defend what remains of the farmlands. Those sending you from Elwynn recognize that your combat prowess is sorely wasted patrolling peaceful orchards when neighboring Westfall is sliding entirely into chaos.",al={"why report to stoutmantle","why westfall","dughan westfall stoutmantle why"},it="motive",add="a1beb42d"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need independent adventurers rather than Stormwind guards?",a="The Stormwind monarchy has refused to send regular army reinforcements to Westfall, leaving the province effectively forsaken by the crown. The local guards and militia cannot cope with the sheer volume of banditry, gnolls, and outlaws overtaking the farms. Gryan Stoutmantle must rely on capable traveling mercenaries and adventurers like you who have demonstrated real combat experience and are willing to take up arms for their cause.",al={"why me westfall","why adventurers instead of army","why peoples militia need help"},it="why_me",add="e97846b7"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you see the divide between Stormwind City's safe marble streets and the harsh, neglected farmlands beyond.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see ordinary citizens forming militias to survive while the royal court argues over politics in Stormwind.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you bring the seasoned discipline Gryan Stoutmantle values, making you an important fighter for the outnumbered People's Militia."},kw={"defias","elwynn","gryan stoutmantle","marshal dughan","people's militia","sentinel hill","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:12","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan,Guard Thomas,Deputy Rainer,Farmer Furlbrow, orFarmer Saldean",["end"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=109},src={"Report to Gryan Stoutmantle"}}
E["quest:117"] = {t="quest",n="Thunderbrew",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Grimbooze Thunderbrew gathers fresh hops for his next batch. Without them, his ale may turn thick as stew, so he shares kegs with those who bring what he needs.",h="In Westfall, Grimbooze Thunderbrew gathers fresh hops for his next batch.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Passion in Westfall",b="Far from Dun Morogh, Grimbooze keeps his family's brewing tradition alive. He insists on proper hops for his current brew, or it may turn to thick stew instead of refreshing ale.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Keg",b="Grimbooze praises hops, barley, yeast, and malt in cheerful rhymes. Fresh hops let him finish fermentation on the spot. In return, he shares whole kegs of Thunderbrew Lager, known for its forceful taste.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grimbooze Thunderbrew?",a="Grimbooze Thunderbrew is a dwarven brewer who roams Westfall. Wherever he camps, he keeps his clan's brewing tradition alive and chants in cheerful rhymes.",al={"grimbooze","who is grimbooze","grimbooze lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Grimbooze need hops?",a="Without fresh hops, Grimbooze's latest batch may turn thick and heavy like stew instead of crisp lager. Hops bring bitterness and balance to the brew.",al={"why hops","grimbooze hops","what are hops for"},it="motive"},{q="What is Thunderbrew Lager?",a="Thunderbrew Lager is a potent dwarven drink made by the Thunderbrew family. Grimbooze shares it by the keg, and its strong taste hits the palate hard.",al={"thunderbrew beer","keg of thunderbrew","what is thunderbrew"},it="item"},{q="Can you bring Grimbooze hops more than once?",a="Yes. Grimbooze welcomes more hops and offers more kegs of his brew in return.",al={"repeatable quest","is thunderbrew repeatable","more kegs"},gp=true},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The work takes place in Westfall, where Grimbooze camps and gathers supplies among the farmlands.",al={"thunderbrew location","where is grimbooze","quest zone"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Grimbooze related to the Thunderbrews in Dun Morogh?",a="Yes. Grimbooze shares his surname and brewing trade with the Thunderbrew family of Kharanos in Dun Morogh.",al={"thunderbrew distillery","grimbooze clan","thunderbrew family"},it="ties"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may welcome seeing a kinsman keep Kharanos's brewing traditions alive on Westfall's rugged frontier, especially when kegs are involved.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know barley, malt, and hops must balance, much like the ingredients in classic dwarven brewing."},kw={"beer","brewing","dwarf","grimbooze","hops","keg","lager","thunderbrew","westfall"},rel={"npc:grimbooze-thunderbrew","zone:westfall"},m={start="Grimbooze Thunderbrew",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=117,ri={"Hops"}},src={"Thunderbrew (quest)"}}
E["quest:12"] = {t="quest",n="The People's Militia",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle puts the People's Militia to the test against outlaws in Westfall's northern fields and mines. Local volunteers defend the region from the Defias Brotherhood while Stormwind's throne is distracted and its army absent.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle puts the People's Militia to the test against outlaws in Westfall's...",sec={{t="The Price of Peace",b="Gryan Stoutmantle founded the People's Militia, and he does not take just anyone. Anyone seeking its badge must prove they can fight and protect innocent settlers. He calls for decisive action to reclaim Westfall from the outlaws, vagrants, and thieves overrunning the region.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Breadbasket",b="Before Gryan Stoutmantle trusts new recruits with deeper operations, he sends them against Defias forces near the northern homesteads. Defias Trappers and Smugglers work openly near Jangolode Mine, Molsen Farm, and Furlbrow's Pumpkin Patch. They pillage stores and ambush travelers. Driving them out disrupts their foraging and shows Stoutmantle's scouts you have the grit for a long fight against crime.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer army organized by Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill. Local farmers, veterans, and commoners formed its ranks to defend Westfall from the Defias Brotherhood while Stormwind's royal army has refused or failed to garrison the region.",al={"peoples militia","who are the militia","what is peoples militia"},it="people"},{q="Why isn't Stormwind sending its royal army?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, Stormwind's noble House of Nobles and council leadership have focused the kingdom's resources elsewhere. Outlying rural territories like Westfall are left to fend for themselves against rising outlaw bands.",al={"where is the army","why no guards in westfall","stormwind garrison"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can I find Defias Trappers and Smugglers?",a="Defias Trappers and Smugglers work across northern Westfall, especially around Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm, Molsen Farm, and the entrance to Jangolode Mine.",al={"trapper location","smuggler location","where are trappers"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a seasoned veteran who commands the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill. He rallies volunteers to defend Westfall's settlers, drive out the Defias Brotherhood, and restore order to the countryside.",al={"who is stoutmantle","gryan stoutmantle lore","militia leader"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest lead to more militia assignments?",a="Yes. This opening trial leads to further duties for successful volunteers, who take on increasingly dangerous ranks of the Defias Brotherhood across Westfall's plains.",al={"is this a chain","next quest","militia progression"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is happening at Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm?",a="The Defias Brotherhood drove the Furlbrows from their homestead and took control of their farmland. Outlaws and scavengers now pillage the fields and terrorize the northern roads.",al={"furlbrow farm","what happened to furlbrows","pumpkin farm"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want this done?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia with a single goal: defending Westfall and reclaiming peace from the criminal syndicate overrunning its farmlands. Bands of Defias outlaws are pillaging homesteads like the Molsen and Furlbrow farms. By clearing out their trappers and smugglers, Gryan aims to push back their encroaching presence and test whether you have the resolve to fight for Westfall's people.",al={"why kill trappers and smugglers","gryan stoutmantle motive","purpose of the people's militia quest"},it="motive",add="b0313ac5"},{q="Who are the Defias Trappers and Smugglers?",a="They are early rank-and-file operatives of the Defias Brotherhood, a ruthless syndicate of thieves and outlaws who have driven the farmers from their lands. The trappers and smugglers lurk around seized estates like the Molsen Farm and Jangolode Mine, securing territory and stockpiling illicit goods to support the Brotherhood's stranglehold over the countryside.",al={"defias trappers","defias smugglers","who are the defias outlaws"},it="target",add="1cf2b131"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need you to fight the Defias?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer force stretched to its breaking point, completely abandoned by Stormwind's royal army. Gryan cannot afford to send his few remaining defenders on risky skirmishes without thinning the guard on Sentinel Hill. He relies on capable volunteers and mercenaries, asking you to prove your worth and dedication before formally welcoming you into the militia's ranks.",al={"why doesn't the militia fight them","why me gryan","why enlist outsiders"},it="why_me",add="b416da40"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you see the kingdom's divide: Stormwind's nobility stays behind the capital's walls while common settlers defend Westfall from ruin.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you see working families and generations of farmers suffer under bandit attacks while royal authorities look away.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you protect the defenseless and bring judgment to outlaws who prey on the vulnerable."},kw={"defias smuggler","defias trapper","furlbrow","gryan stoutmantle","jangolode","molsen farm","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:jangolode-mine","subzone:furlbrow-s-pumpkin-farm","subzone:molsen-farm","topic:light"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=12,ri={"Defias Smuggler","Defias Trapper"}},src={"The People's Militia (quest)"}}
E["quest:13"] = {t="quest",n="The People's Militia",z="westfall",s="Westfall's volunteers face a growing Defias threat. Led by Gryan Stoutmantle, The People's Militia now confronts thieves who have moved beyond highway robbery to ransack Moonbrook and the Gold Coast Quarry. The Militia calls for harsher retaliation.",h="Westfall's volunteers face a growing Defias threat.",sec={{t="Escalating Violence",b="Defias attacks have spread from the roads to Westfall's economic centers. Defias Looters and Pillagers, who hurl fire, occupy Moonbrook and the Gold Coast Quarry. They strip the Alexston Farmstead as well. Gryan Stoutmantle sees what their hold on these places could mean: Westfall may become impossible to reclaim without a formal royal army.",sp=0},{t="The Militia's Philosophy",b="Stormwind has sent Gryan Stoutmantle neither soldiers nor supplies. So he calls on the Holy Light and the resolve of Westfall's remaining farmers. Volunteers carry the fight into Defias strongholds, wearing down the Brotherhood. Driving out the looters will deny them resources and show fearful residents that defenders still fight for Westfall's peace and prosperity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle organized the People's Militia as an armed volunteer force to defend Westfall. Its ranks draw largely from displaced Westfall farmers and sympathetic travelers. They formed to resist the Defias Brotherhood after Stormwind's royal court refused to send city guards.",al={"peoples militia","who are the militia","westfall militia"},it="people"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran human commander who leads Westfall's defense from the redoubt atop Sentinel Hill. Dedicated to the Light and his home, he directs the People's Militia's desperate resistance to outlaw control.",al={"gryan","who is stoutmantle","stoutmantle lore"},it="leader"},{q="Why are the Defias looting farms and quarries?",a="The Defias Brotherhood seeks to cripple Westfall's food supply and seize raw materials. By taking the Gold Coast Quarry, they control stone and minerals. Capturing Moonbrook and farmsteads drives off honest folk and gives them bases for their criminal enterprise.",al={"why defias looting","defias in moonbrook","why pillagers at quarry"},it="conflict"},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind sent soldiers to Westfall?",a="Stormwind has sent no soldiers because King Varian Wrynn has mysteriously vanished. The boy-king Anduin sits on the throne under Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's regency. Gridlock in the noble House of Nobles stretches crown resources thin, leaving outlying territories like Westfall to local defenders.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why no help from stormwind","king varian westfall"},it="why_here"},{q="Where are Defias Pillagers and Looters found?",a="Defias Pillagers and Looters gather around captured settlements in southern and western Westfall. They are found in the abandoned town of Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry along the western bluffs, and the ruined Alexston Farmstead.",al={"pillager location","where are looters","defias locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want the Defias Pillagers and Looters killed?",a="Defias Pillagers and Looters are actively raiding Westfall's remaining homesteads and vital resources, including Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Alexston Farmstead. Gryan Stoutmantle refuses to let the thieves rob the local families of what little peace and livelihood they have left. By cutting down their raiding parties, he hopes to blunt their momentum, protect the surviving settlers, and send an undeniable message that lawlessness and corruption will be met with force.",al={"why kill defias pillagers","gryan stoutmantle motive","why does gryan want pillagers dead"},it="motive",add="3f9873c1"},{q="Who are the Defias Pillagers and Looters targeted in this task?",a="They are the rank-and-file raiders and sorcerers of the Defias Brotherhood, dispatched to strip Westfall bare. While basic cutpurses roam the open fields, these pillagers and looters strike directly at established settlements like Moonbrook and the Gold Coast Quarry. Armed with weapons and destructive fire magic, they gather supplies, plunder abandoned holdings, and violently drive away any homesteaders who attempt to stand in their way.",al={"who are defias pillagers","who are defias looters","defias targets westfall"},it="target",add="599e05d4"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need your help instead of relying on the Militia?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its breaking point. With Stormwind refusing to provide military support, Sentinel Hill has only a handful of volunteers, farmers, and retired veterans to guard the road and hold their fortified hill. They cannot spare soldiers to conduct sweeping counter-offensives across the entire region without leaving their base defenseless. Capable adventurers like you provide the offensive punch the Militia sorely lacks.",al={"why does gryan need me","why not use the militia","why use adventurers"},it="why_me",add="7d97eb03"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you see the bitter divide between Stormwind City's comfortable walls and its starving borderlands, left entirely to their own devices.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you hear Gryan Stoutmantle call on the Light to purge Westfall of criminal corruption. This campaign is a direct mission of justice for you.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face a tragic struggle against former stonemasons and neighbors who have turned violently against their own people."},kw={"alexston farmstead","defias looter","defias pillager","gold coast quarry","gryan stoutmantle","moonbrook","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:12","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:gold-coast-quarry","subzone:alexston-farmstead","topic:light"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=13,ri={"Defias Looter","Defias Pillager"}},src={"The People's Militia (2)"}}
E["quest:132"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="At the edges of Redridge and Westfall, Wiley the Black warns Gryan Stoutmantle. His intelligence shows the Defias threat reaches beyond banditry, and Gryan needs to learn how far it extends.",h="At the edges of Redridge and Westfall, Wiley the Black warns Gryan Stoutmantle.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Dispatch",b="Wiley the Black says sharing what he knows could cost him his life. His sealed note describes how the Brotherhood has coordinated groups across the countryside, though those groups are usually hostile to one another.",sp=0},{t="Unlikely Alliances",b="Wiley warns that the Defias has drawn an alarming network around itself. The red-masked outlaws have enlisted gnoll packs, kobold diggers, and goblin engineers instead of working alone. Their brutal muscle, burrowing labor, and mechanical cunning point to an enterprise beyond what the People's Militia first expected.",sp=0},{t="Stoutmantle's Uneasy Reliance",b="Gryan Stoutmantle has little love for Wiley. He openly laments that he did not leave the rogue to rot when he had the chance. Yet Westfall cannot afford pride. The People's Militia must take useful intelligence wherever it can find it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Wiley's Note about?",a="Wiley the Black's note warns that the Defias Brotherhood is coordinating with gnolls, kobolds, and goblin engineers. It tells the People's Militia that the outlaws are preparing an operation far beyond petty banditry.",al={"wiley note","what is in the note","wiley the black note"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wiley the Black?",a="Wiley the Black is a shady contact stationed at Lakeshire in Redridge. Gryan Stoutmantle sees him as an untrustworthy scoundrel, but Wiley has extensive ties to the criminal underworld and critical information on Defias activity.",al={"who is wiley","wiley the black lore","wiley lakeshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why would the Defias ally with gnolls and kobolds?",a="The Defias uses local creatures to control territory and provide cheap labor. Gnolls serve as brutish skirmishers to distract defenders, kobolds tunnel in regional mines, and goblin tinkers contribute heavy machinery and demolition tools.",al={"why defias use gnolls","kobolds and defias","defias allies"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle dislike Wiley?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a disciplined former soldier who sees Wiley as a common cutpurse and criminal. He regrets sparing Wiley from prison, though Wiley's underworld ears are indispensable.",al={"stoutmantle and wiley","why hate wiley"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this message fit into the militia's investigation?",a="Wiley's message carries the militia's investigation from local reconnaissance toward the deeper Defias conspiracy. Its return prompts Stoutmantle to probe the conspiracy's leadership and staging grounds.",al={"defias chain step","what quest is this"},it="next_step"},{q="Why isn't Stormwind handling this threat?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the Stormwind House of Nobles refuses to divert royal soldiers or funding to defend Westfall. Stoutmantle's ragtag People's Militia is left to defend the region.",al={"stormwind help westfall","where are the guards"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Wiley the Black send you to Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Wiley knows that the Defias Brotherhood is plotting something catastrophic, having pieced together rumors that they are coordinating with gnolls, kobolds, and goblins. He is well aware that possessing such dangerous secrets puts his own life on the line. By putting his knowledge into a sealed message for Gryan Stoutmantle, Wiley passes the burden of action to the People's Militia, doing his part to thwart the conspiracy while staying safely out of the crosshairs.",al={"why does wiley help","wiley the black motive","why send wiley note"},it="motive",add="3bfb9fad"},{q="Why does Wiley rely on you instead of delivering the note himself?",a="Wiley is a criminal rogue keeping a low profile at the Lakeshire tavern, far from the watchful eyes of both the authorities and the Defias. Walking all the way through hostile territory to Westfall would place him in severe danger, and his past history with Gryan Stoutmantle makes him a despised figure rather than a welcome guest. You provide an able courier who can slip through the wilderness unnoticed and deliver the warning directly to Sentinel Hill.",al={"why wiley needs you","why cant wiley go to westfall","why me wiley note"},it="why_me",add="6813809b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, coordination between human outlaws, gnolls, and goblins shows the severe security vacuum on Stormwind's western borders.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how Wiley the Black walks the line between outlaw and useful informant, and how underworld ties carry wartime intelligence.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know the note confirms that bandits pillaging family homesteads in Westfall and Redridge are carrying out a deliberate, coordinated campaign."},kw={"defias brotherhood","gnolls","goblins","gryan stoutmantle","kobolds","sentinel hill","westfall","wiley the black","wiley's note"},rel={"quest:65","npc:wiley-the-black","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","topic:gnoll","topic:kobold","topic:goblin"},m={start="Wiley the Black",["end"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=132},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (2)"}}
E["quest:135"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Gryan Stoutmantle suspects the Defias Brotherhood has ties to Stormwind's old Stonemasons Guild. He sends you there with Wiley's Note.",h="In Westfall, Gryan Stoutmantle suspects the Defias Brotherhood has ties to Stormwind's old Stonemasons Guild.",sec={{t="A Slip of the Tongue",b="Wiley's mention of the Stonemasons catches Gryan's attention. The guild rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War, but many believe it scattered or dissolved. If the Defias are linked to the guild, Westfall's rural insurgency may be more than a band of outlaws.",sp=0},{t="Old Town Secrets",b="Gryan cannot test his suspicions from Sentinel Hill, so he sends you to Master Mathias Shaw, head of Stormwind's covert intelligence wing, SI:7. Shaw works from the Barracks in Old Town, gathering whispers and secrets from across the realm. He may untangle the Defias Brotherhood's origins.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow Over the Crown",b="When you bring Wiley's Note to Master Mathias Shaw, he sees that Westfall's rebellion runs deeper than Gryan understands. It also carries greater political complexity. Its roots reach into Stormwind's turbulent past.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you to Stormwind?",a="Wiley's Note mentions the Stonemasons, leading Gryan Stoutmantle to suspect political intrigue behind the banditry. He sends you to Master Mathias Shaw to confirm the connection.",al={"why go to stormwind","why stormwind quest","stoutmantle stormwind errand"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Mathias Shaw?",a="Master Mathias Shaw leads SI:7, Stormwind's covert intelligence and espionage branch. He works from the Barracks in Old Town.",al={"who is shaw","mathias shaw role","si7 leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Mathias Shaw?",a="You find Master Mathias Shaw on the second floor of the SI:7 headquarters in the Barracks of Old Town, Stormwind City.",al={"where is shaw","shaw location","find mathias shaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the connection between the Defias and the Stonemasons?",a="The Stonemasons Guild rebuilt Stormwind after its destruction in the First War. Gryan Stoutmantle suspects Wiley's mention of the guild links it to the Defias, and Mathias Shaw may confirm or deny the connection.",al={"defias stonemasons","are defias stonemasons","stonemason connection"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What is Wiley's Note?",a="Wiley's Note comes from Wiley the Black, a scoundrel Gryan Stoutmantle has dealt with before. It warns that the Defias are plotting with gnolls, kobolds, and goblins. Wiley's mention of the Stonemasons may link the Defias Brotherhood to the former guild.",al={"wileys note","what is the note","note to shaw"},it="item"},{q="Does Highlord Bolvar or the boy-king know about this?",a="Covert state matters pass through Mathias Shaw and SI:7 before reaching Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the throne. Shaw says the matter may be more complex than Stoutmantle realizes.",al={"does the king know","does bolvar know","stormwind government knowledge"}},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you instead of a People's Militia soldier?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its breaking point just defending Sentinel Hill and the scattered farms of Westfall. Gryan Stoutmantle cannot afford to pull battle-ready defenders away from the front line to run messages back to the capital. Moreover, you are an outsider who already pieced together Wiley's clues, making you a trusted courier to carry sensitive inquiries directly to Stormwind's spymaster.",al={"why send me","why not militia","why stoutmantle needs you"},it="why_me",add="f764ce01"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="At SI:7 headquarters, you meet Mathias Shaw, grandmaster of Stormwind's rogues and spies. His work connects Westfall's local turmoil to wider tradecraft.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see Westfall's lawless frontier meet the bitter political scandals left unresolved after the rebuilding of your capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see fractures within the Alliance's primary kingdom. Some threats come from betrayed citizens, not monstrous outsiders."},kw={"brotherhood","defias","gryan stoutmantle","mathias shaw","old town","si:7","stonemasons","westfall","wiley's note"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","subzone:old-town","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:2300"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",["end"]="Master Mathias Shaw",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=135},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (3)"}}
E["quest:136"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure",z="westfall",s="Along Westfall's shore, Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure begins with a battered parchment map. It sends you searching for his personal footlocker, then onward toward his hidden plunder across the region.",h="Along Westfall's shore, Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure begins with a battered parchment map.",sec={{t="A Sailor's Last Bequest",b="Captain Sanders was an old seafarer who met a watery grave off Westfall's western coast. He left cryptic instructions so his hard-won fortune would not be lost to the Great Sea or taken by scavengers. You can retrace the trail he left behind. Shipwrecks and the restless spirits of drowned sailors mark the western shore.",sp=0},{t="The Rusty Anchor",b="A lone rusty anchor in the surf marks the first clue on Westfall's western coast. Near a wreck, half-buried in the sand, lies Captain Sanders' old footlocker, battered by the waves. Inside are seawater, sand, and a scurrying crab clutching the next piece of Sanders' puzzle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was an old sea captain whose map says he lies in a watery grave. He left the map and a series of clues leading to his hidden plunder.",al={"captain sanders lore","who is sanders","sanders backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the footlocker located?",a="The footlocker lies half-buried in the sand along Westfall's western coast, near a solitary rusty anchor by the shoreline.",al={"footlocker location","where is the rusty anchor","find sanders footlocker"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does the footlocker contain the captain's treasure?",a="The map leads you to a footlocker and the next clue in a longer treasure hunt.",al={"is treasure in the chest","what is in the footlocker","where is the gold"},sp=1},{q="How many clues are in Captain Sanders' treasure hunt?",a="The hunt has four steps across Westfall's coast and countryside. It begins with the map and ends with Captain Sanders' actual treasure chest on an island off the coast.",al={"how long is sanders quest","how many parts","sanders quest chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why did Captain Sanders bury his treasure in Westfall?",a="Captain Sanders' map never says why he chose Westfall. It says he expected to meet a watery grave and wanted whoever followed his clues to find his treasure. The clues are spread across the coast and the bluffs above it.",al={"why hide treasure","why westfall coast"}},{q="Can Horde players follow this treasure map?",a="Yes. Captain Sanders' map and clues are neutral, so any adventurer who reaches Westfall's coast can follow his trail.",al={"can horde do this","horde sanders quest","faction neutral treasure"},gp=true},{q="Why did Captain Sanders leave behind this treasure map?",a="Captain Sanders knew he was facing a watery grave, and he had no intention of letting his accumulated riches rot forgotten beneath the sea. He laid out a cryptic trail of clues for whoever had the cunning and grit to discover his parchment. By challenging ambitious travelers to seek out his old footlocker, he ensures his name and legacy endure long after his death.",al={"why sanders map","sanders motive treasure map","why leave treasure map"},it="motive",add="1a1a7b8a"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the value of following a dead sailor's map along a lawless coast. A pirate's treasure hunt suits scoundrels and privateers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, recovering a fortune from Westfall's wreck-strewn coast is a small victory amid the kingdom's frontier turmoil. Coastal murlocs menace the shore."},kw={"captain sanders","footlocker","hidden treasure","rusty anchor","shipwreck","treasure map","westfall coast"},rel={"zone:westfall"},m={start="Captain Sanders' Treasure Map",["end"]="Captain's Footlocker",level="16",faction="Neutral",id=136},src={"Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 1)"}}
E["quest:138"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure",z="westfall",s="Along Westfall's shore, Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure sends you inland. You leave the coast and follow the next mark in his scattered trail.",h="Along Westfall's shore, Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure sends you inland.",sec={{t="A Trail of Inland Riddles",b="Captain Sanders left riddles across the countryside instead of marking one cache by the beach. The solved cipher points beyond rocky bluffs toward Westfall's main roads.",sp=0},{t="Ruins Along the Road",b="Among the roadside ruins, an old chimney marks the next stop. A discarded, weathered barrel nearby holds another message, and the ruined farmstead gives Sanders a landmark for his trail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was a pirate captain who sailed along Westfall's coasts. He scattered clues and riddles across the region for anyone seeking his hidden wealth.",al={"captain sanders lore","who is sanders","sanders pirate"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this clue send you?",a="The clue sends you east from the western sea, up the bluffs and toward the road. Beside an old stone chimney in the ruins, a broken barrel holds the next piece of the puzzle.",al={"where do i go","clue location","chimney location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why did Sanders hide his treasure in pieces?",a="Sanders divided the directions among several riddles to keep rivals and the authorities from finding his hidden wealth. Only a persistent, resourceful seeker can follow the trail to its final cache.",al={"why clues","why the scavenger hunt"},it="motive"},{q="Is the treasure hunt dangerous to follow?",a="The clues are parchment and old containers, but Westfall's roads and fields bring danger. Wandering beasts, prowling gnolls, and hostile members of the Defias Brotherhood threaten travelers near abandoned homesteads.",al={"is it safe","westfall dangers"},it="threat"},{q="What kind of ruins is the barrel hidden near?",a="The barrel lies beside the crumbling stone chimney of a ruined building near the road. Many Westfall homesteads have been abandoned or demolished during recent years of turmoil.",al={"chimney ruins","which building"},it="place"},{q="Does this quest reveal the treasure itself?",a="No. This step reveals another clue. Sanders laid out several stages across the region before anyone can find the actual prize.",al={"is this the final chest","do i get loot now"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can use stealth and cunning to decipher pirate ciphers and search abandoned ruins for forgotten spoils.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can follow Sanders' trail along Westfall's lawless coast and untended inland roads. The local militia struggles against organized outlaws."},kw={"broken barrel","captain sanders","chimney","pirate","sanders treasure","treasure hunt","westfall"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},m={start="Captain's Footlocker",["end"]="Broken Barrel",level="16",faction="Neutral",id=138},src={"Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 2)"}}
E["quest:139"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure",z="westfall",s="A broken barrel on Westfall's western shore begins Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure trail. Its clue points north to an old jug beside a coastal windmill, one step closer to the late pirate's riches.",h="A broken barrel on Westfall's western shore begins Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure trail.",sec={{t="A Pirate's Breadcrumb Trail",b="Captain Sanders left clues that point only to the next hiding place. No single parchment shows where his plunder lies, so the trail stays unresolved until you find each message.",sp=0},{t="North Toward the Bluffs",b="The parchment sends you due north from the barrel to the sea cliffs. An isolated windmill stands on the bluffs, with another clue in an abandoned jug beside it. Murlocs and Defias scavengers roam the coast, making the way perilous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure?",a="Captain Sanders was a buccaneer who hid his riches along the Westfall coast. Instead of a map, he left written riddles in barrels, chests, and jugs across the countryside.",al={"sanders treasure","what is this quest","who is sanders"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this third clue lead?",a="The parchment points due north from the broken barrel to the ocean bluffs. Near a lone windmill, an old jug holds the next clue.",al={"where do i go","jug location","where is the windmill"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why did Sanders hide his directions in pieces?",a="Sanders split his directions to protect his treasure from mutinous crewmates and rival marauders. One clue alone would not reveal the whole route.",al={"why clues","why not a full map"},it="history"},{q="Can Horde players complete this trail?",a="Yes. Any adventurer can follow Captain Sanders' clues and handle the objects tied to his cache, though Westfall lies deep in Alliance territory.",al={"is this alliance only","horde sanders treasure"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Does this clue directly reveal the chest?",a="No. The jug near the coastal windmill holds another clue pointing to Sanders' chest. This is the penultimate step in the hunt.",al={"is the treasure in the jug","final step"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What dangers surround the trail to the windmill?",a="Riverpaw gnolls, coastal murlocs, and roving Defias bandits prowl Westfall's western bluffs and beaches. A straight march north can be treacherous.",al={"dangers on the bluffs","what mobs are there"},it="danger"},{q="Why is the clue hidden in a broken barrel?",a="The barrel itself has no living will or personal stakes—it is merely an inanimate drop point left behind along the coast of Westfall. Captain Sanders deliberately stashed his riddles in unassuming flotsam and abandoned debris to prevent casual looters and competing scoundrels from piecing together the full route to his chest.",al={"why broken barrel","why is the note in a barrel","sanders broken barrel"},it="motive",add="03354d32"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may find a scoundrel's trail of concealed messages and hidden markers along the bluffs familiar.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Westfall gripped by famine and Defias outlaws, Sanders' lost pirate plunder offers you a welcome windfall."},kw={"bluffs","broken barrel","captain sanders","hidden treasure","old jug","pirate clue","westfall","windmill"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},m={start="Broken Barrel",["end"]="Old Jug",level="16",faction="Neutral",id=139},src={"Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 3)"}}
E["quest:14"] = {t="quest",n="The People's Militia",z="westfall",s="In southern Westfall, volunteers of The People's Militia press their fight against the Defias. The seasoned brigands hold the Dagger Hills, and Gryan Stoutmantle leads a campaign to clear the roads and farms. Complete the patrols, and you earn full induction at Sentinel Hill.",h="In southern Westfall, volunteers of The People's Militia press their fight against the Defias.",sec={{t="Purging the Dagger Hills",b="The Defias Brotherhood has brought great hardship to Westfall's northern farmlands. Those who escaped Gryan Stoutmantle's first sweeps fled south to the rocky Dagger Hills. From there, Defias Highwaymen, Pathstalkers, and Knuckledusters still raid homesteads and waylay travelers. You join hardened recruits sent into the hills to break the brigands' hold over southern Westfall.",sp=0},{t="Stoutmantle's Crusade",b="After returning from the fight against the Scourge in Lordaeron, Gryan Stoutmantle found Westfall abandoned by Stormwind's royal garrison. A criminal syndicate went unchecked, and hunger drove farmers from their land. So he rallied local volunteers to take up arms. Complete this final patrol, and Stoutmantle blesses you in the Light as he formally inducts you into the militia. The fight against the Brotherhood deepens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dagger Hills?",a="The Dagger Hills lie in southern Westfall, southwest of Sentinel Hill. Their rugged ridges and abandoned mineheads give the Defias Brotherhood's tougher fighters ground to gather and hold.",al={"dagger hills location","where to find dagger hills","where are the highwaymen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the People's Militia fighting the Defias alone?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources stretched thin, Stormwind's House of Nobles refuses to send the royal army to protect rural Westfall. Gryan Stoutmantle and local farmers form their own volunteer force to defend their homes.",al={"why no stormwind guards","where is stormwind army","why is westfall abandoned"},it="why_me"},{q="What does completing this task achieve?",a="Clearing out the Highwaymen, Pathstalkers, and Knuckledusters breaks the Defias hold on southern Westfall's roads. You earn formal induction into the People's Militia under Gryan Stoutmantle's command.",al={"peoples militia completion","militia induction","what do i get for finishing"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran soldier who fought the Scourge in Lordaeron during the Third War. He returned to Westfall and saw that the Kingdom of Stormwind had abandoned its rural peasantry. At Sentinel Hill, he founded the People's Militia to fight the Defias.",al={"gryan background","who is stoutmantle","sentinel hill leader"},it="identity"},{q="What kind of Defias hide in the Dagger Hills?",a="The Dagger Hills shelter experienced Defias Highwaymen, deadly Pathstalkers, and brutal Knuckledusters. They lead raids across southern Westfall and guard the Brotherhood's deeper strongholds.",al={"defias mobs southern westfall","what are pathstalkers and knuckledusters","who is in dagger hills"},it="target"},{q="How does this connect to Lordaeron?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle says he recently returned from the tainted lands of Lordaeron, where the Alliance fought the Scourge. Surviving that grim fight gave him resolve to organize Westfall's defense after local authorities failed.",al={"stoutmantle lordaeron","tainted lands of lordaeron","gryan war history"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want these Defias slain?",a="Defias raiders have pushed deep into southern Westfall, pillaging farms and evading militia patrols. Gryan's scouts tracked them to the Dagger Hills, where they are actively gathering to plot their next strike. If they are not rooted out and broken now, the remaining homesteads in the south will fall completely under their sway.",al={"why kill defias dagger hills","gryan motive","why does gryan want them dead"},it="motive",add="12e61ece"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you stand up for forgotten countrymen whose livelihoods the capital's political elite abandoned.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you hear Stoutmantle call on the Light to bless new inductees. His words reflect the holy ideals of justice and protecting the defenseless from predatory outlaws.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind's failure to protect Westfall force common folk to shed their own blood to keep order in their homeland."},kw={"dagger hills","defias highwayman","defias knuckleduster","defias pathstalker","gryan stoutmantle","people's militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:dagger-hills","quest:12","zone:westfall","topic:lordaeron","topic:light"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=14,ri={"Defias Highwayman","Defias Knuckleduster","Defias Pathstalker"}},src={"The People's Militia (3)"}}
E["quest:140"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure",z="westfall",s="A whiskey-soaked clue sends you west from Westfall's shore and out across the Great Sea. Captain Sanders' trail ends at a remote islet, where his hidden prize waits.",h="A whiskey-soaked clue sends you west from Westfall's shore and out across the Great Sea.",sec={{t="A Sailor's Trail",b="Captain Sanders left clues along Westfall's coast for you to piece together. The last parchment came from the dregs of his favorite whiskey jug. It gives the final bearing: head west to the water's edge, then swim into the waves.",sp=0},{t="The Lonely Islet",b="Small rocky outcroppings rise from the Great Sea off Westfall. Swim due west to reach the isolated isle where Captain Sanders hid his prize. A locked chest waits there, its hinges rusted by years of salty surf. Force it open, and the buccaneer's trail ends.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the final clue lead?",a="The note inside the Old Jug sends you west to Westfall's shore, then out into the ocean. The chest waits on a small island.",al={"where is the chest","sanders treasure location","final clue destination"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who was Captain Sanders?",a="Captain Sanders was a buccaneer who sailed along Westfall. He left a riddle-filled trail of clues along the shoreline, leading to a chest on a remote island instead of a bank or stronghold.",al={"who is captain sanders","sanders lore","captain sanders background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the final clue smelling like whiskey?",a="Captain Sanders tucked the final instructions inside his discarded whiskey jug near the coast. Dampness and spirits made the ink run over time, but the directions remain legible.",al={"whiskey note","old jug clue"},it="item"},{q="How many steps are in this treasure hunt?",a="The hunt has four stages. It begins with a sea-battered map on the coast, then leads through a footlocker, a barrel, and a whiskey jug before ending at the island chest.",al={"how long is sanders chain","sanders quest parts","captain sanders questline"},gp=true},{q="Is the island dangerous to reach?",a="The main challenge is the long swim into the Great Sea. Westfall's coastal waters often hold aggressive murlocs and sea beasts, while the islet is where Sanders kept his cache.",al={"swimming to sanders chest","island danger","murlocs near chest"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What state is the treasure chest in?",a="Sea air and crashing surf have battered the chest. Its hinges are heavily rusted, but leverage can force it open to reach the goods inside.",al={"condition of chest","is the chest locked","rusty chest"},it="target"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Following a scoundrel's trail across deserted beaches and out to sea comes naturally to a rogue who values pirate contraband.",["race:Human"]="As a human defending Westfall from Defias brigands and gnolls, you may welcome a break from farm patrol as you track down a forgotten local pirate's stash."},kw={"captain sanders","final clue","hidden treasure","island","locked chest","old jug","treasure hunt","westfall"},rel={"quest:136","zone:westfall"},m={start="Old Jug",["end"]="Locked Chest",level="16",faction="Neutral",id=140},src={"Captain Sanders' Hidden Treasure (Classic 4)"}}
E["quest:141"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="From Stormwind, Mathias Shaw sends Gryan Stoutmantle a confidential report at Sentinel Hill. Shaw investigated the former Stonemasons Guild to help Stoutmantle uncover the Defias Brotherhood's origins.",h="From Stormwind, Mathias Shaw sends Gryan Stoutmantle a confidential report at Sentinel Hill.",sec={{t="A Builder Turned Bandit",b="For months, Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia have faced an uprising across Westfall with no clear face. Highwaymen, thieves, and cutthroats strike along roads and through the countryside. Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 studies Wiley's Note and pieces together the truth. The guild of architects and stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind's white ramparts never disbanded. Their leader, Edwin VanCleef, took them underground.",sp=1},{t="Bitterness and Betrayal",b="After the First War left Stormwind in ashes, VanCleef's Stonemasons' Guild set to work restoring the kingdom's capital. Their labor raised Stormwind into a jewel of humanity once more. When the work ended, a bitter dispute over compensation broke out. VanCleef and his artisans were dissatisfied with their treatment by the crown and the House of Nobles. So they took up daggers and red bandanas, leaving civic craft for violent rebellion against the throne.",sp=1},{t="Stoutmantle's Disbelief",b="Shaw's report reaches Sentinel Hill, and Gryan Stoutmantle struggles to accept what it says. He remembers VanCleef as an industrious, gifted artisan, not a cutthroat hiding in the countryside's shadows. VanCleef's work sheltered thousands of returning citizens. The militia commander demands concrete evidence before fully accepting the alarming accusation that Stormwind's chief architect is orchestrating Westfall's ruin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Shaw's Report?",a="Mathias Shaw's confidential report contains his findings on the former Stonemasons Guild and the Defias. You carry it to Gryan Stoutmantle.",al={"shaws report","mathias shaw document","the report to stoutmantle"},it="item"},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef led the Stonemasons Guild that rebuilt Stormwind. Shaw's report investigates the guild's later history.",al={"vancleef identity","who is edwin vancleef","edwin vancleef lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gryan Stoutmantle skeptical of the report?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle finds Shaw's allegations difficult to stomach. He demands concrete evidence before fully accepting them, and the details emerge when he reads the report.",al={"why doesnt gryan believe it","stoutmantle reaction","why does gryan need proof"},it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Stonemasons turn against Stormwind?",a="The Stonemasons rebuilt Stormwind, then fell into a bitter dispute over compensation. They were dissatisfied with their treatment by the crown and the House of Nobles.",al={"why are defias mad","stonemason dispute","vancleef motive"},it="history"},{q="What role does SI:7 play in this quest?",a="Mathias Shaw of SI:7 investigates possible ties between the former guild and the outlaws, then sends his findings to Stoutmantle.",al={"why mathias shaw","si7 involvement","rogue guild stormwind"},it="allies"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="You deliver the report, then help Stoutmantle pursue further evidence in the ongoing Defias investigation.",al={"what comes next","next quest defias","after shaws report"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Master Mathias Shaw want this report delivered?",a="Mathias Shaw sends his findings to Gryan Stoutmantle so the People's Militia can continue investigating the Defias. The confidential report draws on Shaw's research into the former Stonemasons Guild.",al={"why send report","shaw motive","why shaw sends report to gryan"},it="motive",add="b90c31ae"},{q="Why does Mathias Shaw rely on you to carry the report?",a="You arrived in Stormwind on Gryan Stoutmantle's direct recommendation and have already proven yourself in the field. Rather than risking official SI:7 couriers or city guards when Defias infiltrators might be watching, Shaw trusts you to carry his confidential findings straight back to the People's Militia.",al={"why not send guards","why use an adventurer","why me shaw"},it="why_me",add="d51cfbac"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Stonemasons' rebellion exposes deep fractures within the kingdom. The workers who rebuilt Stormwind's stone ramparts now threaten to tear them down.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how disputes among Stormwind's former craftsmen can trouble distant settlements.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, this revelation reaches close to home. The walls of your homes and the Cathedral itself were built by the same men now pillaging the Westfall countryside."},kw={"defias","sentinel hill","shaw","stonemasons","stormwind","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:first-war"},m={start="Master Mathias Shaw",["end"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=141},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (4)"}}
E["quest:142"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="Gryan Stoutmantle sends you after an elusive Defias courier, hoping to learn how the Brotherhood directs its forces.",h="Gryan Stoutmantle sends you after an elusive Defias courier, hoping to learn how the Brotherhood directs its...",sec={{t="Intercepting the Courier",b="Gryan Stoutmantle's scouts have seen an elusive Defias Messenger traveling between Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Jangolode Mine. Unlike the thugs who hold the countryside, this courier carries written orders across the region. Stoutmantle wants him captured or killed so the People's Militia can read his satchel and learn where the brotherhood directs its forces.",sp=0},{t="A Trail of Ink",b="The recovered message confirms that Edwin VanCleef, the legendary former leader of the Stonemasons Guild, is personally directing the Defias uprising. It confirms his command over the local cells, but does not reveal where he has made his secret base.",sp=1},{t="A Fortuitous Turn",b="The message confirms VanCleef's leadership, and the People's Militia catches a break. A desperate bandit is caught trying to steal farmer Saldean's wagon and agrees to turn traitor in exchange for his life. With written proof in hand, Stoutmantle shifts his focus to the turncoat, hoping he can lead an escort into the heart of the Defias hideout.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Defias Messenger travel?",a="The Defias Messenger starts his patrol in Moonbrook, outside the blacksmith shop. He walks north to the Gold Coast Quarry and the Jangolode Mine, enters both underground digs, then retraces his route to Moonbrook.",al={"messenger route","where is defias messenger","find messenger"},gp=true},{q="What does the intercepted message reveal?",a="Stoutmantle hopes the courier's orders will reveal the Brotherhood's command structure and help locate its hideout. The message's contents become known once it is recovered.",al={"what was in the message","mysterious message text","vancleef note"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle commands the People's Militia from its headquarters at Sentinel Hill. With too few royal Stormwind guards, he organizes volunteers and adventurers to defend Westfall from Defias raiders.",al={"stoutmantle role","who gives this quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the messenger visiting the mines?",a="The brotherhood has overrun Westfall's mineral wealth, using the Jangolode Mine and Gold Coast Quarry for raw supplies, shelter, and staging grounds. The messenger carries word between those operations and the Brotherhood's leadership.",al={"why gold coast quarry","why jangolode mine"}},{q="Does catching the messenger reveal the Defias hideout?",a="Stoutmantle plans to use the intercepted orders to continue searching for the hideout. You learn the next lead when you return to him.",al={"did we find the hideout","where is hideout"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef was Grand Mason of the Stonemasons Guild, which rebuilt Stormwind. Stoutmantle's investigation looks into VanCleef's possible connection to the Brotherhood.",al={"who is vancleef","defias leader"},sp=1,it="leader"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want this done?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia are fighting a desperate campaign to reclaim Westfall from the Defias Brotherhood. While the militia knows the thieves are operating across the province's farms and mines, they still do not know where the brotherhood's main hideout is located. Intercepting this messenger is Stoutmantle's best lead on discovering their stronghold and striking directly at their leadership.",al={"gryan stoutmantle motive","why intercept messenger","why catch defias messenger"},it="motive",add="885172ef"},{q="Who is the Defias Messenger?",a="The courier is a Defias operative tasked with running dispatches between the brotherhood's key strongholds in Westfall: the occupied town of Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry, and the Jangolode Mine. Because he coordinates movements between these scattered outposts, capturing him or seizing his orders offers the People's Militia a rare window into the conspirators' command structure.",al={"defias messenger","who is the messenger","target messenger"},it="target",add="fc5d2b39"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need you for this task?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its absolute limit, maintaining a thin defensive perimeter around Sentinel Hill while defending refugee farmers from rampant bandits and gnolls. Stormwind has refused to send reinforcements or royal troops to Westfall, leaving Stoutmantle without the spare soldiers needed to chase down couriers across hostile territory.",al={"why send me","why doesnt gryan do it","why militia need you"},it="why_me",add="a4c1678d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Without support from Stormwind's royal garrison, the People's Militia handles Westfall's intelligence on its own, tracking couriers along lonely dirt roads.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how skilled scouts and cutpurses coordinate a sprawling shadow network beneath the militia's nose.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can trace the dispatches to Edwin VanCleef and see the bitter, lingering fallout of Stormwind's political and labor disputes."},kw={"defias","jangolode","messenger","moonbrook","quarry","saldean","stoutmantle","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:gold-coast-quarry","subzone:jangolode-mine","subzone:defias-hideout"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=142,ri={"A Mysterious Message"}},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (5)"}}
E["quest:144"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Westfall",z="westfall",s="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon receives a hard answer from Westfall. He asked Gryan Stoutmantle for soldiers to defend Redridge, but Westfall faces troubles of its own.",h="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon receives a hard answer from Westfall.",sec={{t="A Plea Across Shifting Frontiers",b="Magistrate Solomon faces growing troubles in the Redridge Mountains without Stormwind's royal garrison. So he writes to Gryan Stoutmantle, commander of the People's Militia in Westfall, and asks the southern frontier for help. Solomon hopes the volunteers at Sentinel Hill can spare fighters to strengthen Lakeshire's defenses. He does not know how hard pressed the western plains are.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Refusal",b="Gryan Stoutmantle refuses, though the answer weighs heavily on him. Westfall fights the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls because the House of Nobles and the crown have abandoned the kingdom's breadbasket. The People's Militia formed to help the people survive. Its ranks lose good men each day, and Stoutmantle cannot spare a single fighter for Redridge.",sp=0},{t="The Kingdom's Fracturing Realm",b="When you carry Stoutmantle's reply back to Lakeshire, Solomon sees the frontier territories share the same neglect. Local magistrates and citizen militias must defend themselves while the Stormwind Army remains withheld. Solomon turns south toward Darkshire in Duskwood, hoping to find aid there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why did Magistrate Solomon ask Westfall for help?",a="Magistrate Solomon sought help because Lakeshire faces growing threats without Stormwind's army. He knew Gryan Stoutmantle had organized the People's Militia to defend Westfall and hoped it could spare soldiers for Redridge.",al={"why ask westfall","solomon letter to stoutmantle","why westfall militia"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle refuse to send aid?",a="Westfall is already fighting the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls. Stoutmantle says the Militia exists because Stormwind abandoned Westfall, and it has no fighters to spare.",al={"why stoutmantle says no","militia refuse lakeshire","stoutmantle response"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Stormwind Army during these crises?",a="The letters do not say why the Stormwind Army is away. Solomon and Stoutmantle can only wonder what keeps it from defending the outer provinces.",al={"why stormwind not helping","where is the army","stormwind desertion"},it="history"},{q="What happens after returning Stoutmantle's letter to Solomon?",a="After learning Westfall cannot help, Magistrate Solomon turns to Duskwood. He sends you to Darkshire, hoping Mayor Ello Ebonlocke's Night Watch can offer aid.",al={"next quest after messenger to westfall","what does solomon do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer force organized by Gryan Stoutmantle and based at Sentinel Hill. Local farmers, veterans, and residents defend Westfall from outlaws and gnolls without crown troops.",al={"who are the peoples militia","westfall militia"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran soldier who leads Westfall's defense. From the tower at Sentinel Hill, he gathers volunteers and directs the fight against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"gryan stoutmantle lore","who is stoutmantle"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you instead of his own militia?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its breaking point defending Westfall's farms from the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls. Stoutmantle cannot spare a single fighter to make the long journey east through Elwynn Forest to Redridge. Since you arrived carrying Magistrate Solomon's request in the first place, you are already acting as Redridge's courier and are best suited to carry the grim reply back.",al={"why send me","why not send a militia runner","why does gryan need a messenger"},it="why_me",add="84b4f9a5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This correspondence shows the divide between Stormwind Keep's rulers and the outlying provinces. Westfall and Redridge are left to fend for themselves.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you see how isolated the provincial towns are. Commoners and veterans bleed to defend lands the nobles of Stormwind refuse to protect."},kw={"gryan stoutmantle","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","messenger to westfall","peoples militia","redridge","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:143","quest:145","quest:12","zone:westfall","subzone:lakeshire","topic:stormwind-army"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",["end"]="Magistrate Solomon",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=144},src={"Messenger to Westfall (2)"}}
E["quest:151"] = {t="quest",n="Poor Old Blanchy",z="westfall",s="On Westfall's road, Poor Old Blanchy waits with the stranded Furlbrows, worn out and hungry. Their wagon broke as they fled, and Verna asks you to find oats at nearby abandoned farms to feed the mare.",h="On Westfall's road, Poor Old Blanchy waits with the stranded Furlbrows, worn out and hungry.",sec={{t="A Stranded Household",b="Verna and Farmer Furlbrow are stranded beside Westfall's main road. Bandits and rogue mechanical harvest golems have driven families like theirs from their homes. The Furlbrows tried to carry their belongings to safety, but their wagon broke down, leaving them marooned in open country.",sp=0},{t="Comfort for a Faithful Mare",b="Old Blanchy has plowed and hauled for the Furlbrow family through many seasons. Now the delay has left the gentle mare exhausted and starving. Verna asks you to search nearby overrun farmsteads for sacks of oats. Hostile threshers and gnoll scavengers threaten there, but the grain could give the faithful mare a decent meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Old Blanchy?",a="Old Blanchy is the Furlbrow family's beloved, aging workhorse. For years she has pulled their plows and carts across Westfall. Now she is exhausted and stranded beside the road after their wagon axle broke.",al={"who is blanchy","what is old blanchy","blanchy lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Furlbrow wagon broken down?",a="The Furlbrows tried to flee their farm with all their belongings, but the wagon gave out under the strain. They are stranded along the highway, exposed to bandits and prowling beasts.",al={"why are they stuck","furlbrow wagon","broken wagon road"},it="origin"},{q="Where do the oats come from?",a="Sacks of oats lie scattered across the fields and outbuildings of Westfall's overrun farms. Homesteaders left them behind when they fled rogue harvest machines and bandits.",al={"where are oats","find oats","sacks of oats"},it="place"},{q="What threats guard the grain in the fields?",a="Southwest of the road, rogue mechanical harvest watchers and bands of Riverpaw gnolls scavenge in deserted barns.",al={"what attacks at farms","farm dangers","harvest golems oats"},it="threat"},{q="Why hasn't the family moved Old Blanchy to safety?",a="Old Blanchy is spent and starving, unable to pull or travel far without food. The Furlbrows refuse to leave their loyal mare or their belongings behind.",al={"why stay with wagon","can horse walk","why not go sentinel hill"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Stormwind send aid to farmers like the Furlbrows?",a="Stormwind's royal court offers Westfall's homesteaders almost no protection or aid. Rural folk are largely left to fend for themselves or depend on the struggling People's Militia.",al={"stormwind help westfall","where are guards","alliance aid westfall"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Verna Furlbrow want this done?",a="The Furlbrows' wagon broke down unexpectedly along the road, stranding them far from their destination. Their loyal old horse, Old Blanchy, is completely exhausted from the journey and all the hard labor she has endured. Verna fed her before they left home, but Blanchy is now on her last leg. Without fresh oats to nourish her, the tired beast cannot recover the strength needed to carry on.",al={"why help blanchy","verna furlbrow motive","why does blanchy need oats"},it="motive",add="b3f21e2d"},{q="What is the Handful of Oats for?",a="These oats are vital feed meant to sustain and revive Old Blanchy. The Furlbrows' faithful draft horse is utterly exhausted from pulling their loaded wagon and running low on sustenance after their sudden breakdown. Giving her handfuls of grain scavenged from the outlying farmsteads restores her spirits and strength while the family contends with their broken axle.",al={"what are handful of oats for","handful of oats use","purpose of oats"},it="item",add="c126e1f4"},{q="Why does Verna Furlbrow ask you rather than gathering the oats herself?",a="The Furlbrows are helpless roadside travelers stranded beside their wrecked wagon, completely unequipped to face the dangers of Westfall's fields. The abandoned farmlands where grain sacks remain are overrun by hostile mechanical harvest reapers and roaming prowlers. Verna and her husband must stay to watch over their damaged wagon and weakened horse, leaving dangerous foraging to seasoned adventurers like you.",al={"why cant verna get oats","why ask me verna","why furlbrows need help"},it="why_me",add="3b562f8e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The stranded Furlbrows show how rural human subjects suffer neglect while the capital remains paralyzed by political stagnation.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know that caring for a spent draft animal honors the bond between working folk and the beasts that faithfully bear their burdens."},kw={"harvest golem","horse","oats","old blanchy","poor old blanchy","verna furlbrow","wagon","westfall"},rel={"npc:verna-furlbrow","zone:westfall","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Verna Furlbrow",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=151,ri={"Handful of Oats (Classic)"}},src={"Poor Old Blanchy"}}
E["quest:152"] = {t="quest",n="The Coast Isn't Clear",z="westfall",s="Shipwrecked sailors struggle to reach Westfall's western shore as murlocs close in. Captain Grayson calls on you to clear the beaches so survivors can land safely.",h="Shipwrecked sailors struggle to reach Westfall's western shore as murlocs close in.",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships",b="Reefs, squalls, and jagged rocks drive ships onto Westfall's shoals. Survivors cling to wreckage and crawl onto the sand, hoping help will come. They find murloc tribes along the shore instead, and the murlocs show no mercy to castaways.",sp=0},{t="The Ghostly Lookout",b="Captain Grayson watches from a lonely outcropping southwest of the mainland. Though dead, he remains bound to the lighthouse and to his duty toward passing ships and lost sailors. Coastrunners hold the northern shore. Farther south, Tidehunters, Warriors, and Oracles gather.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Grayson?",a="Captain Grayson is the spectral sea captain who haunts the Westfall Lighthouse. He still feels bound to protect sailors in dangerous waters and those who survive a wreck.",al={"captain grayson","ghost in the lighthouse","lighthouse keeper westfall"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Grayson want the murlocs cleared from the coast?",a="Grayson wants the murlocs cleared because shipwrecked sailors often wash ashore along Westfall. Murlocs swarm the beaches from north to south and kill survivors who reach land.",al={"why kill murlocs westfall","coast isn't clear reason","why clear the coast"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these different murlocs located?",a="Murloc Coastrunners generally live along Westfall's northern coast. Murloc Warriors, Oracles, and Tidehunters gather in settlements and camps on the southern beaches.",al={"murloc locations westfall","where are coastrunners","where are tidehunters"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Captain Grayson hostile to the Alliance or Horde?",a="Captain Grayson is neutral. His duty to sailors crosses political lines, and he asks any capable traveler to make the coast safer.",al={"is grayson friendly","grayson faction","can horde do this quest"},it="side"},{q="Does this quest require relighting the lighthouse first?",a="No. Captain Grayson asks you to clear the coast whether or not you have helped relight the Westfall Lighthouse.",al={"do i need keeper of the flame first","prerequisite for coast isnt clear"},gp=true},{q="Are the murlocs working for the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. The murlocs act on their own and attack anyone entering their shoreline hunting grounds. The Defias Brotherhood operates nearby, in the Moonbrook region and southern coves.",al={"are defias allied with murlocs","defias murloc connection"},it="ties"},{q="What murlocs are threatening the Westfall shore?",a="You are hunting the murlocs swarming the western beaches of Westfall: Coastrunners prowling the northern surf, alongside the Warriors, Tidehunters, and Oracles entrenched further south. These aquatic predators nest among the coastal shipwrecks, preying upon stranded vessels and attacking anyone unfortunate enough to wash ashore.",al={"what murlocs am i killing","who are the coast murlocs","murloc targets westfall coast"},it="target",add="9a80f3b4"},{q="Why does Captain Grayson need an adventurer to fight the murlocs?",a="Captain Grayson is a restless ghost bound to the lonely rocks of the Westfall Lighthouse. Incapable of marching along the shoreline himself, and with Stormwind's garrison having abandoned the region to banditry, he relies entirely on passing adventurers like you to secure the beaches for surviving sailors.",al={"why doesnt grayson kill murlocs","why grayson need me","why not the guards clear the coast"},it="why_me",add="49634979"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="With the Stormwind army absent from Westfall, the People's Militia struggles to protect inland farms. Allies such as Captain Grayson help defend the coast.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know merchant vessels and fishermen have long sailed Westfall's waters. The murloc-held shore is a bitter sign of the kingdom's lost frontiers."},kw={"captain grayson","coastrunner","great sea","murloc","oracle","shipwrecks","tidehunter","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"npc:captain-grayson","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","quest:103","quest:104","topic:murloc","zone:westfall"},m={start="Captain Grayson",["end"]="Captain Grayson",level="19",faction="neutral",id=152},src={"The Coast Isn't Clear (Classic)"}}
E["quest:153"] = {t="quest",n="Red Leather Bandanas",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, Red Leather Bandanas mark the Defias fight. Scout Galiaan seeks the red masks worn by outlaws as the People's Militia struggles to track them across Westfall.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Red Leather Bandanas mark the Defias fight.",sec={{t="A Mark of Allegiance",b="Across Westfall, a red bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood. Cutpurses, looters, and traitors from many walks of life join the gang, then rally beneath the same crimson sign. At Sentinel Hill, Scout Galiaan and the People's Militia collect the cloth as proof that bandits have fallen. The bandanas also help them follow the Defias as its fronts shift across the countryside.",sp=0},{t="The Militia's Scouting Efforts",b="Stormwind has denied Westfall proper military support, leaving the People's Militia to chart Defias activity with seasoned observers like Scout Galiaan. From Sentinel Hill, Galiaan watches outlaw patrols and tracks their movements. Passing adventurers and militia volunteers take on the dangerous work of bringing down the highwaymen who drove honest farmers from their land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red leather bandanas?",a="The red leather bandana marks allegiance to the Defias Brotherhood and hides the identities of former laborers, thieves, and outlaws. It also strikes fear into Westfall's remaining farmers.",al={"defias red mask meaning","why red masks","defias bandana lore"},it="item"},{q="Who is Scout Galiaan?",a="Scout Galiaan serves in the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill. He tracks the Defias Brotherhood's movements and shifting fronts across Westfall, and coordinates bounties to curb outlaw activity.",al={"scout galiaan","who gives red leather bandanas","sentinel hill scout"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Militia need adventurers to collect these bandanas?",a="The People's Militia is stretched thin, without royal soldiers or funding from Stormwind. Bounties give scouts like Galiaan proof of fallen bandits and help weaken the Defias while Sentinel Hill stays defended.",al={"why collect bandanas","why militia bounty"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the bandits carrying these bandanas found?",a="Defias outlaws roam nearly every corner of Westfall. They occupy abandoned farmsteads, prowl the crossroads, and camp along the Gold Coast and around the Moonbrook hills.",al={"where find defias bandanas","defias locations westfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to the bandanas after you turn them in?",a="Scout Galiaan uses the bandanas as proof of fallen outlaws. They help him track shifting Defias fronts and gauge how the militia's campaigns affect the Brotherhood's numbers in the region.",al={"what does galiaan do with bandanas"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the Stormwind Army involved in this bounty?",a="No. Stormwind's military has largely left Westfall to focus on other internal troubles. Local defense rests with Gryan Stoutmantle and the volunteer People's Militia.",al={"stormwind guard westfall","does stormwind help sentinel hill"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Scout Galiaan want Defias bandanas collected?",a="Scout Galiaan has been tracking the shifting movements of the Defias Brotherhood across Westfall. By gathering the red leather bandanas worn by their foot soldiers and cutthroats, he can confirm gang activity, gauge the strength of their fronts, and whittle down their numbers before they completely overrun Sentinel Hill.",al={"galiaan bandana motive","why galiaan wants bandanas","why collect red leather bandanas"},it="motive",add="b62187e9"},{q="Who are you hunting for these bandanas?",a="You are hunting the brigands and operatives of the Defias Brotherhood who prowl the plains and abandoned farmsteads of Westfall. Scout Galiaan has learned that many members of the gang can be tracked by the red leather bandanas they wear, and their shifting front has spread across the region through raids, theft and extortion.",al={"who has red bandanas","defias bandanas targets","who drops red leather bandanas"},it="target",add="868cbc1b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of the People's Militia, you help defend Westfall while Stormwind's royal leadership sends no aid.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how Defias highwaymen have joined beneath crimson masks to form an army on Stormwind's doorstep."},kw={"bandanas","defias brotherhood","peoples militia","red leather bandanas","scout galiaan","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall"},m={start="Scout Galiaan",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=153,ri={"Red Leather Bandana"}},src={"Red Leather Bandanas"}}
E["quest:155"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, the People's Militia seeks the Defias Brotherhood's hidden base. A captured brigand will guide you there in exchange for protection, leading through Moonbrook to Edwin VanCleef's inner sanctum.",h="In Westfall, the People's Militia seeks the Defias Brotherhood's hidden base.",sec={{t="A Turncoat's Bargain",b="The Defias Traitor fears execution or assassination by his former brothers. So he bargains with the People's Militia: escort him safely through hostile territory, and he will reveal where Edwin VanCleef and his ringleaders hide. The thieves' network silences those who speak out, and the turncoat needs armed protection along the road.",sp=0},{t="The Road Through Moonbrook",b="The traitor leads you southwest from Sentinel Hill into Moonbrook, a township overrun by the Brotherhood. He guides you past the abandoned town square and fountain, drawing the anger of brigands, looters, and highwaymen who patrol the ruins. Then he leads you to the entrance of the sprawling Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, where VanCleef has fortified an underground stronghold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Defias Traitor?",a="The Defias Traitor is a former member of the Brotherhood who became an informant for Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia. Fearing death at his former comrades' hands, he traded the location of Edwin VanCleef's underground redoubt for an escort to safety.",al={"who is the traitor","defias traitor identity","defias rat"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the traitor lead you?",a="He leads you southwest from Sentinel Hill into Moonbrook, past the ruined town square and fountain, to the Deadmines entrance beneath the town.",al={"where is the defias hideout","traitor path","where does he go"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need this information?",a="The People's Militia has fought highwaymen across Westfall without knowing where Edwin VanCleef directs operations. Finding the entrance to his underground lair gives the militia a clear target at the heart of the rebellion.",al={"why do we escort the traitor","stoutmantle purpose","why find the hideout"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Moonbrook crawling with Defias?",a="Moonbrook was once a thriving agricultural center, but the Kingdom of Stormwind fell into neglect and bandits moved in. Its residents abandoned the town, and the Defias Brotherhood claimed its empty buildings as an above-ground perimeter guarding the Deadmines entrance.",al={"why are there defias in moonbrook","moonbrook takeover","who owns moonbrook"},it="residents"},{q="What happens after you discover the hideout?",a="After the traitor reveals the Deadmines entrance, you report to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill. With proof of VanCleef's location, the militia prepares a direct assault on the underground lair.",al={"what comes next","after defias escort","quest progression"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Brotherhood want the traitor dead?",a="The Defias rely on secrecy, hiding in tunnels while directing operations throughout Stormwind's territories. A turncoat who reveals the entrance to their central operation threatens to unravel their conspiracy.",al={"why kill traitor","defias attacking traitor"},it="conflict"},{q="Why is the Defias Traitor willing to guide you?",a="The traitor struck a desperate bargain with the People's Militia. Having turned his back on Edwin VanCleef and the Brotherhood, he knows he is a marked man whose former comrades want his head. Leading you straight to the secret hideout is the only bargaining chip he has left to buy his own survival and freedom under Gryan Stoutmantle's protection.",al={"why help defias traitor","defias traitor motive","why does the traitor lead you"},it="motive",add="0ac3b75c"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you to escort the traitor instead of his own guards?",a="The People's Militia is stretched desperately thin just holding Sentinel Hill and fending off bandit raids across Westfall. Stormwind has refused to deploy royal troops to aid the region, leaving Stoutmantle without the disciplined soldiers or surplus guards required to mount a secure escort mission through enemy territory. Entrusting the task to capable, independent adventurers is his only practical option.",al={"why not send militia guards","why escort traitor","why does stoutmantle need you"},it="why_me",add="ef72c66d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the embattled People's Militia, finding the hideout is a major military breakthrough and their first real chance to strike a decisive blow against Westfall's criminal insurgency.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the price of betrayal in the criminal underworld, where broken vows are answered with daggers.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see Moonbrook fallen to lawlessness and occupied by former Stonemasons. It shows how deeply the kingdom has fractured since the Third War."},kw={"deadmines","defias traitor","edwin vancleef","escort","gryan stoutmantle","moonbrook","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:the-defias-traitor","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:defias-hideout","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","quest:65"},m={start="The Defias Traitor",["end"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=155},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (6)"}}
E["quest:1651"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Valor",z="westfall",s="At her Westfall farm, Daphne Stilwell calls for aid as the Defias Brotherhood closes in. A paladin must answer her plea.",h="At her Westfall farm, Daphne Stilwell calls for aid as the Defias Brotherhood closes in.",sec={{t="A Stand in the Dust",b="The Defias Brotherhood still contests the land around Daphne's homestead. Earlier clashes have not ended the danger, and another assault is expected. You are sent to hold the ground beside her house. There is no retreat. Your pursuit of the virtues in the Tome of Valor now faces a test of courage.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Valor",b="Daphne has only her own firearm, while you can call on the blessings of the Holy Light. Wave after wave of Defias raiders attacks, and the fight tests whether you can protect someone vulnerable under crushing pressure. True valor means standing between innocent civilians and ruthless violence, even when danger bears down on you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daphne Stilwell?",a="Daphne Stilwell is a human homesteader in Westfall's grasslands. The Defias Brotherhood often intrudes on her land, but she refuses to leave and fights back against their raids.",al={"daphne stilwell","who is daphne","stilwell westfall"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Defias attacking this specific farm?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has taken much of Westfall's countryside, driving farmers away or forcing them to submit. Daphne's husband, Jordan, is away in Ironforge, leaving her alone and unprotected. The Defias want her land.",al={"why defias attack","defias raid daphne","why attack stilwell"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Tome of Valor?",a="The Tome of Valor is a sacred text the Church of the Holy Light uses to guide young paladins. Knights-in-training face physical and spiritual trials across the kingdom to live by its virtues.",al={"what is tome of valor","tome of valor quest","paladin valor tome"},it="item"},{q="What happens if Daphne falls during the battle?",a="If Daphne Stilwell falls in battle, the trial fails. Valor calls you to protect her life as well as your own from the bandit attack.",al={"can daphne die","daphne stilwell dies"},gp=true},{q="Where does this attack take place?",a="The attack takes place outside Daphne Stilwell's farmhouse. Her small farm lies in the Dagger Hills, overlooking the Longshore in southern Westfall.",al={"daphne stilwell location","where is the farm"},it="place"},{q="What comes after defending the farm?",a="After you prove your courage and drive off the Defias raiders, Daphne acknowledges your devotion. She directs you toward the next phase of your paladin trials.",al={"next quest tome of valor","after defending daphne"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Daphne Stilwell need your help defending the farm?",a="Westfall is largely abandoned by Stormwind's army, leaving homesteaders to fend for themselves against the rising tide of outlaws. Although Daphne is determined to defend her home and has a firearm inside, she cannot stand alone against an organized assault. A prior wave has already tested her, and she knows the coming raid will send far more outlaws than a solitary settler could ever hope to survive.",al={"why help daphne stilwell","why can't daphne defend herself","daphne stilwell help why"},it="why_me",add="dca50aad"},{q="Why does Daphne Stilwell want to make a stand?",a="This farm represents Daphne Stilwell's livelihood and her stubborn refusal to be driven out by outlaws. Rather than flee or cede her land to brigands who have overrun Westfall, she chooses to stand her ground. Protecting her homestead is a matter of pure survival and pride; if she yields here, she loses everything she has built.",al={"daphne stilwell motive","why fight defias daphne","why does daphne want to stay"},it="motive",add="3da31dda"},{q="Who are the Defias attackers hitting Daphne Stilwell's farm?",a="The attackers are Defias raiders, members of the widespread criminal brotherhood terrorizing Westfall. They operate across the region, seizing abandoned farmsteads, extorting residents, and forcibly driving out any who defy their presence. Daphne's refusal to abandon her home marks her homestead as a prime target for a coordinated raid to crush any remaining civilian resistance.",al={"who are the attackers","what are defias raiders","defias attacking stilwell farm"},it="target",add="7af5f29f"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you are tested as a steadfast protector. Holding the line beside Daphne puts valor into action as you shield the innocent from harm.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's garrison is spread thin and cannot guard rural homesteads. Defending Westfall's loyal citizens falls to individual heroes."},kw={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","defias raiders","paladin trial","tome of valor","westfall"},rel={"npc:daphne-stilwell","zone:westfall","topic:light"},m={start="Daphne Stilwell",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1651},src={"The Tome of Valor (4)"}}
E["quest:184"] = {t="quest",n="Furlbrow's Deed",z="westfall",s="Farmer Furlbrow and Verna stand driven from their farm, while Defias bandits carry their land grant through Elwynn Forest. Return it to Farmer Furlbrow near the Westfall border, and the couple keeps its claim to the stolen homestead.",h="Farmer Furlbrow and Verna stand driven from their farm, while Defias bandits carry their land grant through...",sec={{t="A Clue on Stolen Paper",b="A deed signed by Theodore and Verna Furlbrow turns up among Defias bandits in Elwynn. On its back, a crude note says the bandits drove the elderly farmer from his property. They carried the deed across the river into Elwynn to copy it and forge claims to other seized land. The note places the stranded Furlbrows just over the border, beside the road, after their wagon broke.",sp=0},{t="The Plight of Westfall's Farmers",b="The Defias have driven dozens of Westfall families from their ancestral land. They use force and false claims to seize more farms for the Brotherhood, while Theodore and Verna leave their own farm for safety. Their lawful deed preserves their claim if order ever returns to the province.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find this deed?",a="Defias Brotherhood bandits carry the deed in southern and western Elwynn Forest, including near Jerod's Landing and in local camps.",al={"deed drop","how to get furlbrows deed","where does the deed drop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is Farmer Furlbrow?",a="Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna are stranded beside their broken wagon on the main road just inside Westfall, shortly after you cross the bridge west from Elwynn Forest.",al={"furlbrow location","where to turn in furlbrows deed","where is the farmer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why did the Defias want the deed in the first place?",a="A note on the back says the bandits mean to copy Furlbrow's legitimate deed and forge claims to other properties. False paperwork would strengthen their hold on stolen farms.",al={"why did bandits steal the deed","why do defias want deeds"},it="motive"},{q="Are the Furlbrows returning to their farm?",a="The couple is fleeing the region because of lawlessness and bandit attacks. Holding their deed lets them legally reclaim their land if Westfall is ever pacified.",al={"are furlbrows going home","what happens to the furlbrow farm"},it="next_step"},{q="Why isn't Stormwind protecting these farms?",a="Stormwind's protection has faltered amid King Varian Wrynn's sudden disappearance and domestic political tension. With royal resources focused on the capital, outer territories like Westfall are left to face the surging Defias Brotherhood.",al={"why no guards in westfall","why is stormwind ignoring westfall"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the connection between Elwynn and Westfall in this quest?",a="The Defias network reaches from Elwynn Forest across the river into Westfall. Its presence there shows how far its reach extends into the kingdom's core territories.",al={"why was deed in elwynn","connection between zones"},it="history"},{q="Why should I return Furlbrow's Deed?",a="The deed itself is just an inanimate scrap of paper, but the message scribbled on its back reveals that Defias ruffians intimidated Theodore and Verna Furlbrow into giving up their land. The thieves intended to use it as a template to forge claims on other properties. Taking it back to the fleeing Furlbrows gives an honest farming family the only proof of ownership they have left, offering them hope to someday reclaim their stolen heritage if peace ever returns to Westfall.",al={"why return the deed","westfall deed motive","furlbrow deed purpose"},it="motive",add="9b306b68"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Furlbrows' plight shows the Stormwind crown has failed to protect its taxpaying citizens beyond the capital's fortified walls.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, returning a stolen deed to refugees honors your holy vows to defend the defenseless and bring justice to lawless borderlands."},kw={"defias","elwynn","furlbrow","theodore furlbrow","verna furlbrow","westfall","westfall deed"},rel={"npc:farmer-furlbrow","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","quest:65"},m={start=":Westfall Deed",["end"]="Farmer Furlbrow",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=184},src={"Furlbrow's Deed (Classic)"}}
E["quest:22"] = {t="quest",n="Goretusk Liver Pie",z="westfall",s="At the Saldean Farm in Westfall, Salma Saldean is making pie through hard times. Bandits have ravaged the kingdom’s breadbasket, and homesteaders hunt aggressive boars to feed their families.",h="At the Saldean Farm in Westfall, Salma Saldean is making pie through hard times.",sec={{t="Frontier Hospitality",b="Westfall once fed Stormwind as its fertile breadbasket. Now neglected roads, roving outlaws, and overgrown fields make life hard for the few settlers who remain. At the Saldean Farm, Salma Saldean works to keep a sense of home despite the dangers. A traditional meat pie offers one of the few comforts to homesteaders trying to preserve their way of life.",sp=0},{t="Westfall's Feral Beasts",b="Goretusks roam Westfall’s plains in great numbers. Their tough hides and vicious tusks make them dangerous to farmhands alone, yet their meat feeds families cut off from regular trade. Salma’s recipe calls for crushed rosemary, minced garlic, chopped dill, and simmering gravy. Prepared with care, the beasts’ pungent organs become a rich, savory meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Salma Saldean?",a="Salma Saldean is a resilient homesteader who lives with her husband, Farmer Saldean, at their farm in central Westfall. Her home-cooked meals lift spirits despite the dangers from bandits and wild beasts.",al={"salma saldean","who is salma","saldean wife"},it="people"},{q="Why does Salma want goretusk livers?",a="Salma wants goretusk livers for her famous savory meat pie, which she is preparing to share with her husband. The crust is baked and the seasonings are ready; only the livers remain before she can finish simmering the filling.",al={"why goretusk liver","what is the pie made of","liver pie purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where are goretusks typically found in Westfall?",a="Goretusks roam across Westfall’s golden plains and fallow farm plots, rooting through abandoned fields and wandering along dirt roads.",al={"goretusk locations","where to find boars","goretusk liver hunt"},gp=true},{q="Are goretusks dangerous to the local farmers?",a="Yes. Goretusks are aggressive, territorial wild boars with sharp tusks. They threaten livestock and pose a significant danger to unprotected travelers across the plains.",al={"are goretusks hostile","boar danger westfall"},it="threat"},{q="Why is food so scarce in Westfall right now?",a="Food is scarce because Stormwind gives little support and organized bandits raid the farms. Many farmers have been driven from their land, leaving the kingdom’s former breadbasket an impoverished frontier.",al={"westfall famine","why no food westfall","westfall hard times"},it="place"},{q="Does completing this task help the Saldean farm survive?",a="Fresh meat cannot solve Westfall’s broader crises, but it helps sustain the Saldean family and gives travelers hearty rations for the road ahead.",al={"does the pie matter","saldean food supply"}},{q="What are the Goretusk Livers used for?",a="Salma Saldean requires fresh goretusk livers as the final, crucial ingredient for her signature Westfall meat pie. She has already prepared the seasoned crust, chopped dill, garlic, rosemary, and simmering gravy, but lacks the meat itself to complete the family meal.",al={"what is goretusk liver for","why goretusk liver","goretusk liver pie recipe"},it="item",add="3baa4b09"},{q="Why does Salma ask an adventurer instead of hunting the goretusks herself?",a="Salma is occupied with running the homestead and tending to the kitchen while the Saldeans struggle to survive the hardships gripping Westfall. With wild boars prowling aggressively outside the safety of the fence and local militia thin on the ground, she depends on capable travelers to gather fresh meat.",al={"why me goretusk liver","why does salma need me","why doesnt salma hunt"},it="why_me",add="ad043644"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Salma’s dish reflects rural human cooking. Garden herbs like garlic, rosemary, and dill weed turn wild game offal into a staple meal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping rural homesteaders like the Saldeans supports loyal human families struggling to hold the kingdom’s frontier without Stormwind’s army."},kw={"boar","cooking","goretusk","liver pie","saldean farm","salma saldean","westfall"},rel={"npc:salma-saldean","npc:farmer-saldean","zone:westfall"},m={start="Salma Saldean",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=22,ri={"Goretusk Liver"}},src={"Goretusk Liver Pie (quest)"}}
E["quest:36"] = {t="quest",n="Westfall Stew",z="westfall",s="Westfall homesteaders are driven from their farms by banditry. As the Furlbrows prepare to leave, Verna entrusts her cherished recipe to Salma Saldean.",h="Westfall homesteaders are driven from their farms by banditry.",sec={{t="A Recipe Passed On",b="Defias thieves and wild mechanical harvest reapers have driven Verna and Farmer Furlbrow from their family acreage. They pack their wagon and prepare to seek refuge behind Stormwind's walls. Before they go, Verna gives her neighbor Salma Saldean the recipe for Westfall Stew. She hopes the farm's home-cooked tradition will live on.",sp=0},{t="Homestead Solidarity",b="Salma Saldean and her husband, Farmer Saldean, still hold their homestead just down the road. Verna's recipe keeps a local farm tradition alive as another family leaves. Salma sets out to gather ingredients to feed those still struggling on the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Furlbrows leaving their farm?",a="Defias thieves and bandits have made the Furlbrows' fields too dangerous to work. Verna and Farmer Furlbrow are packing their wagon to flee to Stormwind City.",al={"why furlough leaving","furlbrows leaving westfall","why verna packing"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Salma Saldean?",a="Salma Saldean is a Westfall homesteader who lives with her family on Saldean's Farm, just past the fork in the road from the Furlbrow homestead. They keep working their land despite the lawlessness around them.",al={"who is salma","salma saldean lore"},it="people"},{q="What is Westfall Stew?",a="Westfall Stew is a traditional regional dish made from ingredients found across the Westfall plains and shared among local farming households.",al={"what is westfall stew","westfall stew recipe"},it="item"},{q="Where are the Furlbrows planning to go?",a="The Furlbrows are heading north to Stormwind City for safety. Verna's friends believe she will fit right in there.",al={"where furlbrows going","furlbrow destination"},it="place"},{q="Where is Saldean's Farm located?",a="Saldean's Farm lies just beyond the fork in the main road, south of the Furlbrow pumpkin patch in Westfall.",al={"saldean farm location","where is salma saldean"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest reward the actual cooking recipe?",a="Delivering the written instructions to Salma is only the first step. To prepare the stew, she asks for help gathering the ingredients.",al={"recipe reward","do i get westfall stew recipe"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Verna Furlbrow want her stew recipe delivered to Salma Saldean?",a="With her homestead overrun by thieves and bandits, Verna Furlbrow is fleeing Westfall for good. Before she and her husband abandon the countryside for the safety of Stormwind, she wants to ensure her beloved recipe for hearty Westfall stew remains in the hands of her dear neighbor and fellow farmer, Salma Saldean.",al={"why deliver westfall stew recipe","verna furlbrow motive","why give salma recipe"},it="motive",add="6757b659"},{q="Why can't Verna Furlbrow deliver the recipe herself?",a="The roads are rife with Defias outlaws, making any travel across the plains precarious. More immediately, Verna and her husband are stranded by the wayside waiting for Farmer Furlbrow to repair their broken wagon so they can flee toward Stormwind, leaving her unable to make the trip over to Saldean's farm on her own.",al={"why does verna need me","why cant verna deliver it","verna delivery why me"},it="why_me",add="5964e98d"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Westfall Stew is frontier fare for human homesteaders, made from scavenged prairie game and hardy root vegetables.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the kingdom's rural citizens driven from their ancestral farms into urban exile as the Stormwind frontier crumbles."},kw={"cooking","farmer furlbrow","recipe","saldean's farm","salma saldean","stew","verna furlbrow","westfall"},rel={"npc:verna-furlbrow","npc:salma-saldean","subzone:saldean-s-farm","npc:farmer-furlbrow","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Verna Furlbrow",["end"]="Salma Saldean",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=36},src={"Westfall Stew (Classic)"}}
E["quest:38"] = {t="quest",n="Westfall Stew",z="westfall",s="On her farm in Westfall, Salma Saldean cooks Westfall Stew from what the frontier offers. Its ingredients reflect how homesteaders endure bandits, famine, and dangerous beasts.",h="On her farm in Westfall, Salma Saldean cooks Westfall Stew from what the frontier offers.",sec={{t="A Homesteader's Necessity",b="Westfall's settlers face bandits, famine, and rampaging beasts, far from Stormwind's lavish larders. Families like the Saldeans make do with what the land provides. Salma Saldean turns ingredients many city folk might call pests or scraps into a meal that sustains her farmhands.",sp=0},{t="The Ingredients of Survival",b="Salma's recipe brings together local okra, stringy meat from circling vultures, and snouts from wild goretusks roaming the plains. It also calls for fresh murloc eyes gathered from coastal raiders. Such fare may turn delicate stomachs in Elwynn, but Westfall cooks swear the blend makes a rich, fortifying meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does the recipe use murloc eyes?",a="Westfall farmers face shortages and frequent murloc raids along the coast and riverbanks. Salma Saldean adds fresh murloc eyes to the broth for moisture and flavor, making food from a threat.",al={"murloc eyes in food","why eat murlocs","murloc stew"},it="item"},{q="Who is Salma Saldean?",a="Salma Saldean is an Alliance homesteader who lives with her husband, Farmer Saldean, at the Saldean Farm in northern Westfall. She feeds travelers and farmhands despite the banditry and chaos pressing into the region.",al={"salma","salma saldean lore","who makes westfall stew"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the okra come from?",a="The okra comes from the few hardy vegetable crops still harvested on Westfall's struggling farms. Boiled pods release juices that thicken frontier broths.",al={"where to find okra","saldean okra","okra origin"},it="item"},{q="Is Westfall Stew considered good food?",a="Stormwind nobles may find boiled goretusk snouts and murloc eyes grotesque. For Westfall's poor farmers and weary wanderers, the stew is warm, filling comfort food.",al={"does westfall stew taste good","is westfall stew gross"},it="fame"},{q="Why do the Saldeans need adventurers to gather the ingredients?",a="Westfall is dangerous, with wild goretusks, aggressive vultures, and hostile murlocs roaming its fields and beaches. Foraging puts ordinary farmers at risk while they stay behind to defend their homesteads.",al={"why gather ingredients","why salma needs help"},it="why_me"},{q="What animal provides the meat for the stew?",a="The stew uses stringy vulture meat from carrion birds soaring over Westfall, along with snouts from wild goretusks hunted across the plains.",al={"what meat is in westfall stew","westfall stew meat"},it="item"},{q="Why does Salma Saldean want this done?",a="Salma Saldean is trying to keep her family and household fed despite the harsh times across Westfall. Between rampant banditry and untended lands, everyday supplies are hard to come by. Preparing a large, hearty batch of Westfall Stew stretches whatever local ingredients can be scavenged into a nourishing meal for the farm.",al={"why make westfall stew","salma saldean motive","why does salma need stew"},it="motive",add="43c10890"},{q="What is the Stringy Vulture Meat for?",a="The stringy vulture meat serves as one of the primary protein bases for the stew. While tough and lean on its own, slow-cooking it within the broth tenderizes the meat, allowing Salma to make good use of the scavengers circling the plains.",al={"vulture meat use","why stringy vulture meat","what is vulture meat for"},it="item",add="acee3b52"},{q="What is the Goretusk Snout for?",a="Goretusk snouts provide rich, fatty flavor and texture to the kettle. Salma considers them a delicious staple of the dish, giving the hearty broth substance that leaner meats simply cannot match.",al={"goretusk snout use","why goretusk snouts","what are snouts for"},it="item",add="939a3557"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Salma's recipe shows how frontier cooks make a fortifying meal from rough game, pungent snouts, and unusual shoreline harvests.",["race:Human"]="For humans beyond Elwynn's protective walls, Westfall Stew speaks to the grit and endurance needed to live in the kingdom's forgotten breadbasket.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's court enjoys fine wine and polished poultry, while Alliance outposts on the frontier rely on rustic dishes like this to sustain their defense against local threats."},kw={"goretusk snout","murloc eye","okra","saldean farm","salma saldean","vulture meat","westfall","westfall stew"},rel={"quest:36","npc:salma-saldean","zone:westfall","topic:murloc"},m={start="Salma Saldean",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=38,ri={"Goretusk Snout","Murloc Eye","Okra","Stringy Vulture Meat"}},src={"Westfall Stew (Classic 2)"}}
E["quest:3861"] = {t="quest",n="CLUCK!",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, a chicken may answer when you call and feed it. Follow its scratched message to the Saldean family, and a warm egg may be yours to hatch.",h="In Westfall, a chicken may answer when you call and feed it.",sec={{t="A Strange Communion",b="Across Azeroth, ordinary chickens wander farmsteads, though most travelers pass them by. Mimic a chicken's gestures and cluck, and one may stop pecking to regard you. In that brief moment, it scratches letters in the dirt, pointing you toward the farmer who can provide the food it wants.",sp=0},{t="The Farmer's Feed",b="The bird asks for Special Chicken Feed, which the Saldean family keeps for its flock in Westfall. Offer the grain and cheer the chicken on as it eats. In return, it lays a warm egg, ready to be nurtured into a feathered companion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How does a chicken offer a quest?",a="Mimic a chicken with repeated calls or flapping gestures. At last, it pauses to inspect you and scratches a message in the dirt about its hunger.",al={"chicken quest start","how to talk to chicken","cluck quest unlock"},gp=true},{q="What does the chicken spell out in the dirt?",a="The chicken scratches out S-A-L-D-E-A-N in the soil. The name points to Farmer Saldean and his wife at the Saldean Farm in central Westfall, where they sell the grain it wants.",al={"chicken scratch words","what does the chicken write","saldean chicken"}},{q="Where do you get the Special Chicken Feed?",a="Farmer Saldean keeps Special Chicken Feed at the Saldean Farm in Westfall.",al={"chicken feed vendor","where to buy chicken feed","saldean feed"},gp=true},{q="Can you do this with any chicken in the world?",a="Ordinary barnyard chickens in settled lands can answer the gesture. They are most often found around human farms, such as those in Westfall.",al={"which chickens work","does any chicken work","where to find chicken"},gp=true},{q="How do you complete the quest once you have the feed?",a="Carry Special Chicken Feed and find a chicken. Cheer it on as it eats, and it lays an egg beneath itself for you to collect.",al={"how to turn in cluck","feed chicken egg","cluck quest hand in"},gp=true},{q="What do you get for finishing the quest?",a="The fed chicken lays a Farm Chicken Egg at its feet. Collect it to receive a Chicken Egg that lets you summon a loyal Westfall chicken to follow you on your travels.",al={"cluck quest reward","chicken egg pet","westfall chicken reward"},gp=true},{q="Why does the chicken want special chicken feed?",a="The bird is simply starving for a specific treat. After you spend enough time mimicking its clucks and flaps, it recognizes you as a sympathetic spirit and scratches out the name of Farmer Saldean in the dirt. It wants nothing more than a serving of Saldean's special feed, waiting hungrily until you return to satisfy its appetite.",al={"why chicken feed","why does the chicken want this","chicken motive"},it="motive",add="dbdbc3c2"},{q="Why does the chicken need your help instead of getting food itself?",a="As an ordinary farm bird, it lacks the coin, words, and hands needed to buy Farmer Saldean's grain for itself. Only an adventurer patient enough to interpret its frantic clucking and claw-scratched messages can make the purchase and bring back the feed.",al={"why can't chicken get food","why does chicken need me","why me chicken"},it="why_me",add="034f7049"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="At the Saldean Farmstead in Westfall, this odd chicken ritual has become a familiar tale among young Alliance adventurers exploring the battered rural kingdom.",["profession:Cooking"]="The chicken's Special Chicken Feed can be eaten, though most cooks save the coarse grain for the birds."},kw={"chicken","chicken egg","cluck","poultry","saldean","saldean farm","special chicken feed","westfall chicken"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:brill","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},m={start="Chicken",faction="Neutral",id=3861},src={"CLUCK!"}}
E["quest:6181"] = {t="quest",n="A Swift Message",z="westfall",s="Quartermaster Lewis needs armor for Westfall's militia, and he sends an urgent note to Stormwind by gryphon. With little help from the kingdom's forces, he asks you to take the requisition to Thor at Sentinel Hill for the flight to the capital.",h="Quartermaster Lewis needs armor for Westfall's militia, and he sends an urgent note to Stormwind by gryphon.",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Skies",b="At Sentinel Hill, the People's Militia faces Defias outlaws and gnolls with little help from Stormwind's forces. Quartermaster Lewis relies on private contacts in the capital for weapons and armor. As the militia's supplies run low, he turns to Osric Strang, an armorer in Old Town. Lewis asks travelers to carry the urgent requisition note to Thor, Westfall's gryphon master.",sp=0},{t="The Flight Network",b="Gryphons carry people and messages swiftly across the Kingdom of Stormwind. Thor manages the air route to the capital from Sentinel Hill. When you give him Lewis's note, he carries the requisition to Stormwind by air. This route links Westfall's frontier garrison to the capital despite the lack of official aid.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Quartermaster Lewis need to send a note to Stormwind?",a="Stormwind gives Westfall little direct military aid, and the People's Militia is running low on armor. Lewis sends a requisition to Osric Strang, a trusted armorer in the city, to secure supplies.",al={"why send note","lewis note purpose","why contact stormwind"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Osric Strang?",a="Osric Strang is an armorer in Old Town, Stormwind, whose shop is called Limited Immunity. He supplies Lewis privately when official channels fail.",al={"osric strang","who is osric","limited immunity owner"}},{q="Who is Thor?",a="Thor is the gryphon master at Sentinel Hill. He carries Lewis's note between Westfall and Stormwind, and manages the gryphon flights connecting them.",al={"who is thor","westfall flight master","thor gryphon master"}},{q="Why isn't Stormwind sending soldiers and gear to Westfall directly?",a="King Varian Wrynn is missing, and Stormwind's resources are stretched thin. Its leaders have largely neglected the outlying farmlands, leaving places like Sentinel Hill to rely on volunteer militias and private arrangements.",al={"why no stormwind help","why stormwind ignores westfall","where is the army"},it="conflict"},{q="Can any adventurer undertake this task?",a="Human adventurers who have proved themselves in Westfall are entrusted with this work. It introduces the kingdom's gryphon routes.",al={"who can take this quest","human only quest","can dwarves do this quest"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="Where does this courier mission lead next?",a="After you present the note to Thor, he prepares a gryphon flight to Stormwind. You land at the capital's gryphon roost, then seek Osric Strang in Old Town.",al={"next step","what happens after thor","where do i go next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Quartermaster Lewis ask you to carry his message?",a="Westfall's defenders are stretched thin, abandoned by the crown and besieged by Defias brigands across the plains. Quartermaster Lewis cannot abandon Sentinel Hill's supply depot, nor can the People's Militia spare sworn defenders to serve as simple messengers when every blade is needed on the watch line. A capable traveler moving toward the capital offers the swiftest, safest way to arrange vital supplies without leaving the outpost shorthanded.",al={"why Lewis need me","why not send a guard to stormwind","why courier Lewis note"},it="why_me",add="be76534e"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you carry Lewis's note while Stormwind's provinces are under strain. You also learn the gryphon routes linking the kingdom's territories.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the strain between Stormwind's capital and the frontier outposts struggling in Westfall."},kw={"armor","flight master","gryphon","old town","osric strang","peoples militia","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","stormwind","thor"},rel={"quest:6281","npc:quartermaster-lewis","npc:thor","npc:osric-strang","quest:6261","quest:6285","zone:westfall","subzone:old-town"},m={start="Quartermaster Lewis",["end"]="Thor",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6181},src={"A Swift Message (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6281"] = {t="quest",n="Continue to Stormwind",z="westfall",s="You carry a requisition from Sentinel Hill to Stormwind by gryphon, where Osric Strang awaits in Old Town.",h="You carry a requisition from Sentinel Hill to Stormwind by gryphon, where Osric Strang awaits in Old Town.",sec={{t="Taking Wing",b="Quartermaster Lewis prepares a requisition note at Sentinel Hill. Thor, the local gryphon master, offers you the fastest way out of the contested plains. For a modest fee, you ride one of the kingdom’s trained gryphons above dusty farmlands and Elwynn Forest’s river border. Then the gryphon carries you over Stormwind City’s high white ramparts.",sp=0},{t="Old Town Supply Lines",b="You land at the capital’s trade roosts, then make your way into Old Town. There you find Osric Strang at his shop, Limited Immunity. Osric supplies the frontier, yet his grim reception shows the growing rift between Westfall’s beleaguered People’s Militia and the distracted rulers in Stormwind Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You carry Quartermaster Lewis’s requisition from Sentinel Hill to Stormwind by gryphon. Along the way, you learn the route between the outpost and the capital.",al={"why do this quest","quest purpose","continue to stormwind objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Osric Strang located?",a="Osric Strang runs Limited Immunity in Old Town, inside Stormwind City.",al={"where is osric strang","find osric strang","limited immunity location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Hill need supplies from Stormwind?",a="The People’s Militia at Sentinel Hill struggles against the Defias Brotherhood and receives little formal military aid from the capital. Quartermaster Lewis must buy gear directly from civilian merchants.",al={"why need supplies","westfall supply issue","sentinel hill gear"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Thor?",a="Thor is the gryphon master at Sentinel Hill. He manages routes connecting Westfall to Stormwind City and other friendly hubs.",al={"who is thor","westfall gryphon master","thor westfall"},it="identity"},{q="What is inside Lewis' Note?",a="Lewis’s Note is an urgent requisition from Quartermaster Lewis, listing the gear and provisions needed to keep Sentinel Hill’s garrison equipped.",al={"lewis note","what does the note say","contents of note"},it="item"},{q="What happens after delivering the note?",a="After Osric receives the requisition, he sends you to speak with Stormwind’s gryphon master, Dungar Longdrink. You arrange transport of the ordered supplies back to Westfall.",al={"what next","follow up quest","after osric strang"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thor want this done?",a="Thor is Westfall's gryphon master, and his responsibility is keeping communication and transport flowing between the frontier and the capital. Quartermaster Lewis urgently needs supplies delivered to Sentinel Hill, but gryphons do not fly themselves without someone to hold the reins and deliver the requisition into Osric Strang's hands. By sending you aboard one of his mounts, Thor ensures Sentinel Hill's plea actually reaches Stormwind City.",al={"why does thor send me","thor motive continue to stormwind","why does gryphon master thor help"},it="motive",add="9888c0f8"},{q="Why does Thor need me instead of flying to Stormwind himself?",a="Thor cannot simply abandon his post at Sentinel Hill. As the settlement's only gryphon master, he must remain on site to tend the roost, manage the flight lines, and keep Westfall connected to the wider kingdom. An able courier like you, willing to cover the travel fee and carry Lewis's requisition directly to Osric Strang in Old Town, lets Sentinel Hill get its message to Stormwind without stripping the outpost of its handler.",al={"why me continue to stormwind","why cant thor deliver the note","why does thor need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="a35c3ce1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can rely on gryphon masters to connect scattered outposts and keep remote garrisons linked to the capital.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see in Old Town how distant common citizens and isolated frontiersmen feel from the politics of the grand House of Nobles."},kw={"flight path","gryphon","lewis' note","limited immunity","old town","osric strang","sentinel hill","thor"},rel={"quest:6181","quest:6261","quest:6285","npc:thor","npc:osric-strang","npc:quartermaster-lewis","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:old-town"},m={start="Thor",["end"]="Osric Strang",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6281},src={"Continue to Stormwind (Classic)"}}
E["quest:64"] = {t="quest",n="The Forgotten Heirloom",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, The Forgotten Heirloom is a pocket watch left behind as the Furlbrows fled their farm. Recovering it gives them a chance to reclaim something personal amid the chaos.",h="In Westfall, The Forgotten Heirloom is a pocket watch left behind as the Furlbrows fled their farm.",sec={{t="A Midnight Eviction",b="Farmer Furlbrow and Verna were driven from their Westfall farm by violence. Shouts from the pumpkin patches woke them in the night, leaving little time to gather what they could carry. In their flight, Furlbrow left behind the pocket watch Verna's father gave him on their wedding day. It remains in the wardrobe of their occupied farmhouse.",sp=0},{t="Hooligans in the Fields",b="Defias thugs and thieves, including Benny Blaanco, now pick through the abandoned Furlbrow farm. Returning for a keepsake could mean death for ordinary folk. You can take the pocket watch from the wardrobe and restore a measure of dignity to a family that has lost nearly everything to Westfall's lawlessness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the pocket watch so important to Farmer Furlbrow?",a="Verna's father gave Farmer Furlbrow the pocket watch on their wedding day. Now refugees who have lost their livelihood, the Furlbrows keep a sentimental link to their former life and family heritage in it.",al={"why watch important","furlbrow watch significance","who gave furlbrow the watch"},it="motive"},{q="Who drove the Furlbrows away from their farm?",a="Defias brigands and looters drove the Furlbrows from their farm during the night. Their attack reflects the lawlessness forcing many farming families to abandon their homes and fields under threat of violence.",al={"who attacked the farm","who took furlbrow farm","what happened to the furlbrows"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the watch hidden?",a="The pocket watch is inside a bedroom wardrobe at the Furlbrow homestead, in the pumpkin patches west of the Furlbrows' roadside camp in northern Westfall. Squatters and Defias outlaws occupy the farmhouse.",al={"where is the pocket watch","find watch","wardrobe location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Benny Blaanco?",a="Benny Blaanco is an outlaw inside the Furlbrow farmhouse with Defias companions. They ransack the abandoned home and guard it against anyone who might reclaim it.",al={"benny blaanco lore","who is the guy in the house"},it="target"},{q="Where are the Furlbrows staying now?",a="Farmer Furlbrow and Verna are stranded by the roadside in Westfall. They shelter near their wagon and try to survive the region's collapse.",al={"where are furlbrows","where is farmer furlbrow"},it="residents"},{q="Does Stormwind send guards to help recover farms like this?",a="Stormwind's official military presence in Westfall is nearly absent, amid political indifference and missing leadership in the capital. The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill lacks the strength to reclaim individual farms, leaving settlers exposed.",al={"stormwind help westfall","why no guards at farm"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Furlbrow's Pocket Watch?",a="It is an ordinary timepiece, but an invaluable family heirloom. Verna's father gave it to Farmer Furlbrow on their wedding day. Having lost their land, harvest, and home to brigands in a single night, retrieving this single keepsake is all the elderly couple has left to salvage from the ruins of their former life.",al={"furlbrow watch","pocket watch heirloom","what is furlbrows watch"},it="item",add="028db52d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Furlbrows' plight shows how badly order has broken down in the kingdom's breadbasket. As an Alliance traveler, you are left to handle what the crown has neglected.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see honest farmers driven from their land by outlaws within a day's march of the capital. Their plight reveals the kingdom's troubles at home."},kw={"benny blaanco","defias","furlbrow","pocket watch","pumpkin patch","verna furlbrow","wardrobe","westfall"},rel={"npc:farmer-furlbrow","zone:westfall"},m={start="Farmer Furlbrow",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=64,ri={"Furlbrow's Pocket Watch"}},src={"The Forgotten Heirloom"}}
E["quest:65"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="westfall",s="From Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle sends you east to Lakeshire, where a contact may know where the Defias Brotherhood hides.",h="From Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle sends you east to Lakeshire, where a contact may know where the Defias...",sec={{t="The Threat in the Dust",b="The People's Militia cannot find who directs the bandits. Gryan Stoutmantle needs the cartel's inner circle and its commander exposed before the thieves can be stopped.",sp=0},{t="An Out-of-Town Contact",b="Wiley the Black waits upstairs at the Lakeshire inn. Stoutmantle trusts the rogue's underworld ties to reveal the Brotherhood's hideouts. Whether Wiley can offer a lead is still uncertain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia, a ragtag defense force based at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. With Stormwind neglecting the borderlands, he coordinates the defense of the few farmers and refugees still there.",al={"gryan stoutmantle","who gives this quest","quest giver westfall"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Stoutmantle send you to Lakeshire?",a="The People's Militia has no informants in Westfall's underworld. Gryan Stoutmantle calls on an old favor from Wiley the Black, a rogue at the Lakeshire inn, hoping his criminal ties can reveal who leads the thieves.",al={"why lakeshire","why go to redridge","why wiley"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Wiley the Black?",a="Wiley the Black is a rogue staying on the second floor of the Lakeshire Inn in the Redridge Mountains. He owes Gryan Stoutmantle a favor and may share underworld rumors and criminal connections.",al={"who is wiley","wiley lakeshire","wiley the black"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Defias Brotherhood?",a="In Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood's thieves wear red bandanas and have seized farms, roads, and abandoned mines. They drive homesteaders out and challenge Stormwind's authority.",al={"defias brotherhood","what is defias","red bandana bandits"},it="threat"},{q="Where can I find Wiley in Lakeshire?",a="Wiley the Black is upstairs on the second floor of the Lakeshire Inn, near the bridge in the Redridge Mountains town of Lakeshire.",al={"where is wiley","find wiley","wiley location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest involve any combat?",a="No. You travel from Sentinel Hill in Westfall across Elwynn Forest to the Lakeshire inn to meet Wiley.",al={"is this quest hard","combat in defias brotherhood quest","enemies"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle need an adventurer instead of his own People's Militia?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle's People's Militia is stretched thin just trying to defend Sentinel Hill and protect the few remaining farmers in Westfall. Stormwind refuses to send royal reinforcements, leaving the local defense desperately undermanned. Furthermore, Stoutmantle specifically needs an outsider capable of covert infiltration rather than recognizable local militia fighters who would be spotted immediately by Defias lookouts.",al={"why send me","why not send militia","why does stoutmantle need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="e3561313"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know soldiering alone cannot uncover a criminal syndicate. Stoutmantle turns to someone who understands shadows and street favors: Wiley the Black.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross from Westfall to Redridge, where the outer territories rely on one another while Stormwind neglects them."},kw={"defias","gryan stoutmantle","lakeshire","redridge","sentinel hill","westfall","wiley the black"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:wiley-the-black","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:lakeshire-inn"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",["end"]="Wiley the Black",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=65},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (quest)"}}
E["quest:79008"] = {t="quest",n="... and that note you found",z="westfall",s="A scorched note lies beside a dying campfire in Westfall. Its brief message points to a place called the twin land.",h="A scorched note lies beside a dying campfire in Westfall.",sec={{t="A Dying Fire",b="Travelers crossing Westfall’s abandoned fields and wind-scoured plains find camps left by vagrants, outlaws, or desperate wanderers. This small camp was left in haste or secrecy. Its provisions lie abandoned, embers still glow, and a scorched slip of parchment rests among the scattered debris.",sp=0},{t="The Cryptic Message",b="The blistered note bears two short sentences: “Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.” Its words point away from Westfall but give no clear direction. What place shares a name, geography, or fate with this land?",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the note say?",a="The blistered note reads, “Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.” It is the only clue at the abandoned campsite.",al={"note text","what is written on the note","blistered note words"}},{q="Where is this note found?",a="The note lies among the remains of a fire and scattered provisions in the wilderness of Westfall.",al={"note location","where is the note","campfire location"}},{q="Who left the campfire?",a="No one knows who left the camp. Whoever made the fire departed recently, leaving scattered supplies and the scorched message among the embers.",al={"who left the note","campfire owner","note author"}},{q="What does 'the twin land' refer to?",a="“The twin land” points to another region connected to the land where the note was found, but the charred message gives no further explanation.",al={"twin land meaning","what is twin land","where is twin land"}},{q="Why was the note burned?",a="The note was blistered and charred in the embers. Someone may have tried to destroy it in haste, or left it carelessly as the flames died down.",al={"why was it burned","did someone try to burn the note","charred note"}},{q="Is this connected to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Westfall is overrun by the Defias Brotherhood and destitute squatters, but the cryptic message suggests something more obscure than ordinary bandit communications.",al={"defias note","is it defias","brotherhood campfire"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how to decipher cryptic clues left in hidden campsites. Such work comes naturally to those who live by whispers, secrets, and concealed messages.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer trying to restore order to Westfall, you face another mystery on the kingdom’s frontier: an unidentified camp and an enigmatic cipher."},kw={"blistered note","campfire","charred note","embers","note","twin land","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall"},m={level="22",id=79008},src={"In-game quest text: ... and that note you found"},fv=true}
E["quest:8675"] = {t="quest",n="Skychaser the Elder",z="westfall",s="During the Lunar Festival, Skychaser the Elder watches over Westfall from Sentinel Tower. Travelers climb to honor her as an ancestral spirit, and she recognizes the living with a blessing.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Skychaser the Elder watches over Westfall from Sentinel Tower.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Dust",b="Sentinel Hill is Westfall's lone fortified redoubt. Below, weary soldiers and settlers face threats from Defias raiders and roving scavengers across the scrublands. During the Lunar Festival, Elder Skychaser appears on the open platform atop Sentinel Tower, watching from above the dust and wind. Anyone may climb and pay her respect.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Ancestors",b="Across Azeroth, the Lunar Festival honors wisdom, heritage, and the deeds of ancient spirits. When you approach, Elder Skychaser recognizes the living spark within you and accepts your homage. She gives you a token of her favor, binding the living to the honored dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Skychaser?",a="Elder Skychaser waits atop Sentinel Tower at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. Climb the spiral stairs to the upper lookout ramparts.",al={"skychaser location","where is elder skychaser","skychaser westfall"}},{q="Why is Elder Skychaser standing on top of Sentinel Tower?",a="During the Lunar Festival, ancestral spirits appear at prominent, symbolic places across Azeroth. From Sentinel Tower's heights, Elder Skychaser watches travelers brave the Westfall basin frontier.",al={"why is he in sentinel tower","skychaser tower"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You honor ancestral elders during the Lunar Festival by seeking Elder Skychaser. Your respect earns a Coin of Ancestry and a blessing that celebrates your living spirit.",al={"skychaser quest reward","why honor elder skychaser"}},{q="Can Horde players honor Elder Skychaser?",a="Elder Skychaser welcomes all pilgrims, but Sentinel Hill is a heavily defended Alliance outpost. Reaching her is perilous for Horde adventurers.",al={"can horde visit skychaser","is skychaser hostile to horde"}},{q="Does Elder Skychaser participate in the defense of Sentinel Hill?",a="No. The Lunar Festival elders are spiritual manifestations devoted to tradition and remembrance. Elder Skychaser takes no part in the People's Militia's skirmishes against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"does skychaser fight defias","is skychaser part of the people's militia"}},{q="What does Skychaser say when you greet her?",a="Elder Skychaser tells you that your spirit burns brightly with life. She accepts your homage and offers an ancestral token in return.",al={"skychaser dialogue","what does the elder say"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Elder Skychaser within the People's Militia base at Sentinel Hill. She is easy to honor while you travel through Westfall.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you face hostile Alliance guards and militia scouts at Sentinel Hill. Reaching Elder Skychaser calls for stealth, speed, or brute force.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you honor the Lunar Festival and its ancestral spirits. Skychaser links ancient traditions with deep reverence for nature."},kw={"coin of ancestry","elder skychaser","lunar festival","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","skychaser","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-tower","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall"},m={start="Elder Skychaser",id=8675},src={"Skychaser the Elder"}}
E["quest:9"] = {t="quest",n="The Killing Fields",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, The Killing Fields begins with Farmer Saldean's crops under threat. Rogue Harvest Watchers overrun his fields and neighboring farms, while the Defias Brotherhood's disruption has left local agriculture in ruin.",h="In Westfall, The Killing Fields begins with Farmer Saldean's crops under threat.",sec={{t="A Beleaguered Homestead",b="Many Westfall farmers abandoned their land when bandits and outlaws swept through. Farmer Saldean and his family chose to stay. Thieves are not the only danger on their farm. Harvest Watchers built to tend and guard the grain have run wild, pacing the furrows and attacking anyone who comes near.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Soil",b="Farmer Saldean asks passing travelers to dismantle twenty hostile Harvest Watchers across his fields and the adjoining plots. Clearing them gives his harvest a little relief. For now, his farm remains one stubborn hope that Westfall's breadbasket can be reclaimed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest The Killing Fields?",a="Farmer Saldean offers The Killing Fields from Saldean's Farm, along the road in central Westfall.",al={"quest giver killing fields","who gives the killing fields","saldean quest"},gp=true},{q="What are Harvest Watchers?",a="Harvest Watchers are clockwork scarecrows built to tend crops and guard fields from pests. After unrest and abandonment spread through Westfall, many were left untended or reprogrammed. Now they attack the farmers they were built to serve.",al={"what are harvest watchers","harvest watcher lore","mechanical scarecrows westfall"},it="target"},{q="Why has Farmer Saldean not fled Westfall like the others?",a="Farmer Saldean refuses to surrender his livelihood as his neighbors abandon their homesteads to thieves and brigands. He keeps his farm with help from hired adventurers who drive back the rogue machinery.",al={"why is saldean still here","farmer saldean lore","saldean staying"}},{q="What are the objectives of The Killing Fields?",a="You are asked to destroy twenty Harvest Watchers roaming Saldean's fields and the surrounding abandoned farms.",al={"killing fields objective","how many harvest watchers","what to kill for killing fields"},gp=true},{q="Who are the 'thieves' Saldean mentions?",a="Saldean means the thieves and brigands loosely organized under the Defias Brotherhood. Their raids and extortion drove most homesteaders from their land.",al={"who are the thieves","saldean thieves","who drove farmers out westfall"}},{q="Does completing this quest fix Westfall's farming troubles?",a="Destroying twenty Harvest Watchers gives Saldean's farm some immediate breathing room. The bandit threat and broken machinery across the wider region remain.",al={"does westfall recover","killing fields ending","saldean outcome"}},{q="Why does Farmer Saldean want the Harvest Watchers killed?",a="Farmer Saldean is one of the few homesteaders who refuses to abandon his land despite Westfall's collapse. The fields that once fed Stormwind have fallen into ruin, overgrown and overrun by rogue mechanical Harvest Watchers. Saldean wants these rogue automata destroyed so he and any remaining folk might stand a chance of reclaiming the soil and seeing Westfall prosper once again.",al={"why kill harvest watchers","saldean killing fields motive","farmer saldean reason"},it="motive",add="a141c1eb"},{q="Why does Farmer Saldean need an adventurer instead of handling the Harvest Watchers himself?",a="Saldean is merely an ordinary farmer trying to protect his home and family with no royal guards or soldiers in sight to help him. Stormwind's military presence in Westfall has dwindled, leaving the local farmers completely defenseless against armed thieves and deadly, malfunctioning farming constructs. Facing twenty Harvest Watchers alone would be suicide, making an armed adventurer his only hope.",al={"why cant saldean do it","why ask me killing fields","why does saldean need help"},it="why_me",add="05cf05c3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help protect one of the few food supplies still standing in a territory the Stormwind crown has abandoned.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can recognize the Harvest Watchers as clockwork wonders gone haywire without proper maintenance."},kw={"clockwork","defias","farmer saldean","harvest watchers","killing fields","saldean's farm","scarecrows","westfall"},rel={"npc:farmer-saldean","zone:westfall"},m={start="Farmer Saldean",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=9,ri={"Harvest Watcher"}},src={"The Killing Fields"}}
E["quest:92742"] = {t="quest",n="Testing the Wells",z="westfall",s="Across Westfall, Alba Fairmoon sends you to test the farm wells. Their samples may show what is poisoning the soil and groundwater.",h="Across Westfall, Alba Fairmoon sends you to test the farm wells.",sec={{t="Blight in the Aquifer",b="Alba Fairmoon asks you to test the water beneath Westfall. Neglect and banditry have already harmed the open plains. Now poison below the earth threatens the farmland that remains. You gather samples from farm wells so Alba can learn what is tainting the soil and water.",sp=0},{t="Farms of the Frontier",b="You gather samples from the wells at Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm. These homesteads lie among scattered farms, exposed to Defias outlaws and feral wildlife. Their water may show whether the blight rises from the ground, comes from magic, or was put there deliberately.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Testing the Wells?",a="Alba Fairmoon wants to learn the source and nature of the poison afflicting Westfall. Fresh samples from farm wells will let her examine the contamination.",al={"why test the wells","testing the wells goal","what is this quest for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who assigns this task?",a="Alba Fairmoon asks you to help as she investigates the spreading corruption and unnatural poisons in Westfall.",al={"who gives testing the wells","alba fairmoon quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Which locations need to be sampled?",a="You sample the wells at Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm in Westfall.",al={"where do i go","which wells","well locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is threatening Westfall's water and soil?",a="An unknown blight or poison is corrupting Westfall's land. Testing well water is the first step toward learning whether the water beneath the homesteads is tainted.",al={"why is westfall poisoned","what is poisoning the land","poison source"},it="threat"},{q="Is the contamination natural or artificial?",a="The cause is not yet known. Samples from Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm may show whether the rot comes from natural corruption in the groundwater or deliberate sabotage.",al={"is the water poisoned on purpose","who poisoned the wells"},it="origin"},{q="Why focus on Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm?",a="Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm are established homesteads with wells that draw from the underground water table across the plains. Testing them can show how far the corruption reaches.",al={"why jansen and molsen","why these farms"}},{q="Why does Alba Fairmoon want this done?",a="Alba Fairmoon is trying to uncover the source and exact nature of the poison currently corrupting Westfall's soil and groundwater. By analyzing water straight from the wells of working homesteads, she hopes to diagnose what is blighting the land before the contamination spreads beyond recovery.",al={"why does alba want water samples","alba fairmoon motive","why test the wells"},it="motive",add="40e3ab69"},{q="What is the Jansen Stead Water Sample for?",a="This sample provides Alba Fairmoon with groundwater drawn directly from the Jansen Stead. By examining it alongside other farm samples, she can trace whether the blight is permeating deep subterranean aquifers across Westfall or leaking from a specific localized contaminant.",al={"jansen stead water sample use","why get jansen stead water","jansen stead sample purpose"},it="item",add="d6dffc38"},{q="What is the Molsen Farm Water Sample for?",a="Drawn from the well at Molsen Farm, this water allows Alba Fairmoon to test the extent of the corruption across different pockets of Westfall's farmland. Comparing its purity against other local wells helps her gauge the path and intensity of the spreading poison.",al={"molsen farm water sample use","why collect molsen farm sample","molsen farm water purpose"},it="item",add="fcb7e3cb"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Westfall's farms must feed the Kingdom of Stormwind. The health of their wells concerns the whole kingdom.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know unnatural toxins in soil and fresh groundwater wound the land's balance and call for healing."},kw={"alba fairmoon","groundwater","jansen stead","molsen farm","poison","testing the wells","water sample","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:jansen-stead","subzone:molsen-farm"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=92742,ri={"Jansen Stead Water Sample","Molsen Farm Water Sample"}},src={"Testing the Wells"},fv=true}
E["quest:92744"] = {t="quest",n="Murloc Gills",z="westfall",s="At Westfall's Longshore, Alba Fairmoon seeks murloc gills to test the sea. She fears the crop blight may reach the Great Sea, and the gills could show whether the coastal waters are tainted.",h="At Westfall's Longshore, Alba Fairmoon seeks murloc gills to test the sea.",sec={{t="A Threat to the Coastline",b="Westfall is close to ruin. Crops fail, farmers leave their homes, and bandits roam the roads. Alba Fairmoon fears the blight may drain from inland fields into the Great Sea. If it taints the coast, fish that feed Westfall's poor and fill Stormwind City's tables could vanish. Then an already strained kingdom may face famine.",sp=0},{t="Sentinels of Water Quality",b="Murlocs are stubborn and violent, but their amphibious bodies can reveal the water's condition. As they breathe, their gills filter seawater and readily take in poisons, blight, and unnatural pollutants. Alba Fairmoon hopes fresh gills from murlocs prowling the Longshore will show how far the contamination has spread.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Alba Fairmoon want murloc gills?",a="Alba Fairmoon wants murloc gills to learn whether Westfall's crop blight has reached the ocean. Their gills filter seawater and can reveal traces of toxins or pollution.",al={"why murloc gills","alba fairmoon murlocs","purpose of quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the murlocs located for this task?",a="The murlocs prowl the Longshore, the beach along Westfall's western coast. They haunt the shallows and tidal flats beyond the bluffs.",al={"where are murlocs","longshore murloc location","murloc gill spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the broader danger if the ocean is corrupted?",a="Westfall is Stormwind's primary breadbasket, and its inland crops are already failing. Coastal fishing provides vital food. If toxins poison marine life along the shore, the kingdom could face famine with no escape.",al={"why does this matter","westfall famine danger","threat to stormwind"},it="threat"},{q="Are murlocs particularly prone to disease?",a="Murlocs survive harsh conditions, but their amphibious breathing systems react quickly to chemical or magical impurities in the water. That makes them useful for studying waterborne pollution.",al={"murloc physiology","do murlocs get sick"}},{q="Does this quest connect to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has brought chaos to Westfall and left farmland neglected. Alba Fairmoon's investigation instead examines ecological blight and the protection of the kingdom's food supply.",al={"defias connection","is this defias"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Alba Fairmoon?",a="Alba Fairmoon is an Alliance researcher in Westfall. She monitors the blight and environmental decline threatening the region's farmland.",al={"who is fairmoon","alba fairmoon lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Longshore Murloc Gill for?",a="Murlocs breathe through their gills while prowling the coastal waters, making their respiratory tissue sensitive to whatever pollutes the sea. Alba Fairmoon uses the gills as a biological test subject. By examining the tissue for toxins, she can determine whether the strange corruption withering Westfall's soil and crops has also begun poisoning the ocean.",al={"murloc gill use","why collect murloc gills","longshore murloc gills"},it="item",add="853673a8"},{q="Why are you hunting the Longshore murlocs?",a="The murlocs dwell along Westfall's western coast, constantly exposed to the tides and sea spray. Because their aquatic bodies filter coastal water directly through their gills, harvesting samples from them offers immediate biological proof of whether contaminants have leached from the troubled farmland out into the sea.",al={"why murlocs","who are the longshore murlocs","why target murlocs"},it="target",add="4abd0ea3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="With King Varian missing and food shortages stirring unrest, protecting Westfall's remaining food supply is vital to Stormwind's stability.",["class:Druid"]="Inland blight spreading into coastal waters threatens native wildlife. Watching indicator species such as murlocs helps guard against that danger.",["race:Human"]="For the people of Stormwind, Westfall's decline threatens their homes, farmland, and dinner tables."},kw={"alba fairmoon","blight","famine","longshore","murloc gills","seawater","stormwind","toxins","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:longshore","topic:murloc","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=92744,ri={"Longshore Murloc Gill"}},src={"Murloc Gills"},fv=true}
E["quest:92745"] = {t="quest",n="The State of the Mines",z="westfall",s="Toxic metals are turning up in Westfall's wells, and Alba Fairmoon fears for the farmland. She suspects the Defias mines and warns that the soil could fail for decades. You head to Jangolode Mine and Gold Coast Quarry to disrupt the mining.",h="Toxic metals are turning up in Westfall's wells, and Alba Fairmoon fears for the farmland.",sec={{t="Poisoning the Land",b="Alba Fairmoon finds dangerous levels of toxic metals in Westfall's wells. Once Stormwind's main breadbasket, the region now faces a threat to its crops. Alba suspects the Defias Brotherhood is poisoning the water through the mines it seized. If the contamination continues, the surrounding earth could lie barren for decades.",sp=0},{t="Forced and Enlisted Labor",b="The Defias put local creatures to work alongside their highwaymen, stripping Westfall of its resources. Riverpaw gnolls dig for stone and minerals at Gold Coast Quarry, while kobold diggers tunnel through Jangolode Mine. Disrupting their labor weakens the Defias' ability to process and distribute contaminated minerals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the mines of Westfall leaking toxic metals?",a="Alba Fairmoon suspects the mines seized by the Defias Brotherhood are contaminating Westfall's groundwater with toxic metals. She wants to disrupt their miners to stop the pollution.",al={"why toxic water westfall","westfall mine pollution","toxic runoff westfall"},it="motive"},{q="Who is behind the mining operations in Westfall?",a="The Defias Brotherhood controls Westfall's mining operations. They seized former kingdom infrastructure and set Riverpaw gnolls and kobolds to extract minerals.",al={"who runs the mines","who controls westfall mines","defias mining"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the Riverpaw gnolls and kobolds working?",a="Riverpaw gnolls work at Gold Coast Quarry along Westfall's western shores, while kobold diggers work inside Jangolode Mine to the north.",al={"where are the miners","gold coast quarry location","jangolode mine location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Alba Fairmoon?",a="Alba Fairmoon investigates Westfall's water and seeks to protect the region's farmland from lasting damage.",al={"who gives state of the mines","alba fairmoon lore","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why are gnolls and kobolds working for the Defias?",a="The Defias use gnolls and kobolds as labor in the seized mines. Alba does not say how the workers were recruited.",al={"why defias hire gnolls","kobolds working for defias"},it="ties"},{q="Can the land in Westfall recover from this contamination?",a="Alba Fairmoon says the soil can recover if the source of the toxicity is cut off quickly. If mining continues, the earth could remain infertile and blighted for decades.",al={"will westfall soil heal","can crops grow again"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Alba Fairmoon want the miners killed?",a="Water samples from the local wells revealed dangerous toxic metals seeping into Westfall's soil. Alba Fairmoon knows that unless the aggressive strip-mining is halted immediately, the environmental poison will linger, leaving the region barren and incapable of growing crops for decades.",al={"why kill the miners","alba fairmoon motive","why stop the mining"},it="motive",add="f9d72c87"},{q="Who are the miners in the Jangolode Mine and Gold Coast Quarry?",a="You are sent against the Kobold Diggers in the Jangolode Mine and the Riverpaw Miners in the Gold Coast Quarry. Rather than working for themselves, these creatures are used as labor by the Defias Brotherhood, who seized the mines to ruthlessly strip Westfall of its mineral wealth.",al={"who are the miners","who are you sent to kill","kobold diggers riverpaw miners"},it="target",add="23ba5f2a"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="At Jangolode Mine and Gold Coast Quarry, the Defias extract minerals with little regard for safety or the mines' structural integrity.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you face an urgent threat from metallic poisons seeping into Westfall's plains and coastal ecosystems.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Westfall helps feed Stormwind. If the Defias ruin its farmland, the kingdom could face famine for years."},kw={"alba fairmoon","defias","gold coast quarry","jangolode mine","kobold digger","mining","riverpaw","toxic runoff","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:jangolode-mine","subzone:gold-coast-quarry","topic:kobold"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=92745},src={"The State of the Mines"},fv=true}
E["quest:92747"] = {t="quest",n="Moonbrook Espionage",z="westfall",s="In Moonbrook, Alba Fairmoon follows signs of industry trouble in Westfall. The poison found across the region does not seem to come from the smaller mines, so the Deadmines beneath the town draw her attention.",h="In Moonbrook, Alba Fairmoon follows signs of industry trouble in Westfall.",sec={{t="A Toxic Trail",b="The mines already searched across Westfall have yielded no answer to the poison spreading through the region. No known surface excavation seems to be its source. One great site remains unexplored: the Deadmines, whose vast shafts lie beneath Moonbrook’s ruined streets.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Deadmines",b="The Horde overran the region during the First War, and accounts say the Deadmines were abandoned afterward. Yet modern industrial gear and supplies lie scattered through Moonbrook. They point to extensive mining and manufacturing hidden behind the town’s ruined, empty appearance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who assigns Moonbrook Espionage?",a="Alba Fairmoon sends you to investigate Moonbrook. She has been looking into suspicious toxins and industrial activity across contested Westfall.",al={"quest giver","who gives moonbrook espionage","alba fairmoon"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Alba investigating Moonbrook?",a="The other local mines show no sign of producing the poison Alba is investigating. Moonbrook lies directly above the Deadmines, so she suspects an illicit operation beneath the town.",al={"why moonbrook","what is in moonbrook","investigate moonbrook"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Deadmines?",a="The Deadmines are the region’s deepest and most expansive gold mines. They have been considered empty ruins since Stormwind fell in the First War, though vermin and bandits are said to haunt them.",al={"deadmines lore","what are deadmines","history of deadmines"},it="place"},{q="What items are gathered during this scouting mission?",a="Scouts are sent to retrieve Suspicious Industrial Supplies scattered through Moonbrook. The supplies point to active industrial work and refining near the mine shafts.",al={"suspicious industrial supplies","quest items moonbrook espionage"},it="item"},{q="What threats occupy Moonbrook right now?",a="The Defias Brotherhood overran Moonbrook and uses its derelict buildings as a forward staging ground. They guard the surface entrance to the underground network.",al={"moonbrook enemies","who controls moonbrook"},it="threat"},{q="What does finding these supplies prove?",a="Modern, heavy industrial equipment in a town believed abandoned points to a coordinated faction carrying out large-scale fabrication beyond Stormwind’s authorities’ sight.",al={"what do the supplies mean","defias industry"},it="purpose"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can slip through Moonbrook to gather intelligence on Defias operations without raising the alarm.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the wealth and logistical scale of the deep shafts beneath Moonbrook.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know active industry in Moonbrook threatens Westfall’s breadbasket and Stormwind’s security."},kw={"alba fairmoon","deadmines","espionage","industrial supplies","mines","moonbrook","poison","westfall"},rel={"subzone:moonbrook","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","zone:westfall","topic:first-war"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92747,ri={"Suspicious Industrial Supplies"}},src={"Moonbrook Espionage"},fv=true}
E["quest:92748"] = {t="quest",n="Explosive Consultation",z="westfall",s="Alba Fairmoon sends you to find a way to stop the poison spreading from the Deadmines into Westfall's fields. In Stormwind's Dwarven District, you seek an engineer who can make the heavy explosives the work requires.",h="Alba Fairmoon sends you to find a way to stop the poison spreading from the Deadmines into Westfall's fields.",sec={{t="A Toxic Source",b="Westfall's poisoned fields lead back to caustic toxins and industrial refuse in the Deadmines. Reinforced machinery guards the underground works, and ordinary weapons cannot disable it. Heavy explosives could break through that machinery and halt the poisoning.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Stormwind's Expertise",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, you seek Sprite Jumpsprocket, an engineer able to devise the needed explosives. Roaring forges, tinkerers, and merchants selling blasting powder fill the district. Its craftsmen may know how to stop the Deadmines operation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do we need explosives in the Deadmines?",a="Evidence from Westfall points to a large industrial operation in the Deadmines, where toxins foul nearby farmland. Heavy explosives can disable its reinforced machinery.",al={"why explosives deadmines","why do we need bombs","deadmines toxins reason"},it="purpose"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Alba Fairmoon sends heroes to investigate the unnatural contaminants and unrest threatening Westfall.",al={"who gives explosive consultation","explosive consultation start"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Sprite Jumpsprocket?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is a gnome engineer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. She works with complex mechanical devices and volatile compounds, and can craft powerful demolitions.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket location","who is jumpsprocket"},it="people"},{q="Why travel to the Dwarven District for help?",a="Stormwind's Dwarven District is the city's industrial heart. Skilled blacksmiths and tinkerers work there, alongside sellers of blasting powder and engineering components.",al={"why dwarven district","stormwind dwarven district connection"},it="place"},{q="Does Stormwind's government assist with this effort?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the House of Nobles is reluctant to send formal military garrisons to Westfall. Local defenders rely on independent volunteers and private craftsmen in the capital rather than regular army regiments.",al={"does the army help","why stormwind engineer"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Alba Fairmoon want you to seek out explosives?",a="Alba Fairmoon has uncovered evidence of a massive industrial operation hidden deep within the Deadmines. She has connected this subterranean machinery directly to the foul toxins poisoning the soil and blighting the farmlands above. Knowing that an operation of this scale cannot simply be dismantled by hand, she wants heavy explosives to obliterate whatever foul machinery is polluting the countryside before the damage becomes irreversible.",al={"why alba fairmoon explosives","alba fairmoon motive","why need explosives alba"},it="motive",add="fe11cddb"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know brute force cannot solve Westfall's poisoned-land troubles. Disabling large underground machinery calls for specialized munitions and careful technical skill.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you bring technological ingenuity that can help counter underground industrial threats beyond the reach of regular Alliance forces.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Westfall's struggling frontier communities rely on the workshops of Stormwind's Dwarven District."},kw={"alba fairmoon","deadmines","dwarven district","engineering","explosive consultation","sprite jumpsprocket","stormwind","toxins","westfall"},rel={"npc:sprite-jumpsprocket","zone:westfall","subzone:dwarven-district","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",["end"]="Sprite Jumpsprocket",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92748},src={"Explosive Consultation"},fv=true}
E["quest:92749"] = {t="quest",n="A Dynamite Plan",z="westfall",s="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Sprite Jumpsprocket is eager to begin a plan sparked by talk of industrial sabotage. She wants ten sticks of coarse dynamite.",h="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Sprite Jumpsprocket is eager to begin a plan sparked by talk of industrial...",sec={{t="Sparks in the Dwarven District",b="Sprite Jumpsprocket is a gnome engineer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. She welcomes talk of industrial sabotage and asks passing mercenaries to bring her a bundle of coarse dynamite.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Ambitions",b="You can make coarse dynamite at an engineering workbench or trade with the city's craftsmen. Sprite asks for ten sticks, enough to disrupt industrial schemes unfolding in the surrounding territories. Her plan shows the practical, perilous methods gnomes favor when facing mechanical and political disruptions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sprite Jumpsprocket?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is an engineer in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, among its smithies and workshops. She pursues bold, volatile engineering projects.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket","who is sprite","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What does Sprite need for this task?",a="Sprite needs ten sticks of coarse dynamite. You can make them with engineering or acquire them through trade or the auction house.",al={"dynamite plan items","what do i need","items needed"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sprite want coarse dynamite?",a="Talk of industrial sabotage has caught Sprite's attention. She wants a stock of basic blasting charges to begin.",al={"why dynamite","dynamite purpose","sabotage motive"},it="motive"},{q="Where do I turn in the quest?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"where to turn in","hand in location","sprite location"},gp=true},{q="Is engineering required to complete this quest?",a="No, engineering is not required. Engineers can make coarse dynamite, and you can also trade for it or buy it at the auction house.",al={"do i need engineering","engineering requirement","can non engineers do this"},gp=true},{q="How does this relate to broader troubles around Stormwind?",a="Sprite does not say what her sabotage targets. She only shows eagerness to begin with dynamite when industrial sabotage comes up.",al={"stormwind troubles","westfall sabotage","industrial sabotage lore"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Coarse Dynamite for?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is eager to engage in a bit of industrial sabotage, and explosive power is central to that scheme. Coarse Dynamite provides the raw concussive force she requires to disrupt mechanical operations or clear structural obstacles for her upcoming undertaking.",al={"coarse dynamite use","what does sprite need dynamite for","why coarse dynamite"},it="item",add="dd094caa"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can make coarse dynamite from coarse blasting powder and linen cloth. It is a straightforward test of early tinkercraft.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see Sprite Jumpsprocket meet complicated industrial problems with clever, combustible contraptions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find Sprite's explosive scheme inside the walls of your capital, Stormwind."},kw={"coarse dynamite","dwarven district","engineering","explosives","sabotage","sprite jumpsprocket","stormwind"},rel={"npc:sprite-jumpsprocket","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:westfall"},m={start="Sprite Jumpsprocket",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92749,ri={"Coarse Dynamite"}},src={"A Dynamite Plan"},fv=true}
E["quest:92750"] = {t="quest",n="Detonation at a Distance",z="westfall",s="Sprite Jumpsprocket needs a safer way to set off explosives, and sends you to Stormwind Intelligence for a remote detonator.",h="Sprite Jumpsprocket needs a safer way to set off explosives, and sends you to Stormwind Intelligence for a...",sec={{t="A Controlled Blast",b="Volatile chemicals are handled recklessly by goblins and gnomes, though some blasts call for care. A standard fuse can put you in danger. Ordinary tinkerers do not keep the special trigger Sprite needs for a controlled explosion.",sp=0},{t="Calling Upon the SI:7",b="Sprite sends you to Stormwind Intelligence in Old Town, rather than to local dwarven blasters or ordinary engineering suppliers. Its agents, known as SI:7, work in sabotage, stealth, and targeted demolitions. Jasper Fel serves among them in the capital and can provide discreet, dangerous equipment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this mission?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket, a gnome tinkerer in Stormwind's Dwarven District, sends you to find a remote detonator.",al={"quest giver","who starts detonation at a distance","sprite jumpsprocket quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who do you need to talk to in Stormwind?",a="Sprite sends you to Jasper Fel, an associate of Stormwind Intelligence in Stormwind.",al={"where to turn in","stormwind intelligence contact","jasper fel location"},it="target"},{q="Why does Sprite Jumpsprocket need a remote detonator?",a="Sprite wants to set off explosives from a distance. A remote trigger is more practical than risking your limbs in an uncontrolled blast.",al={"why remote detonator","purpose of detonation"},it="motive"},{q="Why contact Stormwind Intelligence rather than an engineer?",a="Stormwind Intelligence keeps specialized sabotage gear that ordinary merchants and field tinkerers do not stock or distribute openly.",al={"why si7","why stormwind intelligence"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Jasper Fel located in Stormwind?",a="Jasper Fel is at SI:7 headquarters in Old Town, where Stormwind's spies and covert agents work.",al={"jasper fel stormwind","jasper fel room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction can undertake this task?",a="Only members of the Alliance can undertake this work. It depends on cooperation with Stormwind's royal intelligence division.",al={"is this alliance only","can horde do this"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Sprite Jumpsprocket send you to SI:7 instead of going herself?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket doesn't have a remote detonator herself. Since you want a controlled blast that keeps your limbs intact, she points you to the sneaky folks at Stormwind Intelligence, who she trusts can find one. The quest doesn't say why she doesn't go herself.",al={"why me sprite jumpsprocket","why send player to si:7","why can't sprite go to stormwind"},it="why_me",add="be1ed035"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the heart of SI:7 operations in Old Town, where human covert tradecraft is practiced.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can build fuses and dynamite. Military-grade remote triggers often come through contacts who specialize in quiet sabotage.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you share Sprite Jumpsprocket's interest in engineering problems. She turns to human intelligence for spycraft munitions."},kw={"detonation at a distance","jasper fel","remote detonator","si:7","sprite jumpsprocket","stormwind intelligence","westfall"},rel={"npc:sprite-jumpsprocket","npc:jasper-fel","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Sprite Jumpsprocket",["end"]="Jasper Fel",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92750},src={"Detonation at a Distance"},fv=true}
E["quest:92751"] = {t="quest",n="Detonation at a Distance",z="westfall",s="In Moonbrook, blasts beneath Westfall have drawn SI:7's attention. Jasper Fel, a Stormwind operative, sends a remote detonator kit to let you handle the work from a safe distance.",h="In Moonbrook, blasts beneath Westfall have drawn SI:7's attention.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Jasper Fel and SI:7 watch events across Stormwind's lands, including Westfall's troubled border. When word reaches him of explosive work in Moonbrook, Fel already knows what is happening in the abandoned mining tunnels beneath the countryside.",sp=0},{t="A Prototype Solution",b="Explosions in tight caves endanger anyone nearby. Jasper Fel gives you a prototype Remote Detonator Kit made by Alliance-aligned engineers. It lets charges beneath Westfall be set off from outside. He sends you with the kit to Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind's Dwarven District and warns you not to mention SI:7 to your elven allies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jasper Fel?",a="Jasper Fel is an operative with Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7. He watches covert threats across the kingdom and supplies tools to deal with them.",al={"jasper fel","who gives detonation at a distance","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does SI:7 care about Moonbrook?",a="Bandits and outlaws hold Moonbrook, whose surface leads into the Deadmines. Demolition deep beneath Westfall has caught Stormwind's intelligence network's attention.",al={"why moonbrook","defias connection","westfall caves"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Sprite Jumpsprocket?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket is a gnome engineer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. She is preparing explosives for the demolition.",al={"sprite jumpsprocket","who receives the detonator","turn in npc"},it="identity"},{q="Who is the 'elf friend' Jasper Fel mentions?",a="Jasper Fel means Alba Fairmoon, the elf investigating Westfall's poison who sent you to find explosives. SI:7 keeps its direct support hidden from outside allies.",al={"elf friend","dont tell elf","jasper fel elf"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Remote Detonator Kit used for?",a="The Remote Detonator Kit triggers demolition charges from a safe distance. It lets operatives clear or collapse underground passages without being trapped inside.",al={"remote detonator","detonator kit","what does the kit do"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest take you?",a="You carry the detonator kit to Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"where do i go","quest route","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Jasper Fel helping with the remote detonator?",a="Jasper Fel offers an advanced prototype detonator kit for Sprite. He asks you to keep his involvement from your elf friend while helping with the planned demolition.",al={"jasper fel motive","why help with detonator","why does jasper fel give the kit"},it="motive",add="dd5ef9f7"},{q="Why does Jasper Fel ask you instead of handling it himself?",a="Jasper Fel entrusts you with the prototype detonator kit for Sprite, while asking you to keep his involvement from your elf friend. He does not explain why he cannot deliver it personally.",al={"why send me","why doesn't jasper fel deliver it","why not si7 agents"},it="why_me",add="2c859344"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, your meeting with Jasper Fel gives you a glimpse of SI:7's covert network. It watches field operatives and quietly supplies them with tools.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Sprite Jumpsprocket's work shows how gnome engineering supplies Stormwind's spies with prototypes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind trying to reclaim Westfall through covert engineering and intelligence rather than open military force.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate a prototype detonator that sets off charges from afar, avoiding risky manual fuses in cave demolitions."},kw={"deadmines","dwarven district","jasper fel","moonbrook","remote detonator","si:7","sprite jumpsprocket","westfall"},rel={"npc:jasper-fel","npc:sprite-jumpsprocket","quest:2300","subzone:dwarven-district","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Jasper Fel",["end"]="Sprite Jumpsprocket",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92751},src={"Detonation at a Distance (2)"},fv=true}
E["quest:92752"] = {t="quest",n="Explosive Consultation",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Sprite Jumpsprocket sends a volatile charge to Alba Fairmoon. The primed explosives must reach her safely, with the detonator undisturbed.",h="In Westfall, Sprite Jumpsprocket sends a volatile charge to Alba Fairmoon.",sec={{t="A Volatile Delivery",b="Sprite Jumpsprocket has finished a bundle of Extra-Destructive Explosives for Alba Fairmoon. In wartime Westfall, the road is already threatened by Defias bandits and feral beasts. Carrying a live charge makes the journey more dangerous.",sp=0},{t="Handling with Care",b="Sprite Jumpsprocket warns you to guard the detonator. The explosives are meant to destroy the hidden industrial operation in the Deadmines, which is poisoning Westfall's farmland. Alba Fairmoon needs the explosives intact before she can use them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Explosive Consultation?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket, a gnome tinkerer in Stormwind's Dwarven District, gives you the explosives to carry.",al={"who gives explosive consultation","quest giver explosive consultation","sprite jumpsprocket quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Who receives the explosives at the end of the quest?",a="Alba Fairmoon in Westfall receives the Extra-Destructive Explosives.",al={"where do i take the explosives","who turns in explosive consultation","alba fairmoon explosive"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What item are you tasked with transporting?",a="You carry a package of Extra-Destructive Explosives with a primed, delicate detonator.",al={"what is sprite handing over","explosive consultation item","what bomb is this"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why are explosives needed in Westfall?",a="Alba Fairmoon traced the toxins poisoning Westfall's farmland to a massive industrial operation hidden in the Deadmines. She sought an engineer to supply explosives capable of destroying it.",al={"why do they need bombs","westfall explosives purpose","why blow things up in westfall"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest available to Horde adventurers?",a="No. Sprite Jumpsprocket and Alba Fairmoon support Alliance operations, so only Alliance adventurers can take this on.",al={"can horde do explosive consultation","horde explosive consultation"},gp=true},{q="Does Sprite Jumpsprocket warn you about any specific danger?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket warns that the bomb is primed and tells you to handle the detonator with extreme care on the journey.",al={"sprite warning","bomb warning westfall"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Sprite Jumpsprocket want the explosives delivered to Alba?",a="Sprite Jumpsprocket has finished assembling the extra-destructive explosives commissioned for Alba Fairmoon's efforts in Westfall. Having crafted the perilous payload, Sprite needs an adventurer to handle the delicate, hazardous transport back to Alba so the bomb can be put to work as intended.",al={"why deliver explosives alba","sprite jumpsprocket motive","why did sprite make bomb"},it="motive",add="bb434565"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know gnomish ordnance brings high yield and a hair-trigger detonator.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see Sprite Jumpsprocket bring Gnomeregan's explosive solutions to Westfall's troubled front.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you see operatives across Westfall use unconventional arms against entrenched bandit camps and rogue machinery."},kw={"alba fairmoon","detonator","explosive consultation","explosives","gnome engineering","sprite jumpsprocket","westfall"},rel={"npc:sprite-jumpsprocket","zone:westfall"},m={start="Sprite Jumpsprocket",["end"]="Alba Fairmoon",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=92752},src={"Explosive Consultation (2)"},fv=true}
E["quest:92753"] = {t="quest",n="Destruction in Deadmines",z="westfall",s="In the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, Defias industry blights the land. Alba Fairmoon suspects their metallurgical forge is the source and sends you to destroy it with explosives.",h="In the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, Defias industry blights the land.",sec={{t="Sabotaging the Foundry",b="Beneath Moonbrook, the Deadmines hold a fortified complex that powers the Defias Brotherhood. Its heavy forge smelts metal and builds machinery. Alba Fairmoon believes the forge is the likely origin of the contamination blighting the area. She wants it destroyed.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Blast",b="Beyond barricades, cutthroats, and goblin engineers, the forge waits. You carry Extra-Destructive Explosives and plant them beside the forge works. Then you escape to the hills above Moonbrook. Alba Fairmoon waits there to detonate the charge, hoping the land can begin to heal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this mission?",a="You are to enter the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, find the Defias Brotherhood's metallurgical forge, and plant Extra-Destructive Explosives nearby. Alba Fairmoon waits at the exit.",al={"quest objective","what do i do","what is destruction in deadmines"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Alba Fairmoon?",a="Alba Fairmoon is an Alliance operative in Westfall. She believes the blight and poison in the region come from heavy smelting and industrial work inside the Deadmines.",al={"who is alba","alba fairmoon lore","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Defias forge considered so dangerous?",a="Alba suspects the large metallurgical forge in the Deadmines is the source of the poison. She hopes destroying it will let the land begin to heal.",al={"why destroy the forge","what does the forge do","forge poison"},it="danger"},{q="Where does the player meet Alba after planting the explosives?",a="Alba Fairmoon waits in the hills behind Moonbrook, outside the Deadmines near the mine's upper exit. She is ready to trigger the explosives once you emerge safely.",al={"where is alba waiting","deadmines exit location","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is the forge located inside the Deadmines?",a="The forge lies deep inside the Deadmines, past the mining tunnels in the industrial foundry, where Defias laborers and goblin overseers work.",al={"where is the forge","forge location deadmines","find the forge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does destroying the forge heal the land immediately?",a="Alba hopes ending the heavy smelting will let the land around Moonbrook recover. Years of Defias industry and neglect will take time to wash away.",al={"will the land heal","does the poison stop","forge aftermath"}},{q="Why does Alba Fairmoon want the forge destroyed?",a="Alba believes the Defias forge deep inside the Deadmines is the true source of the foul pollution seeping into the surrounding earth. By planting explosives and shattering the massive smelting operation, she hopes to cut off the blight at its root so Westfall's wounded soil can finally begin to recover.",al={"alba fairmoon motive","why destroy deadmines forge","why does alba want this done"},it="motive",add="cfdfebff"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Alba Fairmoon proposes using specialized Extra-Destructive Explosives against heavy industrial works to remove the suspected source of contamination.",["profession:Mining"]="The Deadmines were once Stormwind's richest gold and iron mines. The Defias have turned them into a fortified smelting complex that blights the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Destroying the Defias forge strikes at the machinery and weapons threatening Stormwind's sovereignty from within Westfall."},kw={"alba fairmoon","deadmines","defias brotherhood","extra-destructive explosives","metallurgical forge","moonbrook","sabotage","westfall"},rel={"subzone:deadmines","zone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=92753},src={"Destruction in Deadmines"},fv=true}
E["quest:92819"] = {t="quest",n="Destruction in Deadmines",z="westfall",s="Alba Fairmoon sends you against the Defias forge beneath Westfall. The explosives are planted, and she waits in the hills behind Moonbrook with the detonator.",h="Alba Fairmoon sends you against the Defias forge beneath Westfall.",sec={{t="Sabotage Beneath Westfall",b="Beneath Westfall, the Deadmines hold the Defias Brotherhood's strength. Alba Fairmoon sends you to sabotage the forge hidden in the mines. The explosives are planted beside it. You return to Alba in the hills behind Moonbrook, where you can set them off from a safe distance. She hopes the blast will let Westfall's poisoned land begin to heal.",sp=0},{t="The Detonator",b="Deep in the Deadmines, the charge waits beside the forge. After you rejoin Alba Fairmoon in the hills behind Moonbrook, a remote detonator lets you set it off from outside the caves. She hopes the destroyed forge will let Westfall's poisoned land begin to heal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Destruction in Deadmines?",a="Alba Fairmoon, an operative in Westfall, sends you against the Defias Brotherhood's stronghold.",al={"who gives destruction in deadmines","quest giver deadmines detonation","alba fairmoon quest"},it="identity"},{q="What is the primary objective of this mission?",a="You set off the explosives planted beside the Defias forge in the Deadmines. Rejoin Alba Fairmoon, then use the detonator from outside the mines.",al={"what do i do in destruction in deadmines","destruction in deadmines goal","how to complete destruction in deadmines"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why target the Deadmines with explosives?",a="Alba Fairmoon traced the poison in Westfall's farmland to a large metallurgical forge hidden in the Deadmines. She hopes its destruction will let the land begin to heal.",al={"why blow up deadmines","deadmines sabotage lore","why use detonator in deadmines"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="After the explosives are planted, you return to Alba Fairmoon in the hills behind Moonbrook, outside the Deadmines.",al={"destruction in deadmines location","where is destruction in deadmines","deadmines detonator location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this mission available to Horde players?",a="No. Alba Fairmoon works with Alliance operatives defending Westfall against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"is destruction in deadmines alliance only","can horde do destruction in deadmines"},gp=true},{q="What threat does the Defias Brotherhood pose in Westfall?",a="The Defias Brotherhood drove out farmers, raided settlements, and seized Westfall's abandoned mines. From deep in the Deadmines, they are building an armed insurrection that threatens the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"defias lore westfall","why fight defias","what are defias doing in deadmines"},it="threat"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Demolition and remote detonators lie at the heart of this assignment, a craft that may appeal to engineers.",["class:Rogue"]="You infiltrate enemy territory, plant charges, then slip away before the blast in an act of covert sabotage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, every blow against the Defias stronghold helps safeguard Westfall's struggling farmsteads and Stormwind's southern border."},kw={"alba fairmoon","deadmines","defias","destruction in deadmines","detonator","explosives","sabotage","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall"},m={start="Alba Fairmoon",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=92819},src={"Destruction in Deadmines (2)"},fv=true}
E["subzone:alexston-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Alexston Farmstead",z="westfall",s="Wild Harvest Watchers prowl the ruined fields at Alexston Farmstead. Baros Alexston grew up here before becoming Stormwind's city architect.",h="Wild Harvest Watchers prowl the ruined fields at Alexston Farmstead.",sec={{t="A Fallen Homestead",b="You find Alexston Farmstead among Westfall's dry plains, abandoned like the neighboring estates. Its caretakers fled as banditry spread across the countryside. The fields have gone wild, and Harvest Watchers left to tend the crops now attack anyone near the barren farmhouse.",sp=0},{t="Humble Roots",b="Baros Alexston worked these fields in his youth, then left to pursue masonry and construction. He became one of Stormwind's most prominent citizens and helped design parts of the rebuilt capital. Something from his early life remains among the ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns the Alexston Farmstead?",a="The Alexston family gives the farmstead its name. Baros Alexston worked this land as a boy before moving to Stormwind to pursue architecture.",al={"who owns this farm","alexston owner","whose farm is this"},it="name"},{q="Why is the farm abandoned?",a="Like much of Westfall, the farmstead was abandoned after widespread unrest and Defias Brotherhood banditry. Unable to protect them, the kingdom left farmers to flee and the homestead to decay.",al={"why abandoned","what happened to alexston farm","who ruined the farm"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are mechanical scarecrows attacking people here?",a="The Harvest Watchers were built to work the soil and guard crops from scavengers. When the farmers fled, the machines went without maintenance and their clockwork failed. Now they attack living creatures.",al={"why harvest watchers attack","hostile scarecrows","harvest golems hostile"}},{q="Is there anything hidden inside the farmhouse?",a="Baros Alexston left his personal compass in the farmhouse during his youth. Travelers working in Stormwind City are sometimes asked to retrieve it from the abandoned homestead.",al={"quest here","loot in farm","baros item"},gp=true},{q="What is Alexston Farmstead?",a="Alexston Farmstead is an abandoned rural farm located in northern Westfall. Like many surrounding homesteads in the province, it once contributed to feeding the kingdom of Stormwind before lawlessness swept through the region. It is also notable as the childhood home of Baros Alexston, who worked these very fields as a young boy before rising to become the City Architect of Stormwind.",al={"what is this place","alexston farm","about alexston farmstead"},it="place",add="3df1ed7f"},{q="What happened at Alexston Farmstead?",a="Once a peaceful and productive family farm, the land fell victim to the troubles plaguing Westfall. As the Defias Brotherhood took control of the countryside, the farm was seized and the residents were displaced. Over time, the living workers were replaced by rogue Harvest Watchers, leaving the farm desolate and overgrown while its fields remain under hostile control.",al={"alexston farmstead history","history of alexston farmstead","what happened here"},it="history",add="10e8b118"},{q="Is Alexston Farmstead dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers should tread carefully around the property. The fields are patrolled by deadly mechanical Harvest Watchers, rogue automatons that attack anyone who approaches. In addition, the Defias Brotherhood maintains an active and hostile presence throughout the region, making the ruined farmstead unsafe for unwary wanderers.",al={"is it dangerous here","threats at alexston farmstead","alexston farm monsters"},it="danger",add="6ef1debd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the farm recalls the humble, hardworking beginnings of Stormwind's finest minds and the struggle to protect its borders."},kw={"alexston","architect","baros","compass","farmstead","harvest watcher","westfall"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","quest:399","zone:westfall","zone:stormwind","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Alexston Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:dagger-hills"] = {t="subzone",n="Dagger Hills",z="westfall",s="Bandits hold Dagger Hills, the rocky heights behind Moonbrook in southern Westfall. With royal patrols gone, the ridge threatens travelers and the plains below.",h="Bandits hold Dagger Hills, the rocky heights behind Moonbrook in southern Westfall.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven",b="The Defias Brotherhood uses this dry highland as a stronghold. Knuckledusters, pathstalkers and highwaymen hide among the crests and scrub. They ambush unwary travelers and watch the approaches to their strongholds below, keeping the surrounding plains under threat.",sp=0},{t="Shadows on the Ridge",b="Darkness brings danger to Dagger Hills. After sunset, Leprithus, a wandering ghoul, has been seen stalking the desolate heights. Outlaws and lingering undead roam the ridge. Nearby, Grimbooze Thunderbrew, a dwarven brewer, sets up his distilling equipment despite the dangers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dagger Hills located?",a="Dagger Hills forms Westfall’s rocky southern border, directly behind Moonbrook.",al={"dagger hills location","where is dagger hills","how to get to dagger hills"},it="place"},{q="Who controls the Dagger Hills?",a="The Defias Brotherhood holds much of the ridge. Highwaymen, pathstalkers and knuckledusters guard the southern hills.",al={"dagger hills defias","who lives in dagger hills","enemies in dagger hills"},it="residents"},{q="Why is a dwarf brewing ale out here?",a="Grimbooze Thunderbrew distills potent dwarven brews in the lonely heights, braving bandits and beasts for good drink.",al={"grimbooze westfall","dwarf in dagger hills","grimbooze thunderbrew lore"}},{q="What is Leprithus?",a="Leprithus is an infamous ghoul roaming the Dagger Hills crags. It frightens travelers and bandits who meet it in the dark.",al={"leprithus spawn","ghoul in dagger hills","dagger hills undead"}},{q="What makes the Dagger Hills dangerous?",a="The rugged ridge looms directly behind Moonbrook, crawling with armed Defias Brotherhood rogues, highwaymen, and knuckledusters who use the high ground to watch the lowlands. Beyond the bandit patrols, the restless undead ghoul Leprithus is known to stalk the desolate heights, making travel through these crags hazardous for any solitary traveler.",al={"dagger hills danger","is dagger hills dangerous","what is dangerous about dagger hills"},it="danger",add="7ebc9df0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The hills show how law has broken down in southern Westfall. Gryan Stoutmantle’s People’s Militia must fight to reclaim ground Stormwind left behind.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Grimbooze Thunderbrew’s solitary presence on this exposed ridge. Brewers seek undisturbed space for their craft with stubborn resolve."},kw={"dagger hills","defias","grimbooze","leprithus","moonbrook","thunderbrew","westfall"},rel={"subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","npc:grimbooze-thunderbrew","quest:12","quest:117"},src={"Dagger Hills"}}
E["subzone:dead-acre"] = {t="subzone",n="Dead Acre",z="westfall",s="In southeastern Westfall, Dead Acre lies burned and abandoned near the bridge to Duskwood. The Defias Brotherhood torched the farm during its uprising, and rogue harvest golems still stalk the blackened fields.",h="In southeastern Westfall, Dead Acre lies burned and abandoned near the bridge to Duskwood.",sec={{t="Ashes on the Border",b="North of the road from Sentinel Hill to Duskwood, Dead Acre stands among Westfall’s old breadbasket farms. The homestead once gave good harvests, until the Defias Brotherhood rose in revolt and drove out the landowners. Then farm and crops went up in flames. Scorched timber and smoking earth remain, while mechanical Harvest Watchers still reap the barren soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called the Dead Acre?",a="The Defias Brotherhood burned the farmstead and fields when they took control of Westfall. Blackened ruins and smoldering earth gave the farm its grim name.",al={"why dead acre","what happened to dead acre","why is it burned"},it="name"},{q="Why are mechanical Harvest Watchers wandering here?",a="Mechanical reapers once tended Westfall’s crops, but settlers fled or died and left them behind. Without caretakers, or corrupted, the Harvest Watchers still patrol the burned fields and attack anyone who comes near.",al={"harvest golems dead acre","why are there golems","harvest watchers"}},{q="Where is the Dead Acre located?",a="Dead Acre lies in southeastern Westfall, just north of the main road near the bridge into Duskwood.",al={"dead acre location","where is dead acre","how to find dead acre"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Dead Acre?",a="The Dead Acre is a ruined, smoldering former farmstead in southeastern Westfall, located near the river bridge leading across into Duskwood. What was once fertile farmland has been reduced to blackened earth and scorched wreckage.",al={"what is dead acre","dead acre westfall","dead acre lore"},it="place",add="6eb41297"},{q="What happened to the Dead Acre?",a="When the Defias Brotherhood seized control across Westfall, their raiders put this farmstead and its fields to the torch. The buildings were completely destroyed, leaving behind nothing but smoking ruins and ruined crop rows.",al={"what happened at dead acre","why was dead acre destroyed","dead acre history"},it="history",add="e7e3cf0f"},{q="Why is the Dead Acre ruined and abandoned?",a="The farm was razed by the Defias Brotherhood during their takeover of the region. With the homestead burned to the ground and the land scorched, the original farmers were driven out or killed, leaving the smoldering fields completely abandoned.",al={"why is dead acre abandoned","dead acre burned down","why is dead acre ruined"},it="ruin",add="80cb4842"},{q="Is the Dead Acre dangerous?",a="Yes. Hostile mechanical Harvest Watchers actively patrol the scorched grounds, attacking any travelers or farmers who wander onto the smoldering plot.",al={"is dead acre dangerous","threats at dead acre","dead acre enemies"},it="danger",add="3f91a783"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Dead Acre recalls Stormwind’s neglect of Westfall, which left loyal farmers defenseless against the Defias Brotherhood’s violence."},kw={"burned farm","dead acre","defias","farm","harvest watcher","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:duskwood","quest:65"},src={"Dead Acre"}}
E["subzone:deadmines"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadmines",z="westfall",s="Beneath ruined Moonbrook, the Deadmines lie quiet, though rumors speak of danger in their forgotten shafts. Once the greatest gold producer in human lands, the mines fell silent during the First War.",h="Beneath ruined Moonbrook, the Deadmines lie quiet, though rumors speak of danger in their forgotten shafts.",sec={{t="A Vein of Gold and Blood",b="Gold once poured from the Deadmines, the richest mines in human lands. Whitestone oak supplied their timber and supports. When the orcish Horde pushed north, the miners fled in haste.\n\nDuring the First War, Sir Anduin Lothar entered the treacherous depths to recover the sacred Tome of Divinity. Subterranean ogres held him captive for twenty months before rescuers freed him. After the kingdom fell, the shafts went quiet, and people came to say they were cursed.",sp=0},{t="VanCleef's Foundry",b="After Stormwind's stonemasons rioted, the newly formed Defias Brotherhood made the Deadmines its chief refuge. Stormwind's Miners' League tried to reopen the tunnels under Foreman Thistlenettle. Defias brigands ambushed the workers and collapsed the shafts, and the slain miners now wander as restless undead.\n\nOgre enforcers and goblin tinkerers guard the deep tunnels. There, around a shipyard in Ironclad Cove, the Defias have built an industrial war camp.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="How do you get into the Deadmines?",a="The main entrance lies inside the Defias Hideout in ruined Moonbrook, in southwestern Westfall. Wind down through the basements to reach the mine shafts.",al={"where is deadmines entrance","how to enter deadmines","deadmines location"},sp=1,it="arrival",gp=true,bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Why were the mines abandoned in the first place?",a="The mines fell silent during the First War, when the Horde overran the kingdom's southern regions. War raged and ogres moved into the depths, ending the mining work. The empty tunnels soon gained a reputation for being haunted.",al={"why did deadmines close","why are deadmines abandoned"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the Defias Brotherhood building down here?",a="Edwin VanCleef and hired goblin engineers are building an enormous ironclad juggernaught in the flooded cavern of Ironclad Cove. VanCleef means to sail it up the coast and bombard and besiege Stormwind City in retribution.",al={"what is in the deadmines","vancleef plan deadmines","ironclad cove ship"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who are the undead wandering near the entrance tunnels?",a="The undead are Miners' League workers led by Foreman Thistlenettle. Defias thugs ambushed the League as it tried to survey and reclaim the mine, then collapsed the shafts. The trapped miners died and rose as restless ghouls.",al={"undead miners deadmines","foreman thistlenettle deadmines","why are there ghouls in deadmines"},it="threat"},{q="What connection does Anduin Lothar have to the Deadmines?",a="During the First War, Sir Anduin Lothar journeyed deep into the Deadmines to retrieve the sacred Tome of Divinity. Ogres in the caverns captured him and held him for nearly two years before he was rescued.",al={"lothar deadmines","anduin lothar deadmines"},it="history"},{q="What is the Deadmines?",a="The Deadmines are an expansive, winding network of tunnels dug beneath Westfall and northern Stranglethorn Vale, entered through the ghost town of Moonbrook. Before the First War, these shafts were the greatest gold production center in human lands. Abandoned amid the chaos of the orcish invasion and long shunned as haunted, the vast underground labyrinth has been secretly taken over by the Defias Brotherhood as their primary base of operations.",al={"what is deadmines","deadmines overview","deadmines lore"},it="place",add="fb059910"},{q="Who controls the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood holds total control over the labyrinth. Led by Edwin VanCleef, the disenfranchised stonemasons and brigands took the caverns by force, crushing the Miners' League workers who tried to operate here. Deep within, VanCleef directs a vast network of Defias thieves, hired goblin engineers, ogre enforcers, and allied cutthroats who labor to fulfill his vendetta against the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"who lives in deadmines","who runs deadmines","deadmines factions"},it="residents",add="00c1b6a4"},{q="Is the Deadmines dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The upper tunnels are infested with restless undead miners and cutthroat brigands, while the depths are heavily fortified by the Defias Brotherhood. Beyond armed outlaws and ruthless overseers, trespassers face goblin-engineered war machines, deadly foundries, ogre brute muscle, and defensive gunpowder charges. Venturing into the complex without skilled allies is considered a death sentence by the People's Militia.",al={"is deadmines dangerous","danger of deadmines","how dangerous are the deadmines"},it="danger",add="3042a935"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you share a holy history with the Deadmines. During the First War, Sir Anduin Lothar entered their darkest chambers to recover the sacred Tome of Divinity from savage ogres.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you walk where human mining once reached its height. Before the First War, the Deadmines led all human lands in gold production. Goblin machinery and Defias outlaws later took over."},kw={"deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","lothar","moonbrook","thistlenettle","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","subzone:ironclad-cove","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:defias-hideout","npc:wilder-thistlenettle","quest:65"},src={"Deadmines"}}
E["subzone:defias-hideout"] = {t="subzone",n="Defias Hideout",z="westfall",s="Vagrants and Defias thugs linger in the ruined house on Moonbrook’s southern edge. Its upper floor conceals a route into chambers beneath the town.",h="Vagrants and Defias thugs linger in the ruined house on Moonbrook’s southern edge.",sec={{t="A Gateway in Ruin",b="Edwin VanCleef’s southern operations lie beneath a ruined house in Moonbrook. Vagrants and Defias thugs move through its ransacked rooms, much like those in other manors and farmhouses in the settlement. On the upper floor, an opening descends into the winding passages of the Deadmines.\n\nThe Brotherhood keeps most of its strength around Moonbrook’s perimeter and at work underground, leaving few guards inside. They watch the hideout as a narrow passage into the mines, not as a stronghold of its own.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="What is inside the Defias Hideout?",a="A staircase inside the house leads to a winding tunnel and the overland entrance to the Deadmines. Vagrants wander through the mostly bare building, with a few bandits nearby.",al={"inside defias hideout","hideout entrance","what is here"},sp=1,it="place",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Why is the hideout relatively unguarded inside?",a="The Defias Brotherhood keeps its fighters in Moonbrook’s streets to intercept intruders. Its laborers and enforcers work deep in the mines.",al={"why empty","where are the defias","why so few guards"}},{q="Where in Moonbrook is this building located?",a="The hideout stands on Moonbrook’s southern edge in southwestern Westfall, near the base of the mountains. It is a large, intact, two-story building.",al={"how to find hideout","where is defias hideout","hideout location"},gp=true},{q="Who are the people lingering around the hideout?",a="Defias bandits and desperate vagrants linger in the building and around Moonbrook. Some vagrants fled poverty; others joined the Brotherhood out of necessity.",al={"who are vagrants","moonbrook vagrants","defias people"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Defias Hideout?",a="The Defias Hideout is a weathered structure in the bandit-held town of Moonbrook. On the surface it appears to be just another abandoned house claimed by vagrants, but upstairs lies the concealed entrance directly into the Deadmines, the sprawling underground stronghold of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"defias hideout","what is this building","what is defias hideout"},it="place",add="34bb7c5e"},{q="Why is it called the Defias Hideout?",a="It serves as the disguised access point for the Defias Brotherhood into their subterranean operations beneath Moonbrook. The bandits use the mundane exterior to hide the main passage leading into the Deadmines from the People's Militia and any prying Alliance authorities.",al={"why defias hideout","defias hideout name","why is it called defias hideout"},it="name",add="d0a92509"},{q="Is the Defias Hideout dangerous?",a="The structure itself is often lightly guarded because most Defias operatives are either patrolling the streets of Moonbrook or working deep underground. However, desperate vagrants linger within, and crossing through its hidden upper doorway places you directly at the threshold of the Deadmines and its armed brotherhood.",al={"is defias hideout dangerous","how dangerous is defias hideout","danger defias hideout"},it="danger",add="5348ff1f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how the Defias conceal a gateway to a vast underground fortress inside a plain ruined manor. Its scale stays hidden from casual Stormwind patrols.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can trace Edwin VanCleef’s conspiracy to this crumbling estate. It is a key staging ground in the effort to end the Defias rebellion."},kw={"deadmines","defias","defias hideout","entrance","moonbrook","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"subzone:moonbrook","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall"},src={"Defias Hideout"}}
E["subzone:demont-s-place"] = {t="subzone",n="Demont's Place",z="westfall",s="Outlaws hold Demont's Place, west of Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall. Once its fields fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. Economic collapse and the Defias Brotherhood drove the caretakers away, leaving the fields empty and the fences weathered.",h="Outlaws hold Demont's Place, west of Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall.",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Demont's Place lies within sight of Moonbrook, among the family holdings that once fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. Economic collapse and outlaw brigands stripped the farm of its livelihood and drove its caretakers away. Now outlaws use its grounds as an extension of the Defias stronghold in Moonbrook.",sp=0},{t="The Grip of the Brotherhood",b="The Defias Brotherhood holds Demont's Place on the outskirts of Moonbrook. Thugs, cutpurses, and displaced laborers linger among its fences and shattered buildings. They ambush travelers who stray from the southern roads. Until Moonbrook is reclaimed and the outlaws are broken, peaceful farming cannot return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Demont's Place located?",a="Demont's Place lies in southwestern Westfall, immediately west of the abandoned town of Moonbrook.",al={"demont's place location","where is demonts place","demonts place map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who owns Demont's Place?",a="A settler named Demont likely owned the farm before peasant unrest and economic troubles swept the countryside. Its original inhabitants have long since fled or perished, and brigands now hold the ruined acreage.",al={"who owns demonts place","who is demont","demont farm owner"},it="residents"},{q="Who currently occupies the farm?",a="Members of the Defias Brotherhood occupy the homestead. They use its ruined grounds as a staging point outside their base in Moonbrook.",al={"who is at demonts place","what enemies are at demonts place","demonts place mobs"},it="threat"},{q="Can the farm be restored to production?",a="The farm cannot be restored under current conditions. The Defias hold southern Westfall, and Stormwind cannot spare garrison troops. The homestead remains too dangerous for ordinary tillers to rebuild.",al={"can you fix demonts place","is demonts place abandoned"},gp=true},{q="What is Demont's Place?",a="Demont's Place is a dilapidated, ruined farmstead situated just west of Moonbrook in Westfall. Like other ruined farms of Westfall such as the Dead Acre, little remains of its former agrarian life.",al={"what is demonts place","demonts place westfall","demont farm"},it="place",add="74f5ac6b"},{q="What happened to Demont's Place?",a="Once a functional homestead in the breadbasket of Westfall, Demont's Place fell victim to the widespread unrest and economic ruin that swept the region. It was claimed and occupied by operatives of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"history of demonts place","what happened at demonts place","why is demonts place abandoned"},it="history",add="51911e59"},{q="Why is Demont's Place ruined?",a="The farmstead was abandoned by its original caretakers amidst Westfall's decline and seized by the Defias Brotherhood, leaving the buildings neglected and reduced to little more than battered ruins.",al={"why is demonts place destroyed","demont farm ruined","why was demonts place abandoned"},it="ruin",add="9301a59d"},{q="Is Demont's Place dangerous?",a="Yes. Situated right next to the outlaw stronghold of Moonbrook, the desolate farmstead is frequently patrolled or overrun by dangerous Defias agents and local scavengers.",al={"demonts place danger","is it safe at demonts place","demont farm threats"},it="danger",add="f73fe511"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, Demont's Place shows how far order has retreated from Westfall. Defias outlaws hold former farmland beneath the kingdom's nose.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see the lawless network the Defias Brotherhood has established across the countryside in the ruined plots around Moonbrook, including Demont's Place."},kw={"defias","defias brotherhood","demont's place","demonts place","farmstead","moonbrook","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook"},src={"Demont's Place"}}
E["subzone:dust-plains"] = {t="subzone",n="Dust Plains",z="westfall",s="Gnoll packs prowl the Dust Plains, Westfall’s dry southern frontier. The wastes stretch toward the coast and eastern hills, where Klaven’s Tower overlooks the plain.",h="Gnoll packs prowl the Dust Plains, Westfall’s dry southern frontier.",sec={{t="A Barren Frontier",b="Across southern Westfall, the Dust Plains lead from troubled farmland toward desolate wilderness. Feral gnolls have long claimed this dry ground. They ambush travelers and challenge anyone bound for the coast or nearby hills.\n\nKlaven’s Tower marks the eastern boundary. Klaven Mortwake, a Defias rogue, holds the old mage tower. Gnolls prowl the surrounding wastes, leaving travelers no shelter there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dust Plains located?",a="The Dust Plains lie in southern Westfall, south of the abandoned farmsteads. They stretch toward the cliffs and Klaven’s Tower to the east.",al={"dust plains location","where is dust plains","where dust plains"},it="place"},{q="What threats can travelers find in the Dust Plains?",a="Savage gnolls keep crude camps across the dusty plains. They attack anyone who wanders near.",al={"what lives in dust plains","dust plains enemies","mobs in dust plains"},it="threat"},{q="What is the tower on the eastern edge of the plains?",a="Klaven’s Tower is an old mage tower overlooking the eastern edge of the Dust Plains. The Defias rogue Klaven Mortwake holds it as a stronghold.",al={"dust plains tower","eastern tower westfall","what is mortwake's tower"}},{q="Does the People's Militia hold any control over the Dust Plains?",a="No. The People’s Militia is stretched thin defending Sentinel Hill and the northern farms from the Defias Brotherhood. Prowling gnolls hold the Dust Plains beyond their reach.",al={"militia dust plains","is westfall guard here"},it="in_charge"},{q="Who lives in the Dust Plains?",a="No peaceful settlers call this arid stretch home. Instead, savage gnolls inhabit rough encampments scattered throughout the plains, attacking anyone who strays south from the northern farmlands. To the east, Defias under the rogue Klaven Mortwake hold Klaven's Tower, ensuring the southern reaches of Westfall remain lawless and fraught with peril.",al={"who lives here","dust plains residents","who controls dust plains"},it="residents",add="008911b2"},{q="How dangerous are the Dust Plains?",a="They are among the most perilous regions in Westfall. Far from Sentinel Hill and the protection of the People's Militia, the plains are overrun by violent gnolls and Defias outlaws. Unprepared travelers venturing into the southern barrens easily find themselves surrounded and cut down.",al={"is dust plains dangerous","dust plains danger level","threats in dust plains"},it="danger",add="54892ac9"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Dust Plains are another lawless frontier where Stormwind’s neglect is plain. Travelers and local defenders face relentless gnoll packs without official reinforcement."},kw={"dust plains","gnolls","klaven's tower","plains","southern westfall","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:mortwake-s-tower","topic:gnoll"},src={"Dust Plains"}}
E["subzone:furlbrow-s-pumpkin-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm",z="westfall",s="Bandits and harvest golems hold Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm in northern Westfall, off the road from Elwynn Forest. Farmer Furlbrow and Verna have lost their home to the Defias Brotherhood.",h="Bandits and harvest golems hold Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm in northern Westfall, off the road from Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Harvest Lost",b="Near Westfall's northern border, Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm once fed the kingdom. The Defias Brotherhood drove Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna from their land. Now mechanical harvest golems roam the fields and attack anyone who approaches. Bandits occupy the farm buildings, while the rightful owners camp beside the road near the Jansen Stead, mourning their home and livelihood.",sp=0},{t="Defias Stronghold",b="The Defias Brotherhood has claimed homesteads like Furlbrow's while Stormwind's military garrison struggles to protect Westfall's rural farmers. Bandits camp at the farm and use it as a staging ground. Lethal harvest watchers guard the perimeter, leaving travelers on the nearby highway open to ambush.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns this pumpkin farm?",a="Farmer Furlbrow and his wife, Verna Furlbrow, own the farm. Outlaws drove them away, and the couple now shelters along the road near the Jansen Stead.",al={"who owns furlbrow farm","furlbrow owner","who lives here"},it="name"},{q="Why is the farm abandoned?",a="The Defias Brotherhood seized the farm and drove the Furlbrows away. Thugs occupy the buildings, while haywire mechanical harvest golems guard the pumpkin patch.",al={"why is it abandoned","what happened to the farm","why are bandits here"},it="ruin"},{q="Where are the Furlbrows now?",a="Farmer Furlbrow and his wife shelter beside the main road just northeast of the farm, near the Jansen Stead. Their cart and belongings are with them.",al={"where is farmer furlbrow","furlbrow location","find furlbrow"},it="residents"},{q="Why are mechanical harvest golems attacking people here?",a="The mechanical constructs are programmed to attack the people of Westfall and patrol land held by the Defias. Their exact origins remain uncertain.",al={"harvest golems","why are golems hostile","who made the golems"},it="threat"},{q="What is Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm?",a="Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm is an overrun homestead in northern Westfall, once dedicated to growing pumpkins for the kingdom of Stormwind. Today, it stands as another casualty of the realm's decline, its fertile fields left untended and taken over by outlaws.",al={"what is furlbrow pumpkin farm","furlbrows pumpkin farm lore","furlbrow farm"},it="place",add="3bec6795"},{q="What happened at Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm?",a="When the Defias Brotherhood rose across Westfall, their bandits swept through local lands and forced Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna to flee for their lives. The brotherhood seized the property, stationing thieves in the farmhouse and setting mechanical harvest golems loose to patrol the patch.",al={"furlbrow farm history","what happened to furlbrow farm","how did furlbrows fall"},it="history",add="1ceb8202"},{q="Is Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm dangerous?",a="Yes. The farm has become a Defias stronghold. Hostile bandits occupy the structures, while rogue harvest golems prowl the pumpkin patches, attacking any travelers or displaced farmers who dare draw near.",al={"is furlbrow farm dangerous","furlbrow farm danger","threats at furlbrow farm"},it="danger",add="25362e80"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the overrun farm shows Stormwind has failed to protect its heartland. Loyal farmers are left defenseless against bandits."},kw={"defias","farm","furlbrow","harvest golem","jansen","pumpkin","verna","westfall"},rel={"npc:farmer-furlbrow","subzone:jansen-stead","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm"}}
E["subzone:gold-coast-quarry"] = {t="subzone",n="Gold Coast Quarry",z="westfall",s="In southwestern Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood holds Gold Coast Quarry and draws on its remaining riches for rebellion. Once, its stone, minerals, and gold helped rebuild Stormwind.",h="In southwestern Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood holds Gold Coast Quarry and draws on its remaining riches...",sec={{t="A Plundered Resource",b="Stormwind once drew stone and gold from Gold Coast Quarry to rebuild the kingdom. After royal troops left Westfall, Defias highwaymen and renegade laborers seized the mine. Now Brotherhood patrols watch from its terraced ramps above the coast and take the minerals still left there to fund their rebellion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the quarry originally used for?",a="Stormwind opened Gold Coast Quarry for stone, minerals, and gold. Stone from quarries across Westfall helped rebuild the city after the Second War.",al={"why is there a quarry here","what did they mine here","gold coast purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls the Gold Coast Quarry right now?",a="The Defias Brotherhood controls Gold Coast Quarry. Its brigands, looters, and highwaymen patrol the terraced cliffs and mine entrances, keeping settlers away while they take resources for their own operations.",al={"who is at the quarry","who owns gold coast quarry","enemies at the quarry"},it="residents"},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind sent guards to clear the quarry?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the Stormwind House of Nobles will not fund a standing garrison in Westfall. The crown has abandoned the region, leaving the People's Militia to fight for control of places like the quarry alone.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are the guards","why is it abandoned"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the Gold Coast Quarry located?",a="Gold Coast Quarry cuts into the cliffs of southwestern Westfall, south of the Saldean and Alexston farmsteads, above the Great Sea.",al={"quarry location","how to find gold coast quarry","where is it"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Gold Coast Quarry?",a="The Gold Coast Quarry was once a valuable open-pit gold and mineral mine serving the kingdom of Stormwind. Situated near the western cliffs of Westfall, the site has slipped from the crown's grasp alongside the rest of the countryside, falling into disrepair and rebel hands.",al={"what is gold coast quarry","gold coast quarry lore","gold coast quarry westfall"},it="place",add="ddbe2f8b"},{q="What happened to the Gold Coast Quarry?",a="Once a productive extraction site feeding Stormwind's treasuries, the quarry was abandoned by the kingdom as unrest and economic collapse swept through Westfall. Stripped of imperial guards and royal funding, the lucrative works were seized by the Defias Brotherhood to fuel their ongoing rebellion.",al={"gold coast quarry history","what happened at gold coast quarry"},it="history",add="f837a40e"},{q="Why was the Gold Coast Quarry abandoned?",a="When the Stonemasons rioted and royal authority collapsed throughout Westfall, Stormwind withdrew its garrisons to protect the capital. Lacking soldiers and support to safeguard miners against bandits and highwaymen, lawful operations ground to a halt, leaving the site ripe for takeover.",al={"why is gold coast quarry abandoned","why is gold coast quarry ruined"},it="ruin",add="0f9583d4"},{q="Is the Gold Coast Quarry dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The quarry crawls with hostile Defias rogues and highwaymen who ruthlessly defend their mineral wealth and outposts from any wandering travelers or members of the People's Militia.",al={"gold coast quarry danger","is gold coast quarry safe","who attacks at gold coast quarry"},it="danger",add="29652250"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner in Westfall, you can find rich stone faces and mineral veins along the quarry cliffs. Working them means fighting through entrenched Defias patrols.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know that reclaiming sites like Gold Coast Quarry is vital to restoring order in Westfall. With no royal garrisons, local volunteers have taken up arms."},kw={"defias","defias brotherhood","gold coast quarry","mine","people's militia","quarry","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:12","quest:65"},src={"Gold Coast Quarry"}}
E["subzone:jangolode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Jangolode Mine",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood works Jangolode Mine for itself. The mine once supplied Stormwind City with ore and raw materials.",h="In Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood works Jangolode Mine for itself.",sec={{t="A Plundered Resource",b="Before Westfall declined, Jangolode Mine sent metal to Stormwind City for rebuilding and supplies. As civil order weakened, the kingdom withdrew its garrisons. The Defias Brotherhood seized the mine to support its own operations. Now the bandits work its rich veins and fiercely defend the shafts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Jangolode Mine?",a="Jangolode Mine once supplied Stormwind City with essential minerals and metal ore. When regional defenses weakened, hostile hands took it.",al={"jangolode mine info","what is jangolode","jangolode westfall"},it="place"},{q="Who controls the mine right now?",a="The Defias Brotherhood controls the underground shafts after driving out the original miners. The bandits work the mine for their own operations.",al={"who is in jangolode mine","jangolode mobs","who lives in jangolode"},it="residents"},{q="Why does Stormwind not reclaim the mine?",a="Stormwind is caught in political unrest and struggles to protect even its core borders. The kingdom lacks troops to garrison Westfall’s outlying mines, so the People’s Militia and local adventurers face the threat.",al={"why doesnt stormwind clear jangolode","stormwind garrison westfall","why abandon the mine"},it="ruin"},{q="What happened to Jangolode Mine?",a="Jangolode Mine was once a vital source of mineral wealth for the Kingdom of Stormwind, feeding stone and ore to the capital. When kingdom authority in Westfall began to crumble, the Defias Brotherhood seized the excavation works and now hold the shafts for themselves, driving off any chance of peaceful mining.",al={"jangolode mine history","what happened at jangolode mine","jangolode past"},it="history",add="18816b92"},{q="Is Jangolode Mine dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely hazardous. Defias bandits hold the shafts and fiercely defend the rich veins against any who approach, and unwary adventurers can easily find themselves cornered underground.",al={"is jangolode mine dangerous","jangolode mine danger","is jangolode safe"},it="danger",add="dff54742"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Jangolode Mine has rich deposits of basic copper and tin. Prospectors can profit from them, if they fight past the subterranean pests.",["faction:Alliance"]="Reclaiming Westfall’s resources matters to the kingdom’s stability. Driving the bandits out of Jangolode is one step toward restoring the region’s prosperity."},kw={"defias brotherhood","jangolode","jangolode mine","kobold","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:kobold","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Jangolode Mine"}}
E["subzone:jansen-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Jansen Stead",z="westfall",s="Defias bandits and mechanical Harvest Watchers roam the fields of Jansen Stead, just west of Elwynn.",h="Defias bandits and mechanical Harvest Watchers roam the fields of Jansen Stead, just west of Elwynn.",sec={{t="A Fallen Homestead",b="Jansen Stead stands beside the road from Elwynn into Westfall. Once its farm fed the kingdom, but unrest has driven the family from the land. Now mechanical Harvest Watchers patrol the fields alongside brigands. The Watchers are tied to the Defias Brotherhood. Couriers and travelers between Goldshire and Sentinel Hill pass close by.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Jansen Stead located?",a="Jansen Stead is the first farmstead on the right after you cross the river bridge from Elwynn Forest into northeastern Westfall.",al={"jansen stead location","where is jansen stead","jansen farm westfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives at Jansen Stead right now?",a="The farm's original residents have been driven away. Hostile Harvest Watchers and footpads loyal to the Defias Brotherhood occupy its overgrown fields and derelict farmhouse.",al={"who is at jansen stead","jansen stead inhabitants","mobs at jansen stead"},it="residents"},{q="Why are mechanical scarecrows attacking people here?",a="Harvest Watchers are mechanical constructs that attack people in Westfall. They patrol the farm alongside Defias agents, though their exact origins remain uncertain.",al={"why harvest watchers attack","mechanical golems westfall","defias scarecrows"},it="danger"},{q="Who is nearby asking for help?",a="Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna are camped just south of the bridge near Jansen Stead's entrance. Forced from their pumpkin patch down the road, they have set up beside their broken wagon.",al={"quests near jansen stead","furlbrows location","who gives quests near elwynn bridge"},gp=true},{q="What is Jansen Stead?",a="Jansen Stead is the northernmost farmstead in Westfall, situated just past the bridge leading out of Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful agrarian homestead feeding the kingdom of Stormwind, it now stands overgrown and deserted by its rightful owners, overrun like much of the region by the unrest sweeping through the province.",al={"what is jansen stead","jansen stead westfall","about jansen stead"},it="place",add="333dbf90"},{q="What happened to Jansen Stead?",a="When the Defias Brotherhood rose up across Westfall, the local farmers were left unprotected by the crown. The Defias drove the landowners from their fields, leaving Jansen Stead abandoned to thieves, rogue harvest golems.",al={"what happened at jansen stead","jansen stead history","how was jansen stead ruined"},it="history",add="49f2e125"},{q="Why is Jansen Stead ruined?",a="The farm was abandoned when the Defias Brotherhood took control of the countryside. Without protection from Stormwind's army, the family who tilled these fields had no choice but to flee, leaving the farmstead to decay under the control of outlaws and rogue machinery.",al={"why is jansen stead abandoned","who ruined jansen stead","why was jansen stead deserted"},it="ruin",add="2506f287"},{q="Why is it called Jansen Stead?",a="The farm is known as Jansen Stead, but the identities of its former owners and the origin of the name are not recorded.",al={"why is it called jansen stead","who is jansen","jansen stead name origin"},it="name",add="159e6b3b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human crossing from the relative peace of Northshire and Elwynn, you see the economic crisis and banditry gripping Stormwind's rural heartland at Jansen Stead.",["faction:Alliance"]="Jansen Stead's fall shows Stormwind has failed to secure its borders. Defenseless homesteaders face outlaws within sight of Elwynn Forest."},kw={"defias","farm","furlbrow","harvest watcher","jansen","stead","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","zone:elwynn","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:farmer-furlbrow","npc:verna-furlbrow","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Jansen Stead"}}
E["subzone:longshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Longshore",z="westfall",s="Murlocs command the surf at Longshore, where broken ships lie beneath the waves.",h="Murlocs command the surf at Longshore, where broken ships lie beneath the waves.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="Along Westfall’s western coast, Longshore stretches wide with unbroken sand. Travelers find little peace here. Murlocs rule the surf, and Old Murk-Eye is among their feared leaders. Sunken ships, including ruined elven destroyers, lie in the shallows.\n\nNear the south, Daphne Stilwell’s isolated farm faces Defias bandits. Across the water, you can see the Westfall Lighthouse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Longshore so dangerous?",a="Aggressive murloc tribes roam Longshore and ambush those who stray near the surf. Defias bandits also raid homesteads at the beach’s southern end.",al={"why are there so many murlocs","longshore hazards","is longshore safe"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Daphne Stilwell?",a="Daphne Stilwell lives alone on a farm in southwestern Longshore. Defias Brotherhood raids threaten her, so the Knights of the Silver Hand send paladin initiates to defend her.",al={"daphne stilwell","stilwell farm","woman on the beach"},it="people"},{q="What are the shipwrecks lying off the coast?",a="Merchant ships and elven destroyers lie among the wrecks submerged off Longshore, lost in past naval conflicts. Scavengers, murlocs, and adventurers seek relics among the underwater ruins.",al={"elven destroyers westfall","sunken ships longshore","shipwrecks"}},{q="Why do druids visit the Longshore?",a="Alliance druids undertake the Trial of the Sea Lion to master their aquatic form. They must retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance from a submerged chest near a shipwreck off northwestern Longshore.",al={"druid quest longshore","strange lockbox westfall","half pendant of aquatic endurance"}},{q="What is the Longshore?",a="The Longshore is the vast expanse of coastline forming the western and southern edge of Westfall. Stretches of sand and rocky shoals make it one of the largest continuous beaches in Azeroth. Despite its natural beauty, it remains mostly wild and perilous, bounded by the Great Sea on one side and the untamed plains of Westfall on the other.",al={"what is longshore","longshore westfall","longshore beach"},it="place",add="f7eb1386"},{q="Why is it called the Longshore?",a="It earns its name quite literally from its immense length. The beach runs unbroken along the entire western and southwestern perimeter of Westfall, creating an enormous shoreline that stands among the longest uninterrupted coastal stretches in all of Azeroth.",al={"why is it called longshore","longshore name origin","longshore meaning"},it="name",add="ae612e51"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin guided by Duthorian Rall in Stormwind, you are sent south to Daphne Stilwell’s homestead on Longshore. There, you prove your valor by protecting an innocent farmer from Defias raiders.",["class:Druid"]="As an Alliance druid, you must brave the waters off northwestern Longshore and find a lockbox near a sunken wreck. Its contents help you assemble the pendant needed for your aquatic form."},kw={"aquatic form","daphne stilwell","longshore","murloc","old murk-eye","shipwrecks","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","npc:daphne-stilwell","quest:1649","quest:31","npc:duthorian-rall","topic:murloc","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Longshore"}}
E["subzone:molsen-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Molsen Farm",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Molsen Farm lies empty, its fields gone untended. Once fertile land that fed Stormwind, it fell into ruin after the Defias Brotherhood rose and mechanical harvest golems were left prowling there.",h="In Westfall, Molsen Farm lies empty, its fields gone untended.",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Molsen Farm is one of Westfall's ruined homesteads, exposed by the kingdom's neglect and the criminal uprising. When the Defias Brotherhood took control of the countryside, farmers here were driven out or worse. They left their crops and buildings behind. Now hostile mechanical Harvest Watchers and wandering outlaws scour the fields, where laborers once gathered grain. The farm is dangerous for anyone traveling through the province.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Molsen Farm abandoned?",a="The Defias Brotherhood swept across Westfall, and Stormwind left Molsen Farm without military protection. Unable to defend their land against bandits and rogue harvest golems, the homesteaders fled their homes.",al={"why is it empty","who lived here","what happened to molsen farm"},it="ruin"},{q="Who controls the farm now?",a="Malfunctioning Harvest Watchers and outlaws aligned with the Defias Brotherhood overrun the fields. No lawful citizens live on or work the property.",al={"molsen farm enemies","who is at molsen farm"},it="residents"},{q="Who was Molsen?",a="Molsen Farm takes its name from the local family that first settled and tilled the land. Recent unrest drove Westfall's farming people into exile or poverty.",al={"who is molsen","molsen family"},it="name"},{q="What is Molsen Farm?",a="Molsen Farm is one of the many agricultural homesteads scattered across the plains of Westfall. Once a working homestead providing grain and produce for the kingdom, it fell along with the rest of the countryside when turmoil and hardship gripped the region.",al={"what is molsen farm","molsen farm westfall","about molsen farm"},it="place",add="b4e71629"},{q="What happened to Molsen Farm?",a="Like much of Westfall, Molsen Farm was driven into ruin during the unrest following the Second War. Its owners were forced off their land, and the territory was seized by the Defias Brotherhood and overrun by mechanical Harvest Watchers.",al={"what happened at molsen farm","molsen farm history","molsen farm story"},it="history",add="f96eccd7"},{q="Is Molsen Farm dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous for ordinary travelers. The fields are patrolled by rogue mechanical Harvest Watchers and roving outlaws aligned with the Defias Brotherhood who violently attack anyone trespassing on their claimed ground.",al={"is molsen farm dangerous","molsen farm threats","dangers at molsen farm"},it="danger",add="977abee8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Molsen Farm's overgrown fields recall Stormwind's failing hold on its rural lands and the pressing threat of the Defias Brotherhood."},kw={"abandoned farm","defias","harvest watcher","homestead","molsen farm","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65"},src={"Molsen Farm"}}
E["subzone:moonbrook"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonbrook",z="westfall",s="In southwestern Westfall, Moonbrook lies under Defias control, and its peaceful residents have fled. The Brotherhood guards the town above its hidden headquarters in the Deadmines.",h="In southwestern Westfall, Moonbrook lies under Defias control, and its peaceful residents have fled.",sec={{t="A Fallen Town",b="Before the First War, Moonbrook stood at the heart of Westfall’s breadbasket. Farming families and the Deadmines gold shafts depended on the town. The Old Horde razed it, but Moonbrook rose again after the Second War.\n\nPeace did not last. The House of Nobles in Stormwind neglected the settlement and stripped away its military protection. Unable to resist the red-masked bandits, the people fled their homes for Sentinel Hill and Elwynn Forest. Citizens and teachers left alike.",sp=0},{t="Defias Stronghold",b="Red-masked thugs and rogue wizards patrol Moonbrook’s streets and ransacked homes. Harvest golems roam the surrounding fields. At the town’s edge, an unassuming barn conceals an entrance beneath it. The Brotherhood guards Moonbrook above the Deadmines tunnels, where rebellion against Stormwind is being prepared.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Why is Moonbrook abandoned?",a="Moonbrook’s peaceful residents fled when the Defias Brotherhood seized control of Westfall. With no Stormwind Army garrison in the region, townsfolk were forced out and bandits took over.",al={"what happened to moonbrook","why are there bandits in moonbrook","who took over moonbrook"},it="ruin"},{q="Where does the mine inside Moonbrook lead?",a="The entrance beneath the barn at Moonbrook’s edge leads into the Deadmines. Once a vast source of gold for Stormwind, its tunnels now shelter the Defias Brotherhood and serve as their staging ground.",al={"where are deadmines","what is under moonbrook","moonbrook mine entrance"},sp=1,it="place",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Who used to live here before the bandits?",a="Miners, farmers, and tradespeople once lived in Moonbrook and supported Westfall’s agriculture. Stalvan Mistmantle briefly led the local Moonbrook Schoolhouse before bandits overran the town.",al={"moonbrook residents","who lived in moonbrook","stalvan mistmantle school"},it="people"},{q="Does Stormwind plan to reclaim the town?",a="Stormwind’s court has repeatedly refused to send royal troops to free Moonbrook and the surrounding farms. It says its resources are stretched thin, leaving the volunteer People’s Militia at Sentinel Hill to defend the area.",al={"will stormwind save moonbrook","why doesn't the army help moonbrook"},it="wants"},{q="What is Moonbrook?",a="Moonbrook is a deserted settlement in southwestern Westfall, situated just beneath the hills housing the Deadmines. Once a flourishing mining and agricultural community serving as the breadbasket of Stormwind, it has fallen into ruin and is now thoroughly occupied by the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what is this town","moonbrook info","about moonbrook"},it="place",add="2fd23d69"},{q="What happened at Moonbrook?",a="Moonbrook fell to the orcish Horde during the First War and was rebuilt after the Second War. When the disenfranchised Stonemasons formed the Defias Brotherhood and seized Westfall, they drove out the citizenry and took over Moonbrook to secure the abandoned gold mines beneath it as their headquarters.",al={"moonbrook history","history of moonbrook","what happened here"},it="history",add="ef8d3ecf"},{q="Who lives in or runs Moonbrook?",a="The Defias Brotherhood holds absolute sway over Moonbrook. Edwin VanCleef's brigands, highwaymen, and rogue cutpurses occupy the ruined houses and roam the surrounding streets, using the town to guard the secret entrance leading into their subterranean stronghold in the Deadmines.",al={"who controls moonbrook","who lives in moonbrook","moonbrook residents"},it="residents",add="4b3385a0"},{q="Is Moonbrook dangerous?",a="Yes. Moonbrook crawls with heavily armed Defias brigands and rogue harvest reapers that attack any traveler on sight. Because Stormwind has stationed no troops in the town, entering Moonbrook unprepared will quickly draw the attention of multiple coordinated thieves lying in ambush.",al={"is moonbrook safe","moonbrook danger","threats in moonbrook"},it="danger",add="00d0c34b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Moonbrook is a bitter reminder of the kingdom’s neglect. Its law-abiding subjects were left to face the Defias Brotherhood alone.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see an outlaw syndicate operating in broad daylight among Moonbrook’s alleys and ransacked homes."},kw={"deadmines","defias","moonbrook","schoolhouse","sentinel hill","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:moonbrook-schoolhouse","quest:12","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Moonbrook"}}
E["subzone:moonbrook-schoolhouse"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonbrook Schoolhouse",z="westfall",s="In Moonbrook's northwestern corner, Defias outlaws occupy the schoolhouse, with a small graveyard behind it. Stalvan Mistmantle once taught local children there.",h="In Moonbrook's northwestern corner, Defias outlaws occupy the schoolhouse, with a small graveyard behind it.",sec={{t="A Beacon Fallen into Shadow",b="The mayor commissioned Stalvan Mistmantle to run a school after he began tutoring local children. In Moonbrook's brighter days, the town prospered and students filled the hall. Now outlaws occupy the building, while weathered headstones in the rear cemetery look out over Westfall's decline.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Floorboards",b="An old footlocker on the schoolhouse's main floor holds an unsent letter about Stalvan Mistmantle's arrival in Moonbrook. It tells how he tutored local children, then received the mayor's commission to build a new schoolhouse. A separate letter found later in Goldshire says regional troubles forced him to leave his post and seek work as a private tutor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was this building originally used for?",a="Moonbrook's schoolhouse gave local children a formal education. Its broad hall resembles a town hall, reflecting the township's ambition and pride before its fall.",al={"why was it built","moonbrook school purpose","what is this place"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was Stalvan Mistmantle?",a="Stalvan Mistmantle was a learned scholar who became the schoolhouse's headmaster. Letters he left behind tell more of his career.",al={"who is stalvan","stalvan mistmantle lore","school headmaster"},it="people"},{q="Why is the schoolhouse abandoned now?",a="Economic strife brought Moonbrook down, and the Defias Brotherhood took over southern Westfall. The town's civic institutions fell, and bandits now overrun the abandoned schoolhouse.",al={"why abandoned","what happened to moonbrook school","who lives here now"},it="ruin"},{q="What can be found inside the schoolhouse today?",a="An old, dusty footlocker on the ground floor holds an unsent letter. Alliance investigators tracking Stalvan Mistmantle can find it inside.",al={"footlocker location","loot in schoolhouse","quest item inside"},it="today"},{q="What is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse?",a="The Moonbrook Schoolhouse is a prominent building resembling a town hall located in northwestern Moonbrook in southern Westfall. Built specifically for the scholar Stalvan Mistmantle, it once served as an academy for local children before Moonbrook fell into ruin. A small graveyard sits quietly behind the structure.",al={"what is moonbrook schoolhouse","moonbrook school","schoolhouse westfall"},it="place",add="8f4dfb64"},{q="What happened at the Moonbrook Schoolhouse?",a="The schoolhouse was constructed to provide education for the community, with Stalvan Mistmantle appointed as its headmaster. During his tenure, Stalvan taught local pupils and corresponded with friends and officials. When Westfall collapsed into turmoil and Moonbrook was overrun by the Defias Brotherhood, the school was abandoned, leaving behind old belongings and forgotten correspondence in dusty footlockers.",al={"schoolhouse history","what happened at moonbrook schoolhouse","stalvan schoolhouse past"},it="history",add="5cab6b72"},{q="Is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse dangerous?",a="Yes. While the schoolhouse itself is a dilapidated hall, it sits directly inside Moonbrook, which is heavily occupied by the Defias Brotherhood. Rogue bandits, brigands, and outlaws patrol the surrounding streets and frequently loiter near the building's entrance, making any visit a hazardous venture for unprotected travelers.",al={"is moonbrook schoolhouse dangerous","schoolhouse threats","danger in moonbrook schoolhouse"},it="danger",add="eb59fad3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, the abandoned schoolhouse shows how far Westfall has fallen from the Crown's protection. A center of learning now shelters outlaws."},kw={"defias","footlocker","headmaster","mistmantle","moonbrook","schoolhouse","stalvan","westfall"},rel={"subzone:moonbrook","quest:66","zone:westfall","topic:alliance"},src={"Moonbrook Schoolhouse"}}
E["subzone:mortwake-s-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Klaven's Tower",z="westfall",s="In southeastern Westfall, Klaven's Tower guards a river crossing near the kingdom's borders. Klaven Mortwake commands the tower, where stolen goods pass along Defias routes.",h="In southeastern Westfall, Klaven's Tower guards a river crossing near the kingdom's borders.",sec={{t="A Smuggler's Stronghold",b="North of the Dagger Hills, Klaven's Tower anchors the Defias Brotherhood's work in southern Westfall. Across the river in Elwynn Forest, Jerod's Landing receives and stages goods plundered from the Redridge Mountains. Together, the two sites move contraband toward Westfall.\n\nFrom the tower, the Brotherhood watches the waterways and slips supplies past Kingdom patrols. This helps shield its supply routes from the crown's eyes.",sp=0},{t="Fumes and Shadows",b="Klaven Mortwake controls the tower. An alchemist and rogue, he spends his hours brewing exotic troll poisons within its walls. Thick, noxious fumes fill the upper chambers.\n\nThe vapors are deadly to intruders, but they also dull the senses of Mortwake's own guards. That weakness gives Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7, a blind spot to exploit as its agents monitor the tower from nearby hills.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls this tower?",a="Klaven Mortwake, a Defias rogue, controls the tower. He oversees smuggling and experiments with volatile poisons. Defias sentries and patrollers guard the grounds under his command.",al={"who is mortwake","who is klaven","who lives in the tower"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the tower important to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The tower relays stolen goods moving into Westfall. Cargo from the Redridge Mountains crosses Elwynn Forest, passes Jerod's Landing, then reaches the tower to supply the Brotherhood's wider rebellion.",al={"defias tower purpose","what is this tower used for","why is the tower here"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is SI:7 watching this place?",a="Stormwind intelligence watches the tower because of Mortwake's poison-making and its central place in Defias supply routes. Master Mathias Shaw leads the service, and operatives like Amber Kearnen scout the perimeter to assess Brotherhood movements and seize valuable intelligence.",al={"si7 mortwake tower","amber kearnen tower","why is stormwind watching"},it="threat"},{q="What are the fumes lingering inside the tower?",a="The haze comes from Klaven Mortwake's experiments with troll poisons. The protected section describes their effects on the tower's guards.",al={"poison tower westfall","tower fumes","klaven poison"}},{q="What is Klaven's Tower?",a="This stone watchtower sits at the southeastern edge of Westfall, tucked near the river just north of the Dagger Hills. Long seized by the Defias Brotherhood, it serves as an entrenched redoubt and smuggling hub connecting their operations between Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and the Redridge Mountains.",al={"what is klavens tower","mortwake tower westfall","defias tower westfall"},it="place",add="2b1660bb"},{q="What happened at Klaven's Tower?",a="The tower is held by rogue Defias operative Klaven Mortwake and his followers. The brotherhood turned it into a fortified smuggling depot for contraband routed through Jerod's Landing, drawing the sharp attention of SI:7, who sent spies like Amber Kearnen to surveil its courtyard and counter Klaven's deadly concoctions.",al={"mortwakes tower history","history of klavens tower","what went down at the tower"},it="history",add="d8588bd0"},{q="Is Klaven's Tower dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous. Armed Defias sentries and patrollers guard every entrance, while altered drones lurk within. More insidious than the blade-wielding bandits are the noxious fumes lingering from Klaven Mortwake's alchemical brews, which poison the air and threaten unwary intruders.",al={"is klavens tower safe","mortwakes tower threats","how dangerous is mortwakes tower"},it="danger",add="6fe20dc9"},{q="Why is it called Klaven's Tower?",a="The stronghold takes its title directly from Klaven Mortwake, the Defias rogue commander and poisoner who established control over the structure and transformed it into a focal point of brotherhood activity.",al={"why is it mortwakes tower","who is mortwake","why klavens tower"},it="name",add="61b98615"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue trained in Stormwind, you come to Klaven's Tower at SI:7's direction. You infiltrate Mortwake's stronghold, test your lockpicking and stealth, and learn the dangerous craft of virulent poisons.",["faction:Alliance"]="Near the borders of Elwynn, Westfall, and Redridge, this Defias stronghold shows how deeply the Brotherhood has compromised the kingdom's interior riverways and trade routes."},kw={"amber kearnen","dagger hills","defias tower","klaven mortwake","klaven's tower","si:7","troll poison","westfall"},rel={"quest:2359","npc:amber-kearnen","quest:2300","subzone:jerod-s-landing","zone:westfall","zone:redridge","subzone:dagger-hills","topic:troll"},src={"Mortwake's Tower"}}
E["subzone:saldean-s-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Saldean's Farm",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, Saldean's Farm remains the one homestead not wholly overrun and abandoned to the Defias Brotherhood. Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma keep the farmhouse as a rare safe haven amid the region's troubles.",h="In Westfall, Saldean's Farm remains the one homestead not wholly overrun and abandoned to the Defias...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Dust",b="The Saldean family held to their land as neighboring farms fell to banditry and mechanical sabotage. Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma still offer travelers hot food and a kind word. Harvest golems deployed across the plains now plague their fields, so the family stays close to the farmhouse walls.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Stormwind's crown has largely neglected Westfall, and few guards are left to keep order. A handful of Sentinel Hill and Stormwind guards patrol the edges, but the Saldeans rely chiefly on their own grit and help from passing travelers. Salma's famous Westfall stew and goretusk liver pie bring small comforts, as does the farmhouse shelter, against the Defias threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this farm still standing when the others fell?",a="Farmer Saldean and his wife refused to flee when the Defias Brotherhood swept through Westfall. Hostile harvest golems prowl their crops, but the family defends the ground around the farmhouse with help from passing militia and adventurers.",al={"why not overrun","saldean farm survival","how is the farm alive"},it="history"},{q="Who are all the people gathered around the house?",a="Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma live at the farm. Anyone else there is likely a passing traveler; the couple welcome visitors and adventurers willing to help with the dangers in their fields.",al={"refugees at saldean","homeless westfall","orphans at farm"},it="residents"},{q="Why are mechanical golems attacking the fields?",a="The Defias Brotherhood turned the region's mechanical harvest reapers and golems into deadly sentries. They roam the fields and attack anyone trying to cultivate or clear the land.",al={"harvest golems","why are robots in crops","mechanical scarecrows"},it="danger"},{q="Is the Stormwind Army protecting the farm?",a="Stormwind's military presence is nearly gone. A few scattered guards from Sentinel Hill and Stormwind keep watch, but the crown has largely left Westfall's defense to local initiative.",al={"stormwind military presence","sentinel hill guards here","guard support"}},{q="What is Saldean's Farm?",a="Saldean's Farm is one of the last surviving homesteads in Westfall not fully claimed by the Defias Brotherhood. While neighboring lands lie broken or abandoned, this stubborn farmstead still stands in the northern plains, serving as an enduring refuge amid the region's collapse.",al={"what is saldeans farm","saldean farm overview","saldeans farm lore"},it="place",add="a60e97c5"},{q="Why is it called Saldean's Farm?",a="The farm takes its name from Farmer Saldean and his wife, Salma Saldean. Unlike most landowners across Westfall who fled when the Defias Brotherhood took hold, the Saldean family stubbornly stood their ground, refusing to abandon their homestead and offering food and a kind word to passing travelers.",al={"who named saldeans farm","saldeans farm name meaning","why saldean farm"},it="name",add="a483aabd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Saldean's Farm shows the failing edge of the kingdom's frontier and the hardship ordinary citizens face while Stormwind's leaders are distracted.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may know Salma Saldean's name among travelers. She makes hearty, lifesaving dishes such as Goretusk Liver Pie from ingredients scavenged in Westfall."},kw={"farmer saldean","halfway house","harvest golem","refugees","saldean","salma saldean","westfall"},rel={"npc:farmer-saldean","npc:salma-saldean","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:stormwind-guard","quest:65"},src={"Saldean's Farm"}}
E["subzone:sentinel-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Sentinel Hill",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Hill, the Alliance holds its main stronghold in Westfall, and the People's Militia keeps its command post there. Overgrown fields, scavenging gnolls, and hostile outlaws surround the rise, leaving it as the lawful citizens' only secure foothold in the region.",h="At Sentinel Hill, the Alliance holds its main stronghold in Westfall, and the People's Militia keeps its...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Dust",b="Sentinel Hill rises above central Westfall. Around Sentinel Tower stand a barracks-style inn, a gryphon roost with flights to Stormwind and beyond, a forge, and a lumber mill. Overgrown fields, scavenging gnolls, and outlaws crowd the surrounding land. Within the fragile perimeter, travelers, beleaguered farmers, and recruits can regroup under the eyes of veteran defenders.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Militia",b="The royal army is detained in Stormwind and cannot spare soldiers for the outlying territories. So Gryan Stoutmantle established the People's Militia on Sentinel Hill. Volunteer fighters organize scouts, strike at the Riverpaw gnolls, and investigate the organized banditry tearing through Westfall's abandoned farmsteads. This is no opulent fort or comfortable refuge. It is a working frontline camp, determined to reclaim the kingdom's former breadbasket.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why hasn't Stormwind sent soldiers to defend Sentinel Hill?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources spread thin across the realm, Stormwind's regency has largely left the western provinces to their own devices. Local citizens and veterans formed the People's Militia themselves to hold Sentinel Hill and protect what remains of Westfall.",al={"why no stormwind guards","where is stormwind army","why militia here"},it="motive"},{q="Who is in charge of Sentinel Hill?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle commands the People's Militia from the base of Sentinel Tower. He coordinates local defense, gathers intelligence on nearby threats, and directs visiting adventurers against the gnolls and highwaymen pressing in on the settlement.",al={"who leads sentinel hill","sentinel hill commander","gryan stoutmantle"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats actively endanger the hill?",a="Aggressive Riverpaw gnolls roam the western plains. The Defias Brotherhood carries out coordinated sabotage and lurks throughout the abandoned farms.",al={"what attacks sentinel hill","sentinel hill enemies","who is attacking"},it="threat"},{q="What services are available here for travelers?",a="Travelers can find a gryphon master with flights to Stormwind City and other Alliance outposts, an innkeeper, a mailbox, trade supply vendors, and repair facilities around the local forge.",al={"sentinel hill amenities","sentinel hill flight path","is there an inn here"},gp=true},{q="What is Sentinel Hill?",a="Sentinel Hill is the central Alliance outpost in Westfall. Built around a prominent watchtower overlooking the plains, it serves as the operational headquarters for the People's Militia. Surrounded by encroaching outlaws and gnolls, the hill offers weary travelers a rare bastion of safety with a flight roost, an inn, a forge, and essential supplies.",al={"what is sentinel hill","about sentinel hill","sentinel hill westfall"},it="place",add="3c1a5a7a"},{q="Is Sentinel Hill dangerous?",a="Within the immediate perimeter around the tower and inn, the guards keep you safe from harm. However, the surrounding slopes and plains are exceptionally perilous. Riverpaw gnolls prowl close to the roads, rogue harvest watchers wander nearby fields, and Defias brigands actively patrol the territory just outside the outpost's boundaries.",al={"is sentinel hill safe","danger sentinel hill","sentinel hill safety"},it="danger",add="fc9f9bfd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Sentinel Hill is your only fortified outpost and supply hub in Westfall. It anchors the Alliance's presence against outlaws and raiders.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Westfall's farmers forced to raise their own militia here. Their struggle shows the kingdom's deepening crisis while the throne remains vacant."},kw={"gryan stoutmantle","gryphon roost","peoples militia","riverpaw gnolls","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-tower","zone:westfall","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:gryphon-roost","zone:stormwind","topic:gnoll","quest:65"},src={"Sentinel Hill"}}
E["subzone:sentinel-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Sentinel Tower",z="westfall",s="At Sentinel Tower, defenders watch Westfall and organize resistance against bandits, gnolls, and the Defias Brotherhood. Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia hold the line.",h="At Sentinel Tower, defenders watch Westfall and organize resistance against bandits, gnolls, and the Defias...",sec={{t="Watch over the Wild West",b="Sentinel Tower watches over Westfall's unsettled plains. With Stormwind's army largely absent and aid withheld, local volunteers and veterans have gathered around this stronghold. From its stone heights, lookouts see across dusty plains, past abandoned pumpkin patches to the misty shores. They watch for highwaymen and gnoll raiding parties moving through the region.",sp=0},{t="Headquarters of the Militia",b="Gryan Stoutmantle and local leaders direct the militia from Sentinel Tower. Makeshift defenses ring the stronghold, where wounded refugees and weary soldiers gather. Homesteaders driven from their lands find emergency shelter there. Militia members piece together reports about the Defias Brotherhood and organize volunteers for strikes against the syndicate that has brought Westfall to ruin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is in charge at Sentinel Tower?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle directs operations from Sentinel Tower. As head of the People's Militia, he coordinates Westfall's displaced farmers in their defense and recruits willing adventurers.",al={"sentinel tower leader","who leads sentinel tower","who runs the tower"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the tower so important to Westfall?",a="Sentinel Tower is the only fortified garrison and lookout post left in the central plains. Stormwind has left Westfall largely undefended, making the tower the region's last organized bastion of order and safety for refugees.",al={"why sentinel tower matters","purpose of sentinel tower"},it="purpose"},{q="Who stays in and around the tower?",a="Militia officers, sentinels on watch, quartermasters, and farmsteader families stay in and around Sentinel Tower. The families left their ruined lands to seek shelter near its stone walls.",al={"who is at sentinel tower","sentinel tower occupants"},it="residents"},{q="What threats are watched from the tower?",a="Sentinels watch for Riverpaw gnolls, murlocs moving inland from the coast, and roaming highwaymen and brigands of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"sentinel tower enemies","what does the tower guard against"},it="threat"},{q="What is Sentinel Tower?",a="Sentinel Tower is a prominent scout tower perched atop Sentinel Hill in central Westfall. Established as the fortified stronghold and command center for the People's Militia, it allows Gryan Stoutmantle and his scouts to survey the rolling plains and monitor hostile movements across the entire region.",al={"what is sentinel tower","sentinel tower westfall","about sentinel tower"},it="place",add="226a51b2"},{q="What happened at Sentinel Tower?",a="Constructed as a watchtower to safeguard Westfall's homesteaders, Sentinel Tower became the primary bastion of defense once Stormwind withdrew its garrisons. Displaced farmers and refugees have repeatedly sought shelter within its shadow under the militia's protection.",al={"sentinel tower history","what happened sentinel tower","history of sentinel tower"},it="history",add="7792f636"},{q="Is Sentinel Tower dangerous?",a="The tower itself is safe for Alliance travelers, serving as the heavily guarded nerve center of the People's Militia. However, the surrounding hills are fraught with peril, constantly harassed by Defias bandits, hostile Riverpaw gnolls, and prowling mechanical harvest watchers.",al={"is sentinel tower safe","is sentinel tower dangerous","sentinel tower danger"},it="danger",add="3b2e4075"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sentinel Tower shows the grit of ordinary Alliance subjects fighting for their homeland while Stormwind's high lords turn a blind eye.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you see Stormwind's agrarian breadbasket barely holding together against rebellion from within."},kw={"defias","gryan stoutmantle","peoples militia","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","watchtower","westfall"},rel={"subzone:sentinel-hill","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","topic:alliance"},src={"Sentinel Tower"}}
E["subzone:stendel-s-pond"] = {t="subzone",n="Stendel's Pond",z="westfall",s="At Stendel's Pond, anglers still come for fresh fish despite the gnolls along its banks.",h="At Stendel's Pond, anglers still come for fresh fish despite the gnolls along its banks.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Watering Hole",b="Southwest of Sentinel Hill, Stendel's Pond still draws anglers. Gnolls roam the muddy banks, where scattered skeletons and two lone graves mark a perilous shore. No one knows whether foul water or the beasts caused the deaths. Yet schools of sagefish still bring anglers to the pond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Stendel's Pond located?",a="Stendel's Pond lies southwest of Sentinel Hill in central Westfall, just off the dusty paths toward the southern reaches.",al={"stendel pond location","where is stendel's pond","find stendel pond"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures lurk around the pond?",a="Riverpaw gnolls prowl the pond's muddy shore and attack wanderers who approach the water.",al={"who lives here","monsters at stendel's pond","stendel pond gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there skeletons and graves by the shore?",a="Scattered skeletons and two unnamed graves mark the shore's dangers. The dead may have fallen to gnolls or been poisoned by the pond water, but no one knows for certain.",al={"whose graves are these","why skeletons","grave at pond"},it="history"},{q="What is Stendel's Pond?",a="Stendel's Pond is a small, quiet body of water nestled southwest of Sentinel Hill in the central plains of Westfall. While peaceful from a distance, the pond's shores tell a grim story of hardship in the dust-choked region.",al={"what is stendels pond","stendel pond overview","about stendels pond"},it="place",add="a33fcb3a"},{q="Is Stendel's Pond dangerous?",a="Yes, it is far from safe for lone travelers. Aggressive gnolls prowl around the water's edge, making any approach hazardous. Furthermore, the skeletal remains and lonely graves lining the bank suggest that either the local wildlife is lethal or the stagnant water itself may be foul and undrinkable.",al={"is stendels pond safe","dangers at stendels pond","how dangerous is stendels pond"},it="danger",add="9e1e18fd"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooks value sagefish from these murky waters for their fish dishes.",["faction:Alliance"]="Near Sentinel Hill, gnoll encampments make the pond an uncontrolled threat on the People's Militia's southern perimeter."},kw={"gnolls","graves","pond","sagefish","sentinel hill","stendel","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:gnoll"},src={"Stendel's Pond"}}
E["subzone:westfall-lighthouse"] = {t="subzone",n="Westfall Lighthouse",z="westfall",s="Westfall Lighthouse stands dark on the rocky isle off Westfall's southwestern shore, and its keepers are gone. Old Murk-Eye led the attack that killed them. Captain Grayson's spirit remains by the tower.",h="Westfall Lighthouse stands dark on the rocky isle off Westfall's southwestern shore, and its keepers are gone.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Mist",b="Westfall Lighthouse once guided ships past Westfall's dangerous southwestern bluffs and along the coast near Stormwind. As law and order failed across the region, royal patrols dwindled and coastal dangers grew unchecked. Murloc tribes drove the keepers inland. The family returned to relight the beacon, but Old Murk-Eye rallied his kin to attack again. The murlocs killed the keepers and put out the light.",sp=0},{t="The Ghostly Watch",b="Captain Grayson haunts the rocky outcrop beside Westfall Lighthouse. Bound to the place where he watched the keepers die, the ghost cannot rest while the beacon is dark and monsters crawl along the shore. Grayson asks passing adventurers to gather oil from the harvest golems to keep the flame burning. He also asks them to hunt Old Murk-Eye in revenge for the fallen keepers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Westfall Lighthouse abandoned?",a="Local murlocs drove the human family who tended Westfall Lighthouse inland. When they returned to relight the beacon, Old Murk-Eye led another attack and killed them before Captain Grayson.",al={"what happened to the keepers","who lived at the lighthouse","why is it ruined"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Captain Grayson?",a="Captain Grayson is a ghost who haunts the island outside Westfall Lighthouse. After witnessing the keepers' deaths, he asks travelers to gather oil to keep the beacon lit and hunt the coastal murlocs responsible.",al={"ghost at lighthouse","who is the ghost","captain grayson lore"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Old Murk-Eye?",a="Old Murk-Eye is a cunning, vicious murloc chieftain who stalks the Westfall shoreline. He rallied the coastal tribes to attack Westfall Lighthouse and kill its keepers.",al={"murk eye","murloc boss","who killed the keepers"},it="threat"},{q="Does the lighthouse still function?",a="The mechanical lantern still works and casts a beam across the ocean at night. Captain Grayson asks travelers for the oil needed to keep its flame burning.",al={"does the light turn on","beacon working"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Westfall Lighthouse?",a="The Westfall Lighthouse is a lonely coastal beacon standing on a rocky island off the southwestern shore of Westfall. Built to guide mariners safely along the treacherous shoals of the Great Sea, it now stands largely desolate, watching over a shoreline overrun with ferocious coastal murlocs.",al={"what is westfall lighthouse","westfall lighthouse","about westfall lighthouse"},it="place",add="fe113f6d"},{q="What happened at Westfall Lighthouse?",a="The lighthouse was originally tended by a human keeper and his family. The infamous murloc Old Murk-Eye drove them off, but when they bravely returned to rekindle the beacon, Murk-Eye led a brutal second assault. The family was slaughtered helplessly under the gaze of Captain Grayson's ghost, leaving the tower unattended.",al={"westfall lighthouse history","what happened here","lighthouse tragedy"},it="history",add="db6e5f33"},{q="Is Westfall Lighthouse dangerous?",a="While the lighthouse island itself is relatively calm under Captain Grayson's spectral watch, the surrounding waters and beaches crawl with vicious murlocs, including the notorious Old Murk-Eye. Unwary travelers can easily find themselves swarmed if they wade across without caution.",al={"is westfall lighthouse safe","westfall lighthouse danger","are there enemies at westfall lighthouse"},it="danger",add="c45dc608"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see how far Stormwind's reach has failed at Westfall Lighthouse. The kingdom's isolated servants were left without military support against the coastal beasts."},kw={"beacon","captain grayson","coast","flame","lighthouse","murloc","old murk-eye","westfall"},rel={"npc:captain-grayson","quest:103","quest:104","topic:murloc","zone:westfall","topic:alliance","topic:pirate"},src={"Westfall Lighthouse"}}
E["topic:westfall-brigade"] = {t="topic",n="People's Militia",z="westfall",s="In Westfall, the People's Militia holds its ground against the Defias Brotherhood. Gryan Stoutmantle raised the volunteers at Sentinel Hill after Stormwind withdrew its troops. With local farmers and visiting adventurers, they defend the region from banditry.",h="In Westfall, the People's Militia holds its ground against the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="A Region Abandoned",b="Westfall once fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. Then the kingdom withdrew its troops, leaving the people defenseless. The Defias Brotherhood spread across the plains, seizing family homesteads, taking over iron mines, and extorting local farmers. With no royal reinforcements in sight, veteran warrior Gryan Stoutmantle rallied citizens and retired soldiers to form the People's Militia.",sp=0},{t="Holding Sentinel Hill",b="Sentinel Tower, atop Sentinel Hill, is the Militia's base. From there, volunteers patrol the region's main roads with little military gear or steady supplies. Gryan Stoutmantle directs them against the growing ranks of Defias highwaymen, thieves, and pillagers. When Redridge asks for mutual aid, the Militia must refuse. Sending even a handful of men could leave Westfall lost.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Conspiracy",b="Scouting and outside help reveal the scale of the Defias threat to the People's Militia. The Brotherhood is more than a band of country thieves. It operates under Edwin VanCleef, the former Guildmaster of the Stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind. From the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, the Defias plan to overthrow the kingdom. The embattled Militia is the only barrier between the capital and open insurrection.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Why is the People's Militia fighting alone without Stormwind's army?",a="Stormwind withdrew its troops from Westfall, leaving its people defenseless, and no one in the countryside has been told why. Gryan Stoutmantle rallied the People's Militia to defend what remained of the land.",al={"why no stormwind guard","where is stormwind army","why westfall abandoned"},it="motive"},{q="Who leads the People's Militia?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle, a seasoned human veteran, founded and leads the People's Militia.",al={"who leads westfall brigade","militia leader","gryan stoutmantle role"},it="leader"},{q="Where is their headquarters located?",a="The People's Militia is based at Sentinel Hill, around the tall stone watchtower in the heart of Westfall.",al={"militia base","where is sentinel hill","westfall militia base"},it="place"},{q="Can the Militia help other troubled regions like Redridge?",a="No. When Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire asked for military reserves, Gryan Stoutmantle had to refuse because the Militia was barely holding on against the Defias.",al={"why wont they help lakeshire","solomon request stoutmantle"},it="allies"},{q="Who is the main enemy the Militia fights?",a="The People's Militia fights the Defias Brotherhood, a criminal syndicate of former masons, rogues, and highwaymen led by Edwin VanCleef.",al={"who are they fighting","militia enemy","defias enemy"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Where did the Westfall Brigade come from?",a="There is no Westfall Brigade in Westfall; the defenders of Sentinel Hill are the People's Militia. Gryan Stoutmantle gathered local farmers, veterans, and common citizens there after the Defias Brotherhood seized Westfall and Stormwind failed to intervene, so they could take up arms in defense of their own homes and farmland.",al={"westfall brigade history","westfall brigade origin","peoples militia origin"},it="history",add="e3ac0fe0"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how Stormwind's rural folk defend their homes when the royal court turns a blind eye.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see Gryan Stoutmantle and his protectors lead from the front. They make do with worn blades and makeshift armor against overwhelming odds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you see Westfall's crisis expose dangerous cracks in the kingdom and show how fragile peace is in its heartlands."},kw={"defias brotherhood","edwin vancleef","gryan stoutmantle","moonbrook","people's militia","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","westfall brigade"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:12","npc:edwin-vancleef","subzone:deadmines","quest:143"},src={"Westfall Brigade"}}
E["zone:westfall"] = {t="zone",n="Westfall",z="westfall",s="Westfall's farms lie exposed, and the Defias Brotherhood holds much of the countryside. Once Stormwind's breadbasket, the territory now struggles without crown support or military garrisons.",h="Westfall's farms lie exposed, and the Defias Brotherhood holds much of the countryside.",sec={{t="A Land Left Behind",b="Westfall's pastures and wheat fields once fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. After the Second War, the kingdom's finances ran thin, and its leaders neglected the territory. Stormwind sent resources elsewhere and let its garrisons go. The land fell fallow.\n\nNow barren pastures, harsh coastal winds, rogue harvest golems, and Riverpaw gnolls make survival hard for the few homesteaders who remain.",sp=0},{t="The Rise of the Brotherhood",b="The Defias Brotherhood's arrival hastened Westfall's collapse. The bandits wear red masks and follow a leader whose name no one in the countryside knows. They made Westfall their stronghold, burning farmers' fields, salting the soil, and taking abandoned mines.\n\nFrom Moonbrook, a ghost town, the Brotherhood rules most of the countryside in all but name.",sp=0},{t="The People's Militia",b="The House of Nobles has ignored Westfall's plight, so local people have taken up their own defense. At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle formed the People's Militia, a volunteer force holding the line against gnolls and bandits. Stormwind sends no formal soldiers or supplies.\n\nThe Militia depends on wandering adventurers to push back the Defias and protect the farms that remain.",sp=0},{t="Masons in Red Masks",b="Edwin VanCleef leads the Brotherhood. He was the guildmaster who rebuilt Stormwind City, but the House of Nobles denied his stonemasons their pay, and riots drove them out. They took up the red mask in Westfall. The bandits burning its fields are the same hands that raised the capital's walls.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="The Deadmines Conspiracy",b="Beneath Moonbrook, Edwin VanCleef has gathered cutthroats, goblins, and renegades in the abandoned gold shafts of the Deadmines. The Brotherhood is building a massive ironclad juggernaut there. It is meant to sail up the coast and bombard Stormwind City.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout","defias.juggernaut"}}},faq={{q="Why are so many farms abandoned in Westfall?",a="Stormwind withdrew its garrisons when upkeep grew too expensive, leaving Westfall unprotected. The Defias Brotherhood then seized much of the countryside, driving off homesteaders, burning cropland, and reprogramming mechanical harvest watchers as lethal sentries.",al={"abandoned farms","why is westfall dead","why fallow"},it="ruin"},{q="Why does Stormwind not send troops to help Westfall?",a="The kingdom's treasury is strained, and the House of Nobles gives greater priority to threats in other lands. Court manipulation has also quietly deprived Westfall of attention and supplies, leaving residents to defend themselves.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are the guards","stormwind aid"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle organized the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill to defend Westfall. With no soldiers from the crown, farmers and settlers joined to fight the Defias Brotherhood and Riverpaw gnolls.",al={"peoples militia","sentinel hill militia","gryan stoutmantle army"},it="in_charge"},{q="Who leads the Defias Brotherhood in Westfall?",a="Edwin VanCleef, former guildmaster of the Stonemasons Guild, leads the Defias Brotherhood. He oversaw Stormwind City's rebuilding, then led his workers into Westfall and armed them after a bitter payment dispute ended in riots.",al={"defias leader","who leads defias","vancleef"},sp=1,it="leader",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What is hidden inside Moonbrook?",a="Beneath an unassuming barn in Moonbrook lies the entrance to the Deadmines. The Defias Brotherhood turned the abandoned gold mine into an underground fortress and shipwright for its war against Stormwind.",al={"moonbrook secret","what is in deadmines","moonbrook mine"},sp=1,it="place",bt={"defias.hideout","defias.juggernaut"}},{q="Why are the mechanical scarecrows attacking people?",a="Defias-aligned goblin tinkerers captured the mechanical harvest watchers, originally built to tend crops and scare away pests. They retrofitted them to patrol fields and kill trespassers.",al={"harvest golems attacking","harvest watchers","evil scarecrows"},it="threat"},{q="What is Westfall?",a="Westfall is the windswept western territory of the Kingdom of Stormwind, lying west of Elwynn Forest and south to the sea. Once the fertile breadbasket of the kingdom, its rolling hills and wide pastures fed Stormwind for generations. Today, neglected by the crown and ravaged by conflict, it has deteriorated into fallow dust plains, ruined homesteads, and outlaw territory.",al={"what is this zone","tell me about westfall","westfall lore"},it="place",add="cd1e134e",nx={8,9}},{q="Why is it so empty out here?",a="A compounding mix of drought, neglect, and banditry emptied the countryside. After the Second War, Stormwind focused its soldiers elsewhere, leaving local homesteads defenseless. When the Defias Brotherhood rose up, they drove out farmers, burned croplands, and salted fields. With no royal garrisons to protect them, most inhabitants either fled or starved.",al={"why is westfall barren","why so empty","why are there no people here"},it="ruin",add="44cadea7"},{q="Was Westfall always this poor?",a="Not at all. For generations, Westfall was Stormwind's proud agricultural heartland, celebrated for golden wheat fields, rich soil, and bountiful gold mines like Jangolode and the Deadmines. Its food fed the capital, and its mines filled royal treasuries before wars and domestic unrest left it barren.",al={"was westfall always poor","was westfall wealthy before","westfall past"},it="history",add="1a97e791"},{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is a massive criminal organization composed of rogue stonemasons, thieves, brigands, and outcasts. Led by Edwin VanCleef, they took over Westfall's abandoned farmlands and mines to wage a bitter shadow war against the Kingdom of Stormwind, intent on exacting retribution for unpaid debts and perceived betrayals.",al={"who are the defias","what is the defias brotherhood","who are these bandits"},it="threat",add="1d4a9481",nx={11,12}},{q="Why do the Defias wear red bandanas?",a="Red bandanas are the Defias Brotherhood's trademark, and the material indicates a member's rank. Red silk bandanas identify higher-ranking members; Scout Riell asks adventurers to collect them as proof of their deaths.",al={"why red bandanas","defias red masks","red masks meaning"},it="threat",add="b6953315"},{q="What do the Defias want in Westfall?",a="They treat Westfall as their sovereign stronghold and staging ground. By controlling its gold mines, seizing food supplies, and driving out loyalist farmers, they can secretly build their forces and machinery away from Stormwind's direct sight while plotting the kingdom's downfall.",al={"what do defias want","defias goals westfall","why are defias in westfall"},it="threat",add="908b4fe1"},{q="Why was I sent to Westfall?",a="You were directed here because Stormwind's regular military refuses or fails to deploy troops to Westfall, leaving the territory on the verge of falling entirely to banditry. Authorities in Elwynn redirect capable adventurers westward to bolster the struggling locals who are desperate for aid.",al={"why am i in westfall","who sent me to westfall","why send me here"},it="arrival",add="d384bc2d"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a paladin of the Silver Hand and a Westfall native. Returning home after fighting in Lordaeron during the Third War, he found his homeland overrun by bandits and deserted by Stormwind's military. In response, he gathered local defenders to establish the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",al={"who is stoutmantle","gryan stoutmantle","who leads sentinel hill"},it="in_charge",add="d59f010f",nx={15}},{q="Is Gryan Stoutmantle actually in charge of Westfall?",a="Practically speaking, yes. While the boy-king in Stormwind holds legal claim to Westfall, the crown exerts almost no real authority here. Stoutmantle and his volunteer militia at Sentinel Hill represent the only functioning defense and law enforcement remaining in the realm.",al={"who rules westfall","is stoutmantle the leader","who is in charge"},it="in_charge",add="af1c3ddb"},{q="What happened to the Stonemasons Guild?",a="Under Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef, the Stonemasons Guild spent years rebuilding Stormwind City after the First War. When the job was done, the House of Nobles refused to pay the agreed sum. After peaceful pleas failed, the guild was forcibly disbanded, sparking furious riots that drove the masons into exile.",al={"what happened to the stonemasons","stonemasons guild story","who were the stonemasons"},sp=1,it="history",add="c01912f7",nx={17}},{q="Did Stormwind really refuse to pay the Stonemasons?",a="Yes. The House of Nobles had amassed staggering debts expanding military expeditions elsewhere, leaving the kingdom nearly bankrupt. Influenced by court intrigue and aristocratic arrogance, the nobles offered mere pocket change for colossal labor, outright refusing to honor the full contracts.",al={"did stormwind cheat the stonemasons","why did nobles not pay","stonemasons pay dispute"},sp=1,it="history",add="ec2fd06e"},{q="Why are there so many gnolls in Westfall?",a="The Riverpaw pack gnolls have migrated across the border to exploit the absence of Stormwind soldiers. Worse, the Defias Brotherhood actively hired them as mercenary muscle, stationing them across the hills and plains to ambush travelers and harass any surviving homesteads.",al={"why are gnolls here","riverpaw gnolls westfall","danuvin gnolls"},it="threat",add="cf60f690"},{q="What is Moonbrook?",a="Moonbrook was once the primary market and mining town of southern Westfall. Sitting above the ancient entrance to the Deadmines, it was completely seized and cleared out by the Defias Brotherhood, who now use its empty buildings as a perimeter guard for their underground stronghold.",al={"what is moonbrook","moonbrook lore","tell me about moonbrook"},it="place",add="e40fa3bd"},{q="Where does the Defias investigation lead?",a="Your investigation uncovers the Brotherhood's secret heart beneath Moonbrook in the Deadmines. There, deep within the subterranean caverns, Edwin VanCleef oversees the construction of a massive ironclad juggernaut meant to bombard Stormwind from the sea, leading to a direct assault on the guildmaster himself.",al={"where does defias questline go","how does defias story end","deadmines conclusion"},sp=1,it="next_step",add="46f1c864",bt={"defias.hideout","defias.juggernaut","defias.masons"}},{q="How did I end up in Westfall?",a="You likely crossed the river bridge from Elwynn Forest following the road west, sent by authorities or friends of Sentinel Hill. With Stormwind stretched thin and unable to spare royal troops, word has spread across the neighboring lands that Gryan Stoutmantle and the local farmers desperately need capable hands. Whether you walked in answering a call for aid or simply followed the king's highway looking for work, you crossed into a realm that the kingdom's soldiers have all but abandoned.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to westfall","how did i end up here"},it="arrival",add="27471424"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Westfall?",a="Your primary mission is to assist the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in pushing back the myriad threats choking the province. Gryan Stoutmantle needs volunteers to cull the aggressive wildlife, silence the rogue harvest watchers prowling fallow fields, and push back Riverpaw gnolls. Above all, you are tasked with hunting down the elusive Defias Brotherhood, uncovering where they are hiding, and breaking their stranglehold on what remains of Westfall's struggling farmsteads.",al={"what should i do here","what am i doing in westfall","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="6324593c"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Westfall shows Stormwind's political decay. The farmers starving in the dirt were abandoned by the nobility they toiled to feed.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how the People's Militia holds Sentinel Hill. Without it, the Defias Brotherhood would control the southern approaches to Elwynn Forest.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find a shadow war across Westfall, where SI:7 spies face the Defias Brotherhood's street-smart scouts, thieves, and assassins.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn how the beleaguered homesteaders at Saldean's Farm make do with tough local beasts and teach travelers to prepare Westfall Stew."},kw={"deadmines","defias","harvest golem","militia","moonbrook","saldean","sentinel hill","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:gryan-stoutmantle","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:moonbrook","zone:deadmines","quest:12","quest:36"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Westfall (Classic)","Westfall"}}
